109
00:10:40,238 --> 00:10:46,468
因为随着生成式人工智能技术的演进，必须解决几个伦理方面的考量。
Because as generative AI technology evolves, several ethical considerations must be addressed.

110
00:10:47,502 --> 00:10:57,316
一个主要的担忧是 AI 可能创建出真实但具有误导性的内容，比如深度伪造，这可能导致虚假信息的传播。
One major concern is the potential for AI to create realistic but misleading content, such as deepfakes, which can contribute to misinformation.

111
00:10:58,158 --> 00:11:05,252
还有一种风险是延续训练数据中存在的偏见，这可能会影响公平性和准确性。
There is also the risk of perpetuating biases present in the training data, which can impact fairness and accuracy.

112
00:11:05,614 --> 00:11:14,372
AI 生成内容的归属权是另一个挑战，建立清晰的知识产权准则非常重要。
Ownership of AI-generated content poses another challenge, as it is important to establish clear guidelines for intellectual property rights.

113
00:11:15,086 --> 00:11:23,812
此外，AI 系统可能会无意中泄露训练数据中的敏感信息，因此需要强大的隐私保护措施。
Additionally, AI systems might inadvertently reveal sensitive information from their training data, necessitating strong privacy measures.

114
00:11:24,654 --> 00:11:34,884
最后，建立标准以确保生成式人工智能被道德且负责任地使用，避免误用和有害应用至关重要。
Finally, it is crucial to establish standards to ensure that generative AI is used ethically and responsibly, avoiding misuse and harmful applications.

115
00:11:35,534 --> 00:11:37,476
究竟什么是 LLM？
What exactly is an LLM?

116
00:11:38,062 --> 00:11:44,676
想象一下你有一个超级聪明的朋友，他读过世界上所有的书、文章和博客帖子。
Imagine you have a super smart friend who has read every book, article, and blog post in the world.

117
00:11:45,358 --> 00:11:52,900
这个朋友可以和你聊几乎任何话题，帮你做作业，写故事，甚至还能给你讲笑话。
This friend can chat with you about almost anything, help you with your homework, write stories, and even tell you jokes.

118
00:11:53,614 --> 00:11:55,780
这基本上就是 LLM 所做的事情。
That's pretty much what an LLM does.

119
00:11:56,270 --> 00:12:03,492
从技术术语来说，LLM 是一种在海量数据上进行训练的人工智能。
In technical terms, an LLM is a type of artificial intelligence that has been trained on vast amounts of data.

120
00:12:04,142 --> 00:12:10,468
它能基于从所有这些阅读中学习到的模式，来理解并生成类人文本。
It can understand and generate human-like text based on the patterns it has learned from all that reading.

121
00:12:11,374 --> 00:12:18,724
这是属于一个更广泛的领域，叫做生成式人工智能，它专注于创作与人类产出相似的内容。
This is part of a broader field called generative AI, which focuses on creating content that resembles human output.

122
00:12:19,022 --> 00:12:20,772
现在让我们来拆解一下基础知识。
Let's now break down the basics.

123
00:12:21,166 --> 00:12:22,400
大语言模型。
Large language model.

124
00:12:23,054 --> 00:12:27,620
“大”只是意味着该模型是用海量的数据进行训练的。
Large just means that the model has been trained with a massive amount of data.

125
00:12:28,238 --> 00:12:33,840
我们所说的是来自书籍、网站、文章等各种渠道的数十亿个词汇。
We are talking about billions of words from books, websites, articles, and more.

126
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:40,964
“模型”指的是一组指令或算法，帮助人工智能理解并生成语言。
Model refers to a set of instructions or algorithms that help the AI understand and generate language.

127
00:12:41,646 --> 00:12:44,516
你可以把它想象成一个指导如何制作蛋糕的食谱。
Think of it like a recipe that guides how to make a cake.

128
00:12:44,910 --> 00:12:49,092
在这种情况下，它是在指导 AI 如何创作有意义的文本。
In this case, it is guiding the AI on how to create meaningful text.

129
00:12:49,678 --> 00:12:50,980
我们来聊聊语言。
Let's talk about language.

130
00:12:51,406 --> 00:12:55,140
这关乎词汇、句子以及我们沟通的方式。
This is all about words, sentences, and how we communicate.

131
00:12:55,662 --> 00:13:01,188
当你给朋友发短信、写邮件或在社交媒体上发布内容时，你就在使用语言。
When you text your friends, write an email, or post on social media, you are using language.

132
00:13:01,806 --> 00:13:08,560
既然你现在了解了 LLM 中每个词的含义，让我们快速看看它的技术定义。
So now that you understand what each word in LLM stands for, let's quickly see what is the technical definition.

133
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:18,788
LLM 是由拥有数十亿参数的神经网络组成的语言模型，它们通过自监督学习在海量的无标注文本上进行训练。
LLMs are language models made up of neural networks with billions of parameters that are trained by self supervised learning on vast amounts of unlabeled text.

134
00:13:19,726 --> 00:13:22,372
现在让我们深入探讨 LLM 是如何运作的。
Now let's dive into how LLMs work.

135
00:13:23,054 --> 00:13:24,996
我们用一个例子来简化这个过程。
Let's simplify this with an example.

136
00:13:25,614 --> 00:13:29,380
假设你输入“天空是——”。
Imagine you type the sky is dash dash dash.

137
00:13:30,094 --> 00:13:36,868
LLM 可能会预测下一个词是“蓝色”，因为它在训练过程中见过很多次这个短语。
The LLM might predict the next word to be blue because it has seen that phrase so many times during its training.

138
00:13:37,486 --> 00:13:45,124
像 GPT-4 这样的大语言模型是基于在海量文本数据上训练的复杂神经网络来运行的。
Large language models like GPT-4 operate based on complex neural networks trained on vast amounts of text data.

139
00:13:45,742 --> 00:13:49,284
这里有一个关于它们如何在两个阶段中运作的简化解释。
Here is a simplified explanation of how they work in two phases.

140
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:53,764
第一个阶段是训练阶段，随后是推理阶段。
The first phase is the training phase, followed by the inference phase.

141
00:13:54,382 --> 00:13:56,196
训练阶段包含四个步骤。
The training phase has four steps.

142
00:13:56,974 --> 00:14:02,756
第一步，数据收集，即从各种来源收集多样化的文本数据。
Step one, data collection, that is, gathering diverse text data from various sources.

143
00:14:03,374 --> 00:14:10,244
第二步，预处理，这意味着对文本数据进行清洗并分词成数值表示。
Step two, pre-processing, which means cleaning and tokenizing text data into numerical representations.

144
00:14:10,958 --> 00:14:18,020
第三步，模型架构，这本质上就是设计神经网络结构，通常是 Transformer。
Step three, model architecture, which is nothing but designing the neural network structure, typically a transformer.

145
00:14:18,542 --> 00:14:24,132
第四步，训练，即通过预测句子中的下一个词来调整模型参数。
Step four, training is adjusting model parameters by predicting the next word in sentences.

146
00:14:24,718 --> 00:14:30,788
到这个训练阶段结束时，LLM 已经通过海量数据训练完成，可以进行进一步的预测。
By this training phase, the LLMs are being trained on vast amounts of data to do further predictions.

147
00:14:31,374 --> 00:14:35,908
现在进入下一个阶段，即推理阶段，它同样包含四个步骤。
Now coming to the next phase, which is inference phase, it also has four steps.

148
00:14:36,590 --> 00:14:42,980
第一步，输入处理，这意味着对输入文本进行分词并转换为嵌入。
Step one, input processing, that means tokenizing and converting the input text into embeddings.

149
00:14:43,534 --> 00:14:49,316
第二步，生成输出，现在利用模型来预测并生成后续的词语。
Step two, generating output, now using the model to predict and generate the next words.

150
00:14:49,934 --> 00:14:55,716
第三步，采样，即从预测的概率分布中选择词汇。
Step three, sampling, which is selecting words from a predicted probability distribution.

151
00:14:56,270 --> 00:15:03,716
第四步，也是最后但同样重要的一步，就是后处理，也就是把生成的标记转换回可读的文本。
Step four, last but not the least, post-processing, which means converting generated tokens back to readable text.

152
00:15:04,366 --> 00:15:12,260
在训练阶段之后，进入推理阶段时，LLM 会识别模式、采样内容并给出预测。
After the training phase, in the inference phase, the LLMs will recognize patterns, sample content, and give predictions.

153
00:15:12,846 --> 00:15:18,468
除了这些步骤，还有三个关键概念，我们需要了解它们来揭开 LLM 的神秘面纱。
Apart from these steps, there are three key concepts which we should know to demystify LLMs.

154
00:15:18,958 --> 00:15:21,124
首先是注意力机制。
First, attention mechanism.

155
00:15:21,518 --> 00:15:28,356
这让模型能够关注输入文本的相关部分，从而更好地理解上下文和含义。
This allows the model to focus on relevant parts of the input text, improving its understanding of context and meaning.

156
00:15:28,846 --> 00:15:36,356
第二是嵌入，即对单词或标记的数值表示，用以捕捉它们的含义和关系。
Second, embeddings, which are numerical representations of words or tokens that capture their meaning and relationship.

157
00:15:36,974 --> 00:15:38,724
第三是 Transformer。
Third, transformers.

158
00:15:39,278 --> 00:15:47,364
Transformer 是采用自注意力机制并行处理输入数据的架构，使其更高效且更强大。
Transformers are the architecture that uses self-attention to process input data in parallel, making it efficient and more powerful.

159
00:15:47,758 --> 00:15:50,788
让我们来看看一些 LLM 的实际应用案例。
Let's see some examples of LLMs in action.

160
00:15:51,118 --> 00:15:53,028
例子一，聊天。
Example one, chatting.

161
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:56,484
你的提示词可以是：日本的首都是哪里？
Your prompt can be, what is the capital of Japan?

162
00:15:56,942 --> 00:16:00,868
LLM 回答：日本的首都是东京。
LLM replies, the capital of Japan is Tokyo.

163
00:16:01,358 --> 00:16:06,084
LLM 知道这个，是因为它读过大量关于国家和首都的信息。
LLM knows this because it has read a lot of information about countries and capitals.

164
00:16:06,670 --> 00:16:08,516
让我们看第二个例子，关于写作。
Let's see example two about writing.

165
00:16:08,878 --> 00:16:11,812
你的提示词可以是：你能帮我写个故事吗？
Your prompt can be, can you help me write a story?

166
00:16:12,238 --> 00:16:24,036
LLM 回答：当然，在遥远的一片土地上，有一位勇敢的骑士…… LLM 可以根据它从阅读故事中学习到的内容来生成富有创意的文本。
LLM says, sure, once upon a time in a land far away, there was a brave knight who the LLM can generate creative text based on what it has learned from reading stories.

167
00:16:24,558 --> 00:16:25,552
例子三。
Example three.

168
00:16:25,902 --> 00:16:27,428
让我们看看回答问题。
Let's see answering questions.

169
00:16:27,822 --> 00:16:31,748
你的提示词可以是：用简单的术语解释一下光合作用。
Your prompt can be explain photosynthesis in simple terms.

170
00:16:32,686 --> 00:16:33,860
LLM 回答：
LLM replies.

171
00:16:34,382 --> 00:16:40,804
光合作用是植物利用阳光将二氧化碳和水转化为食物的过程。
Photosynthesis is a process by which plants use sunlight to make food from carbon dioxide and water.

172
00:16:41,454 --> 00:16:47,236
它通过利用从教育内容中学习到的模式，来简化复杂的课题。
It simplifies complex topics by using the patterns it has learned from educational content.

173
00:16:48,142 --> 00:16:53,508
有不同类型的 LLM，每种都为特定的任务和应用而设计。
There are different types of LLMs, each designed for specific tasks and applications.

174
00:16:54,318 --> 00:16:56,132
现在让我们来探索这些类型。
Now let's explore these types.

175
00:16:56,654 --> 00:16:58,244
首先是基础模型。
First are base models.

176
00:16:58,766 --> 00:17:04,992
它们在广泛的数据上进行训练，可以执行通用的语言理解和生成任务。
They are trained on a wide range of data and can perform general language understanding and generation tasks.

177
00:17:05,550 --> 00:17:10,212
它们不针对任何特定类型的指令进行专门优化，但非常全能。
They aren't specialized for any particular type of instructions but are versatile.

178
00:17:10,766 --> 00:17:19,236
例如 GPT-3.5 Turbo，它以其多功能性以及生成连贯且符合上下文相关的文本能力而闻名。
For example, GPT-3, which is known for its versatility and ability to generate coherent and contextually relevant text.

179
00:17:19,568 --> 00:17:22,050
另一种类型是指令微调模型。
Another type is instruction-based models.

180
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:26,819
它们经过微调，比基础模型更能更好地遵循特定的指令。
They are fine-tuned to follow specific instructions better than base models.

181
00:17:27,438 --> 00:17:32,324
它们能够理解并执行用户提供的详细提示词中的任务。
They can understand and execute tasks based on detailed prompts given by the user.

182
00:17:32,814 --> 00:17:41,408
例如 T5，也就是 Text-to-Text Transfer Transformer，它将所有的 NLP 问题都转化为文本到文本的
For example, T5, that is Text-to-Text Transfer Transformer, it converts all NLP problems into a text-to-text

183
00:17:41,648 --> 00:17:48,420
格式，使其在翻译、摘要和问答等任务中具有极高的通用性。
format, making it highly versatile for tasks like translation, summarization, and question answering.

184
00:17:48,750 --> 00:17:58,468
另一个例子是 Instruct GPT，它经过专门优化，能更好地遵循特定的用户指令，并提供更有用且更安全的回答。
Another example is Instruct GPT, which is tailored to follow specific user instructions better and provide more useful and safe responses.

185
00:17:58,926 --> 00:18:00,772
以上就是这些 LLM 的类型。
So these were the types of LLMs.

186
00:18:01,102 --> 00:18:05,604
不过，市场上还有付费的和开源的 LLM。
However, there are paid and open source LLMs as well in the market.

187
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:08,996
你可以根据自己的使用需求和预算来选择。
Based on your usage and budget, you can explore them.

188
00:18:09,614 --> 00:18:17,648
一些付费的 LLM 包括 GPT-4、4.0、Microsoft Azure OpenAI Services 等。
Some paid LLMs are GPT-4, 4.0, Microsoft Azure OpenAI Services, etc.

189
00:18:18,190 --> 00:18:22,768
而开源的包括 GPT Neo、BERT 等。
And open source are GPT Neo, BERT, etc.

190
00:18:23,008 --> 00:18:26,852
让我们来看看这些 LLM 是如何变革 AI 世界的。
Let's see how our LLMs revolutionizing the world of AI.

191
00:18:27,598 --> 00:18:33,924
在教育领域，它们可以帮助解释复杂的概念、回答问题，甚至担任学生的导师。
In education, they can help explain difficult concepts, answer questions, and even tutor students.

192
00:18:34,766 --> 00:18:42,852
在内容创作方面，它们通过生成创意、起草内容和润色，为作家、营销人员和创作者提供支持。
In content creation, they assist writers, marketers, creators by generating ideas, drafting content, and editing.

193
00:18:43,534 --> 00:18:48,324
在编程领域，它们能帮助专业人士针对特定问题生成代码。
In coding, they assist professionals with generating code to their specific problems.

194
00:18:49,198 --> 00:18:58,148
在客户支持方面，许多公司利用 LLM 来驱动聊天机器人，为客户的咨询提供快速且准确的回复。
In customer support, many companies use LLMs to power their chatbots, providing quick and accurate responses to their customer inquiries.

195
00:18:59,086 --> 00:19:04,164
除了这些领域，LLM 正被应用于每一个领域和领域中。
Apart from all these fields, LLMs are being utilized in every field and domain.

196
00:19:04,590 --> 00:19:06,340
但并非一帆风顺。
But it's not all smooth sailing.

197
00:19:06,574 --> 00:19:07,968
也存在一些挑战。
There are challenges too.

198
00:19:08,366 --> 00:19:10,756
让我们来看看其中一个挑战，那就是偏见。
Let's see one such challenge, which is bias.

199
00:19:11,534 --> 00:19:18,052
由于 LLM 从人类编写的文本中学习，它们可能会吸收并复制数据中存在的偏见。
Since LLMs learn from human written text, they can pick up and reproduce biases present in the data.

200
00:19:18,606 --> 00:19:20,676
另一个问题是错误信息。
Another one is misinformation.

201
00:19:21,166 --> 00:19:28,164
它们有时会提供错误或误导性的信息，尤其是当它们训练的数据有缺陷时。
They can sometimes provide incorrect or misleading information, especially if the data they were trained on was flawed.

202
00:19:28,622 --> 00:19:33,316
不过，抛开这些挑战不谈，LLM 的前景非常令人兴奋。
However, keeping challenges aside, the future of LLMs is exciting.

203
00:19:33,710 --> 00:19:40,388
随着它们的不断改进，我们可以预见它们会变得更加准确、可靠且多功能。
As they continue to improve, we can expect them to become even more accurate, reliable, and versatile.

204
00:19:40,878 --> 00:19:48,196
它们将更好地理解上下文，处理复杂任务，甚至能从较少的数据中学习。
They will be better at understanding context, handling complex tasks, and even learning from smaller amounts of data.

205
00:19:48,718 --> 00:19:49,648
这就是全部内容。
So there you have it.

206
00:19:49,902 --> 00:19:57,444
大语言模型，也就是 LLM，就像是由海量数据和先进算法驱动的超级聪明的伙伴。
Large language models, LLMs, are like super smart friends powered by tons of data and advanced algorithms.

207
00:19:57,870 --> 00:20:01,380
它们可以聊天、写作，并以无数种方式帮助我们。
They can chat, write, and help us in countless ways.

208
00:20:01,966 --> 00:20:07,012
随着它们的不断进化，它们将变得更加深入到我们的日常生活中。
As they continue to evolve, they are set to become even more integral in our daily lives.

209
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:17,060
欢迎来到 Langchain 和生成式人工智能入门课程。
Welcome to the session on Introduction to Langchain and Generative AI.

210
00:20:17,742 --> 00:20:28,228
在本模块中，我们将探讨什么是 Langchain，为什么它对构建生成式人工智能应用至关重要，以及它是如何融入更广泛的 AI 生态系统的。
In this module, we'll explore what Langchain is, why it's become essential for building Gen AI applications, and how it fits into the broader AI ecosystem.

211
00:20:28,718 --> 00:20:33,124
首先，让我们来了解一下什么是 Langchain 以及它存在的意义。
Let's start by understanding what Langchain actually is and why it exists.

212
00:20:34,030 --> 00:20:42,980
Langchain 是一个用于构建基于大语言模型应用的框架和生态系统，它提供了结构化的构建块和集成功能。
Langchain is a framework and ecosystem for building applications with large language models, providing structured building blocks and integrations.

213
00:20:43,726 --> 00:20:49,636
它不是一个完整的生产系统，但为基于 LLM 的应用提供了可重用的组件。
It's not a full production system, but offers reusable components for LLM based apps.

214
00:20:50,382 --> 00:20:53,380
仅将 LLM 用作聊天机器人是受限的。
Using an LLM as a chatbot is limiting.

215
00:20:53,902 --> 00:20:58,352
真正的应用需要数据、工具、上下文和控制权。
Real applications need data, tools, context, and control.

216
00:20:59,150 --> 00:21:08,036
Langchain 将 LLM 集成到更广泛的工作流中，解决了数据库、API 和外部工具等方面的挑战，
Langchain integrates LLM into broader workflows, addressing challenges like databases, APIs, and external tools,

217
00:21:08,430 --> 00:21:12,672
同时将凭证、权限和错误处理交给开发者去处理。
while leaving credentials, permissions, and failure handling to the developer.

218
00:21:12,942 --> 00:21:20,900
Langchain 将语言模型转化为系统组件，为超越文本生成的应用提供架构支持。
Langchain transforms language models into system components, offering scaffolding for applications beyond text generation.

219
00:21:21,774 --> 00:21:32,592
它在集成方面表现出色，能将模型连接到数据库、API、文档和工具中，将 AI 与您现有的基础设施无缝融合。
It excels in integration, connecting models to databases, APIs, documents, and tools, seamlessly integrating AI with your existing infrastructure.

220
00:21:32,942 --> 00:21:44,292
