01:06:25,166 --> 01:06:28,068
NumPy 用于处理数组运算。
NumPy is used for handling array operations.

676
01:06:28,400 --> 01:06:31,920
接着是 sentence Transformer，用于创建句子嵌入。
Then sentence transformers for creating sentence embeddings.

677
01:06:32,160 --> 01:06:38,596
来自 Transformers 的 Pipeline 是为了使用预训练模型来进行摘要和问答。
Pipeline from Transformers is for performing summarization and question answering using pre trained models.

678
01:06:39,758 --> 01:06:45,636
有了这些库之后，我们将进入加载并提取 PDF 文件内容的步骤。
With these libraries in place, we will move to load and extract the content from our PDF file.

679
01:06:46,446 --> 01:06:53,316
接下来，我们将加载包含可持续发展内容的 PDF 文件并提取其中的文本。
Next, we will load the PDF file containing our content on sustainable development and extract its text.

680
01:06:54,222 --> 01:06:57,380
这里我们首先设置 PDF 文档的路径。
Here we first set the path to the PDF document.

681
01:06:58,126 --> 01:07:05,348
接下来是 LoadPDF 函数，它会打开 PDF 文件并读取每一页的文本内容。
Next is LoadPDF function, opens the PDF file and reads the text content of each page.

682
01:07:05,966 --> 01:07:09,796
它使用 with open(pdf_path) 来加载 PDF。
It uses FITS OpenPDF path to load the PDF.

683
01:07:10,542 --> 01:07:16,036
然后，对于每一页，都会使用 get_text 函数来提取文本。
Then, for each page, page get text function is used to extract the text.

684
01:07:16,878 --> 01:07:21,572
该函数将所有页面的提取文本作为单个字符串返回。
The function returns the extracted text from all pages as a single string.

685
01:07:22,222 --> 01:07:26,692
为了演示，我使用了一个内容较少的短 PDF。
For this demonstration, I have used a small PDF with limited text.

686
01:07:27,502 --> 01:07:33,284
使用这个小 PDF 的目的是展示提取和清洗过程是如何运作的。
The goal of using this small PDF is to demonstrate how the extraction and cleaning process works.

687
01:07:34,094 --> 01:07:42,336
当你处理自己的项目时，使用包含更多内容的较大 PDF 很重要，比如报告、手册
When you are working on your own project, it's important for you to use larger PDFs with more content, such as reports, manuals,

688
01:07:42,576 --> 01:07:43,748
或者学术论文。
or academic papers.

689
01:07:44,622 --> 01:07:54,916
较大的 PDF 提供更丰富的内容，从而能提高模型的准确性，并在摘要和问答过程中提供更有见地的回答。
Larger PDFs provide richer content, which in turn leads to better model accuracy and more insightful responses during summarization and question answering.

690
01:07:55,758 --> 01:07:59,876
现在我们已经提取了文本，是时候对其进行清洗和规范化了。
Now that we have extracted the text, it's time to clean and normalize it.

691
01:08:00,526 --> 01:08:06,724
接下来，我们通过删除不必要的空格和格式问题来清理提取出的文本。
Next, we have cleaned the extracted text by removing unnecessary white spaces and formatting issues.

692
01:08:07,406 --> 01:08:12,964
所以，这里的 cleanText 函数会去除多余空格并规范化文本格式。
So, here, cleanText function removes extra spaces and formats the text.

693
01:08:13,678 --> 01:08:18,084
这里，这个 resub 函数用于替换字符串中的部分内容。
Here, this resub function is used to substitute parts of a string.

694
01:08:18,702 --> 01:08:23,108
我们使用的是匹配一个或多个空格字符的模式。
We are using this pattern which matches one or more white space characters.

695
01:08:23,310 --> 01:08:27,939
这些匹配到的空格随后会被替换为文本字符串中的单个空格。
These matched white spaces are then replaced with a single space in the text string.

696
01:08:28,910 --> 01:08:38,819
然后，strip 方法会移除文本开头和结尾的任何空格，确保字符串的首尾没有多余空格。
Then the strip method removes any leading and trailing spaces from the text, ensuring there are no necessary spaces at the beginning or end of the string.

697
01:08:39,950 --> 01:08:46,500
我们打印出清洗后文本的前 300 个字符，来验证清理过程以及它的总长度。
We print the first 300 characters of the clean text to verify the cleaning process and its total length.

698
01:08:47,438 --> 01:08:56,644
在应用了 resub 和 strip 方法后，我们对原始文本进行了清洗，去除了多余空格并确保文本格式正确。
After applying the resub and strip methods, we clean the raw text, removing extra spaces and ensuring the text is properly formatted.

699
01:08:57,486 --> 01:09:04,131
我们打印出清洗后文本的前 300 个字符，以确认清理过程是否运行正常。
We print the first 300 characters of the clean text to verify that the cleaning process has worked correctly.

700
01:09:04,974 --> 01:09:10,724
我们还打印了清洗后文本的总长度，以确认它已按预期处理。
We also print the total length of the clean text to confirm that it has been processed as expected.

701
01:09:11,502 --> 01:09:17,572
所以在输出中，你可以看到我们打印了清洗后文本的预览以及它的总长度。
So, in the output, you can see that we print a preview of the clean text along with its total length.

702
01:09:18,094 --> 01:09:20,932
现在，文本已经准备好进行语义表示了。
The text is now ready for semantic representation.

703
01:09:21,326 --> 01:09:29,348
接下来，在生成嵌入之前，我们检查了文本中是否存在诸如“可持续发展”之类的特定关键词。
Next, before proceeding with the generating embeddings, we checked if a specific keyword like sustainable development exists in the text.

704
01:09:30,029 --> 01:09:37,124
这里，Search in Text 函数会以不区分大小写的方式搜索关键词，并打印出它是否存在。
Here, Search in Text function searches for the keyword in a case insensitive manner and prints whether it's present.

705
01:09:37,870 --> 01:09:45,283
在这里，我们得到的输出是 keyword present 等于 true，这意味着该词存在于文档中。
Here, we got the output as keyword present equal to true, which means that the word is present in the document.

706
01:09:45,805 --> 01:09:49,091
在下一步中，我们为文档创建了嵌入。
In the next step, we have created the embeddings for the document.

707
01:09:49,710 --> 01:09:53,508
在这一步，我们将为清洗后的文档文本生成嵌入。
In this step, we will generate embeddings for the clean document text.

708
01:09:54,286 --> 01:10:00,336
嵌入是文本的数值表示，这对于搜索和摘要非常有用。
Embeddings are numerical representations of the text, which will be useful for search and summarization.

709
01:10:00,558 --> 01:10:04,964
我们使用 Sentence Transformer 将清洗后的文本编码为嵌入。
We use Sentence Transformer to encode the clean text into embeddings.

710
01:10:05,742 --> 01:10:10,436
打印出生成的嵌入的形状，以确认其维度。
The shape of the generated embeddings is printed to confirm its dimensionality.

711
01:10:11,278 --> 01:10:17,188
接下来，我们创建了 faiss index，以便对文档嵌入进行相似性搜索。
Next, we have created face index to perform similarity search over the document embeddings.

712
01:10:18,158 --> 01:10:26,148
这里我们建立了一个 faiss index，它能让我们高效地对文档嵌入进行相似性搜索。
Here we have set up a face index, which will allow us to efficiently perform similarity searches on the document embeddings.

713
01:10:26,990 --> 01:10:31,716
Faiss 基本上代表 Facebook AI Similarity Search。
Face basically stands for Facebook AI Similarity Search.

714
01:10:32,142 --> 01:10:35,652
它用于在嵌入中进行快速的相似性搜索。
It is used for fast similarity searches over the embeddings.

715
01:10:36,270 --> 01:10:42,308
在这里，我们创建了一个维度与生成的嵌入一致的 FAISS 索引。
Here we have created a FAISS index with the dimension of the generated embeddings.

716
01:10:42,862 --> 01:10:47,140
这里是 FAISS.indexFlatIP。
Here, FAISS.indexFlatIP.

717
01:10:47,502 --> 01:10:55,904
这会创建一个使用内积相似度方法的索引，并且 faiss_index.add 函数会将文档嵌入添加到 faiss
This creates an index using the inner product similarity method, and faceindex.add function adds the document embeddings to the face

718
01:10:56,144 --> 01:10:56,580
索引中。
index.

719
01:10:57,358 --> 01:11:01,732
现在 faiss index 准备就绪了，我们将进入文档摘要环节。
Now that face index is ready, we'll move on to summarizing the document.

720
01:11:02,254 --> 01:11:08,516
所以对于文档摘要，我们使用了一个预训练模型来生成文档的摘要。
So for document summarization, we have used a pre-trained model to generate a summary of the document.

721
01:11:09,070 --> 01:11:14,436
我们使用 Hugging Face 流水线加载了一个预训练摘要模型，也就是 BART。
We loaded a pre-trained summarization model, that is BART, using Hugging Face pipeline.

722
01:11:14,990 --> 01:11:20,644
在这里，摘要文档函数利用 BART 模型来生成清洗后文本的摘要。
Here, the summarize document function uses the BART model to generate a summary of the clean text.

723
01:11:21,390 --> 01:11:26,052
然后，最大长度和最小长度定义了摘要的长度限制。
Then, max length and min length define the length constraints for the summary.

724
01:11:26,542 --> 01:11:29,028
文档的摘要将打印在下方。
The summary of the document is printed below.

725
01:11:29,486 --> 01:11:34,372
有了摘要后的文档，我们现在可以开始实现问答功能了。
So having the summarized document, we are now ready to implement the question answering.

726
01:11:34,862 --> 01:11:38,084
这里我们使用了一个预训练模型来进行问答。
Here we have used a pre-trained model for question answering.

727
01:11:38,542 --> 01:11:41,904
该模型将根据文档内容来回答问题。
The model will answer questions based on the content of the document.

728
01:11:42,144 --> 01:11:46,468
我们通过 Hugging Face 流水线加载一个预训练的问答模型。
We load a pre-trained question answering model using Hugging Face pipeline.

729
01:11:47,214 --> 01:11:54,980
在这里，回答问题函数接收问题和文档文本的上下文，并利用模型来寻找答案。
Here, the answer question function takes a question and context of document text and uses the model to find the answer.

730
01:11:55,854 --> 01:12:01,124
正如你看到的，这里使用 QA 流水线来生成问题的答案。
Here, as you can see, the QA pipeline is used to generate answers to questions.

731
01:12:02,030 --> 01:12:07,396
在这里，结果回答提供答案，而结果分数提供置信度分数。
Here, the result answer provides the answer and result score gives the confidence score.

732
01:12:07,886 --> 01:12:12,964
我们用“什么是可持续发展”这个问题来测试这个函数，并打印出结果。
We test this function with the question, what is sustainable development, and print the result.

733
01:12:13,358 --> 01:12:18,436
所以这里我们用一个示例问题进行了测试，即：什么是可持续发展？
So here we have tested it with a sample question, that is, what is sustainable development?

734
01:12:18,958 --> 01:12:25,348
既然我们已经实现了问答功能，下一步就是评估这些答案的置信度。
Now that we have implemented the question answer, now next step is to evaluate the confidence of this answers.

735
01:12:25,806 --> 01:12:29,028
现在进入代码的评估和日志记录部分。
Now it comes evaluation and logging part of the code.

736
01:12:29,518 --> 01:12:33,636
我们需要评估答案的置信水平并记录结果。
We need to evaluate the confidence level of the answers and log the results.

737
01:12:34,446 --> 01:12:40,068
在这里，评估答案函数会检查置信度分数并对答案质量进行分类。
Here, the evaluate answer function checks the confidence score and classifies the answer quality.

738
01:12:40,622 --> 01:12:43,364
这里你可以看到置信度是一个浮点数。
Here you can see the confidence colon float.

739
01:12:43,854 --> 01:12:48,196
这个参数代表模型生成的答案的置信度分数。
This parameter represents the confidence score of the answer written by the model.

740
01:12:48,718 --> 01:12:52,100
置信度分数通常在 0 到 1 之间。
The confidence score typically ranges from 0 to 1.

741
01:12:52,464 --> 01:13:00,740
0 表示低置信度，1 表示高置信度，反映了模型对答案正确性的确定程度。
0 means low confidence and 1 means high confidence, indicating how certain the model is about the correctness of its answers.

742
01:13:01,390 --> 01:13:08,420
在这里，记录结果函数表示结果已被记录，包括基于置信度的质量分类。
Here, the log result function indicates the result is logged, including the quality classification based on confidence.

743
01:13:09,102 --> 01:13:12,644
结果被记录在评估日志中，以便后续查阅。
The result is logged in the evaluation log for further review.

744
01:13:13,006 --> 01:13:16,544
接下来是回答多个问题并记录它们的结果。
Now next is to answer multiple questions and log their results.

745
01:13:16,846 --> 01:13:24,644
现在开始回答来自文档的多个问题，并记录每个答案及其置信度分数和质量。
So here comes answering the multiple questions from the document and log each answer with its confidence score and quality.

746
01:13:25,518 --> 01:13:29,444
我们遍历一个问题列表，获取答案并将其记录下来。
We loop through a list of questions, get answers, and log them.

747
01:13:30,126 --> 01:13:36,836
提供一个问题列表，智能体使用回答问题函数来回答每个问题。
A list of questions is provided and the agent answers each question using the answer question function.

748
01:13:37,838 --> 01:13:43,748
每个问题的答案、置信度和质量都会被打印并记录，以便后续查阅。
Each question's answer, confidence, and quality are printed and logged for further review.

749
01:13:44,622 --> 01:13:49,540
置信度分数表示模型对提取出的答案的支持程度。
The confidence score indicates how strongly the model supports the extracted answers.

750
01:13:50,414 --> 01:13:56,804
这个输出显示模型从文档中提取出了关于可持续发展的简洁定义。
This output shows the model extracted a concise definition of sustainable development from the document,

751
01:13:57,390 --> 01:14:05,380
而日志中的置信度分数表明答案可能不完整，需要结合更多上下文进行核查。
while the log confidence score indicates the answer may be partial and should be reviewed for expanded using additional context.

752
01:14:06,190 --> 01:14:14,372
最后，我们将所有结果保存到 JSON 文件中，然后将评估结果导出到 JSON 文件以便日后参考。
Finally, we save all our results to a JSON file, then we'll export the evaluation result to a JSON file for future reference.

753
01:14:15,598 --> 01:14:22,480
我们将评估日志写入名为 pdf insightsresults.json 的 JSON 文件。
We write the evaluation log to a JSON file named pdf insightsresults.json.

754
01:14:22,880 --> 01:14:27,204
系统会打印一条消息，确认结果已成功导出。
A message is printed confirming that the results have been successfully exported.

755
01:14:27,598 --> 01:14:28,480
就这样搞定了。
And that's it.

756
01:14:28,878 --> 01:14:38,788
现在你已经构建了一个能够利用 Langchain 和预训练模型来读取、清洗、总结并回答 PDF 文档问题的系统。
You have now built a system that can read, clean, summarize, and answer questions about a PDF document using Langchain and pre-trained models.

757
01:14:39,438 --> 01:14:48,644
在这次实操中，我们成功构建了一个 PDF见解提取器，它可以读取、清洗并理解 PDF 内容，
In this hands-on, we successfully built a PDF Insights extractor that can read a PDF, clean, and understand its content,

758
01:14:49,006 --> 01:14:51,940
生成摘要并回答用户的问题。
generate a summary, and answer user questions.

759
01:14:52,590 --> 01:15:01,920
该系统展示了一个完整的文档智能工作流，它使用的是轻量级的开源工具，而不依赖复杂的框架。
The system demonstrates an end-to-end document intelligence workflow using lightweight open source tools without relying on complex frameworks.

760
01:15:02,080 --> 01:15:07,524
你可能会注意到，在这个例子中，问答输出的置信度分数较低。
You may notice that the confidence score for the question-answering output is low in this example.

761
01:15:08,206 --> 01:15:11,780
这是符合预期的，原因主要有两个。
This is expected and reasonable for two main reasons.

762
01:15:12,270 --> 01:15:17,444
首先，我们处理的是一个包含有限上下文的小样本 PDF。
First, we are working with a small sample PDF containing limited context.

763
01:15:18,190 --> 01:15:24,420
问答模型在有丰富、详细的段落供其提取答案时表现最好。
Question-answering models perform best when they have rich, detailed passages to extract answers from.

764
01:15:25,294 --> 01:15:32,420
当文档内容较短时，模型可能仍能找到正确答案，但会给出一个较低的置信度分数。
When the document content is short, the model may still find the correct answer but assign a lower confidence score.

765
01:15:32,846 --> 01:15:40,932
其次，在目前的实现中，我们直接将整个文档文本作为上下文，而没有进行分块或检索过滤。
Second, in this implementation, we use the entire document text as context without chunking or retrieval filtering.

766
01:15:41,326 --> 01:15:49,680
虽然这让系统保持简单且易于理解，但可能会稀释答案片段的相关性，从而影响置信度评分。
While this keeps the system simple and easy to understand, it can dilute the relevance of the answer span, which affects the confidence scoring.

767
01:15:49,934 --> 01:15:54,660
今天我们要处理构建生产级 AI 系统中的两个关键方面。
Today we are tackling two critical aspects of building production AI systems.

768
01:15:55,182 --> 01:16:02,084
首先是：如何设计能够进行推理、使用工具甚至随着时间推移自我改进的智能体。
First, how to design intelligent agents that can reason, use tools, and even improve themselves over time.

769
01:16:02,446 --> 01:16:11,280
其次是：如何处理 AI 面临的最大挑战之一，也就是幻觉问题，并确保我们的系统提供可信的、
And second, how to handle one of the biggest challenges in AI, that is, hallucinations, and ensure our systems provide trustworthy,

770
01:16:11,440 --> 01:16:13,040
可验证的信息。
verifiable information.

771
01:16:13,454 --> 01:16:14,564
让我们直接进入正题。
Let's dive right in.

772
01:16:14,990 --> 01:16:23,268
首先，我们来聊聊什么是 Langchain 智能体，以及为什么它们在 AI 应用开发中代表了一个巨大的飞跃。
To begin with, let's talk about what Langchain agents are and why they represent a significant leap forward in AI application development.

773
01:16:23,854 --> 01:16:31,428
最重要的一点是，智能体是自主的决策者，它们利用 LLM 来决定采取哪些行动以及执行顺序。
First and foremost, agents are autonomous decision makers that use LLMs to determine which actions to take and in what order.

774
01:16:31,982 --> 01:16:40,196
与我们之前讨论过的、工作流预先定义的链不同，智能体会独立思考并规划自己的路径来解决问题。
Unlike the chains we discussed earlier, where the workflow is predefined, agents think for themselves and chart their own path to solve problems.

775
01:16:40,462 --> 01:16:48,400
其次，它们是配备了工具的系统，可以动态访问搜索引擎、计算器、数据库和 APIs
Second, they are tool-equipped systems that dynamically access search engines, calculators, databases, and APS

776
01:16:48,720 --> 01:16:49,956
来完成任务。
to complete tasks.

777
01:16:50,510 --> 01:16:53,668
你可以把智能体想象成拥有一个工具箱。
Think of agents as having a toolbox at their disposal.

778
01:16:54,062 --> 01:16:59,428
根据当前情况，它们可以在需要的时候去拿任何需要的工具。
They can reach for whatever tool they need whenever they need it based on the situations at hand.

779
01:16:59,918 --> 01:17:09,600
第三，智能体是迭代式的问题解决者，它们会观察行动结果，对结果进行推理，并决定下一步操作直到任务完成。
Third, agents are iterative problem solvers that observe action results, reason about outcomes, and decide next steps until task completion.

780
01:17:09,934 --> 01:17:16,804
它们不仅仅是执行完就结束，还会评估自己是否取得了进展，并相应地调整方法。
They don't just execute and finish, they evaluate whether they are making progress and adapt their approach accordingly.

781
01:17:17,230 --> 01:17:21,732
最重要的一点是，与链不同，智能体是动态且自适应的。
Most importantly, agents are dynamic and adaptive, unlike chains.

782
01:17:22,414 --> 01:17:31,140
链遵循预设路径，而智能体会实时评估情况并根据结果调整策略。
While chains follow a predetermined path, agents assess situations in real time and adjust their strategies based on results.

783
01:17:32,014 --> 01:17:40,132
如果某种方法行不通，它们会转向并尝试不同的做法，就像人类处理陌生问题时一样。
If one approach isn't working, they pivot and try something different, much like how a human would tackle an unfamiliar problem.

784
01:17:41,006 --> 01:17:52,196
这种自主且自适应的能力，让智能体在复杂、不可预测的场景中非常强大，而固定的工作流根本无法满足需求。
This autonomous, adaptive capability makes agents incredibly powerful for complex, unpredictable scenarios where a fixed workflow simply won't suffice.

785
01:17:53,038 --> 01:17:57,444
它们为你的 AI 应用带来了真正的智能和灵活性。
They bring true intelligence and flexibility to your AI applications.

786
01:17:58,126 --> 01:18:03,492
那么，现在让我们来了解 AI 智能体实际运作的基本原理。
So, let's now understand the fundamentals of how AI agents actually work.

787
01:18:04,238 --> 01:18:09,252
如果你曾看过人们解决难题的过程，你就会看到这种模式。
If you have ever watched a person solve a difficult problem, you have seen this pattern.

788
01:18:09,902 --> 01:18:17,380
他们观察情况，思考该做什么，采取行动，看看发生了什么，然后循环往复。
They observe the situation, think about what to do, take action, see what happens, and then repeat.

789
01:18:17,742 --> 01:18:20,452
AI 智能体的工作方式也是一样的。
AI agents work exactly the same way.

790
01:18:21,102 --> 01:18:23,012
这被称为推理循环。
This is called the reasoning loop.

791
01:18:23,760 --> 01:18:26,820
观察、思考、行动，然后重复。
Observe, think, act, and repeat.

792
01:18:27,470 --> 01:18:29,508
它是连续且动态的。
It's continuous and dynamic.

793
01:18:30,062 --> 01:18:36,420
智能体不是在执行预设好的脚本，而是根据遇到的情况进行调整。
The agent isn't just executing a pre-programmed script, it's adapting based on what it encounters.

794
01:18:36,640 --> 01:18:44,228
目前最流行的实现方式是 ReAct 模式，即推理与行动。
Now, the most popular implementation of this is the React pattern, which stands for reasoning and acting.

795
01:18:44,942 --> 01:18:46,116
它的流程如下：
This is how it flows.

796
01:18:46,926 --> 01:18:56,068
智能体会针对需要做什么产生一个想法，决定采取什么行动，比如调用工具或查询数据库，
The agent generates a thought about what it needs to do, decides on action to take, maybe calling a tool or querying a database,

797
01:18:56,750 --> 01:18:59,460
然后获取关于发生了什么的观察结果。
then receives an observation about what happened.

798
01:19:00,430 --> 01:19:05,316
基于该观察结果，它会生成另一个想法，循环继续下去。
Based on that observation, it generates another thought and the cycle continues.

799
01:19:06,446 --> 01:19:08,740
但智能体需要记忆才能发挥作用。
But agents need memory to be effective.

800
01:19:09,198 --> 01:19:11,204
这里我们涉及两个层级。
We work with two layers here.

801
01:19:11,694 --> 01:19:18,372
短期记忆是你的上下文窗口，即智能体当前正在处理的直接对话历史。
Short-term memory is your context window, the immediate conversation history the agent is currently working with.

802
01:19:18,958 --> 01:19:26,404
然后长期记忆利用向量数据库从过去的交互或知识库中检索相关信息。
Then long-term memory uses vector stores to retrieve relevant information from past interactions or knowledge bases.

803
01:19:27,150 --> 01:19:32,420
你可以把短期记忆看作你的工作记忆，而长久记忆则是你的参考资料库。
Think of short-term as your working memory and long-term as your reference library.

804
01:19:32,814 --> 01:19:35,012
而且至关重要的一点是，我们需要护栏。
And critically, we need guardrails.

805
01:19:35,534 --> 01:19:39,172
在智能体处理任何内容之前，我们要验证输入。
Before the agent processes anything, we validate inputs.

806
01:19:39,918 --> 01:19:41,348
这个请求安全吗？
Is this request safe?

807
01:19:41,678 --> 01:19:43,300
它的格式正确吗？
Is it properly formatted?

808
01:19:43,822 --> 01:19:50,916
在智能体生成输出后，我们还要仔细处理它，确保结构正确且逻辑通顺。
And after the agent generates output, we process it carefully to ensure it is structured correctly and makes sense.

809
01:19:51,630 --> 01:19:54,980
这些护栏能防止你的智能体跑偏。
These guardrails prevent your agent from going off the rails.

810
01:19:55,534 --> 01:20:03,524
既然我们了解了核心架构，接下来就来聊聊构建能在生产环境中可靠运行的智能体需要具备哪些要素。
Now that we understand the core architecture, let's talk about what it takes to actually build agents that work reliably in production.

811
01:20:03,982 --> 01:20:11,556
在构建智能体时，有三个不可逾越的要点，能让稳健的生产系统区别于脆弱的原型。
When you're building an agent, there are three non-negotiables that separate robust production systems from fragile prototypes.

812
01:20:12,302 --> 01:20:14,692
第一，清晰的工具架构。
First, clear tool schemas.

813
01:20:15,182 --> 01:20:19,296
你的智能体可以使用的每一个工具，都需要极其清晰的定义。
Every tool your agent can use needs a crystal clear definition.

814
01:20:19,566 --> 01:20:21,188
它接受哪些参数？
What parameters does it accept?

815
01:20:21,934 --> 01:20:24,196
它返回数据的格式是什么？
What format does it return data in?

816
01:20:24,878 --> 01:20:26,084
可能会出什么问题？
What can go wrong?

817
01:20:26,702 --> 01:20:31,396
如果你的智能体有权调用天气 API，那么架构中应该明确说明：
If your agent has access to a weather API, the schema should specify.

818
01:20:32,206 --> 01:20:39,044
该工具接收一个地点字符串，并以 JSON 格式返回温度、天气状况和预报。
This tool takes a location string and returns temperature, conditions, and forecast as JSON.

819
01:20:39,536 --> 01:20:40,740
没有任何歧义。
No ambiguity.

820
01:20:41,358 --> 01:20:48,016
当你的 LLM 准确理解每个工具的功能时，它就能更好地判断何时使用它们。
When your LLM understands exactly what each tool does, it makes better decisions about when to use them.

821
01:20:48,398 --> 01:20:50,724
第二，回退推理路径。
Second, fallback reasoning paths.

822
01:20:51,342 --> 01:20:52,576
事情总会出问题的。
Things will go wrong.

823
01:20:52,846 --> 01:20:57,188
API 超时了，或者数据库暂时无法访问。
API is timeout, databases are temporarily unavailable.

824
01:20:57,806 --> 01:21:00,196
智能体需要预设的备选方案。
The agent needs predefined backup plans.

825
01:21:00,750 --> 01:21:05,092
如果主要的搜索工具失败了，也许它可以尝试次要的数据源。
If the primary search tool fails, maybe it tries a secondary source.

826
01:21:05,774 --> 01:21:13,284
如果计算工具报错了，也许它可以尝试简单的估算，或者向用户寻求澄清。
If a calculation tool errors out, maybe it attempts a simpler approximation or asks the user for clarification.

827
01:21:14,094 --> 01:21:20,068
最糟糕的情况是你的智能体直接停止运行，并返回一个没有任何替代方案的错误信息。
The worst thing that can happen is your agent just stops and returns an error message with no alternative.

828
01:21:20,590 --> 01:21:23,044
第三，人工参与触发机制。
Third, human in the loop triggers.

829
01:21:23,758 --> 01:21:28,676
有些决策太重要或风险太大，不能完全交给 AI 处理。
Some decisions are too important or too risky to leave entirely to AI.

830
01:21:29,294 --> 01:21:36,356
你需要定义明确的阈值：当智能体即将删除数据时，它必须暂停并请求确认。
You need to define clear thresholds where the agent is about to delete data, pause, and ask for confirmation.

831
01:21:37,102 --> 01:21:42,212
如果它对医疗诊断不确定，就转交给人类专家。
If it's uncertain about a medical diagnosis, escalate to a human expert.

832
01:21:42,862 --> 01:21:47,940
如果它在进行超过一定金额的金融交易，则需要获得批准。
If it's making a financial transaction above a certain amount, require approval.

833
01:21:48,590 --> 01:21:54,212
这些触发机制能确保你的智能体是辅助性的，而不是在危险情况下盲目自主运行。
These triggers ensure your agent is assistive, not autonomous in dangerous ways.

834
01:21:54,702 --> 01:22:01,536
既然我们已经涵盖了 Langchain 智能体的基础知识，现在是时候进入实操演示了。
Now that we have covered the basics of what Langchain agents are, now it's time to move on to a hands-on demonstration.

