897
01:28:39,982 --> 01:28:47,268
Langchain 让你有能力构建能够解决复杂任务、且无需硬编码工作流的智能智能体。
Langchain gives you the ability to build the intelligent agents that can solve complex tasks without hard-coded workflows.

898
01:28:47,472 --> 01:28:52,420
现在，尽管这些智能体功能强大，但我们需要解决一个核心问题。
Now, as powerful as these agents are, we need to address the core problem here.

899
01:28:52,672 --> 01:28:54,372
那就是幻觉。
That is hallucination.

900
01:28:55,118 --> 01:29:01,092
即使是最复杂的智能体架构，也无法克服 LLM 面临的基础性挑战。
Even the most sophisticated agent architecture cannot overcome fundamental challenges with LLMs.

901
01:29:01,806 --> 01:29:10,020
所以，幻觉是部署 LLM 到生产环境中的最大障碍，它影响到我们讨论过的每一个智能体，
So, hallucination is the single biggest obstacle to deploying LLMs in production, and it affects every agent we have discussed,

902
01:29:10,192 --> 01:29:12,228
无论它们的架构设计得多么出色。
regardless of how well designed they are.

903
01:29:12,750 --> 01:29:14,820
那么，究竟什么是幻觉？
So, what exactly are hallucinations?

904
01:29:15,438 --> 01:29:18,020
它们是自信但完全错误的输出。
They are confident but completely wrong outputs.

905
01:29:18,894 --> 01:29:29,220
LLM 生成的文本听起来权威、逻辑严密且看似合理，但实际上在事实层面是错误的或完全编造的。
LLM generates the text that sounds authoritative, well-reasoned, and plausible, but it's factually incorrect or entirely fabricated.

906
01:29:29,646 --> 01:29:32,004
让我给你们一些令人警醒的数据。
Let me give you some sobering statistics.

907
01:29:32,686 --> 01:29:39,812
在长文本回复中，研究显示高达 80% 的内容可能包含至少一个虚构的事实。
In long-form responses, studies show that up to 80% can contain at least one fabricated fact.

908
01:29:40,654 --> 01:29:45,872
对于知识密集型任务，错误率在 30% 到 50% 之间。
For knowledge-intensive tasks, error rates sit between 30% to 50%.

909
01:29:46,734 --> 01:29:56,912
而当你要求模型进行多跳推理，即它需要整合多项信息来得出结论时，错误率会飙升到 70% 以上。
And when you ask the model to do multi-hop reasoning where it needs to combine multiple pieces of information to reach a conclusion, error rates jump above 70%.

910
01:29:57,710 --> 01:29:58,820
为什么会发生这种情况？
Why does this happen?

911
01:29:59,374 --> 01:30:01,124
有三个根本原因。
There are three root causes.

912
01:30:01,678 --> 01:30:03,364
第一个是训练数据缺口。
First is training data gaps.

913
01:30:04,142 --> 01:30:07,364
模型是在截止日期之前的特定数据上进行训练的。
The model was trained on data up to a certain cutoff rate.

914
01:30:07,886 --> 01:30:10,404
在那之后的任何内容，模型都必须靠猜测。
Anything after that, the model has to guess.

915
01:30:11,086 --> 01:30:19,396
即使是包含在训练数据中的话题，如果某些内容代表性不足，模型就会因为缺乏强信号而开始胡编乱造。
Even for topics within its training data, if something was underrepresented, the model lacks strong signal and starts making things up.

916
01:30:19,918 --> 01:30:21,988
第二个是上下文窗口限制。
Second is context window limits.

917
01:30:22,702 --> 01:30:29,632
即使是支持 10 万到 20 万标记的现代模型，也无法容纳所有信息。
Even with modern models that support 100,000 to 200,000 tokens, you can't fit everything.

918
01:30:29,902 --> 01:30:36,452
如果相关信息不在上下文中，模型就会填补空白，而且往往填错。
If the relevant information isn't in the context, the model fills in the blanks, often incorrectly.

919
01:30:37,326 --> 01:30:43,332
第三个，这也是 LLM 工作原理的核心：过度自信的标记预测。
Third, and this is a fundamental to how LLMs work, overconfident token prediction.

920
01:30:43,982 --> 01:30:48,484
模型是根据它学到的模式来预测下一个最可能的标记。
The model is predicting the next most likely token based on patterns it learned.

921
01:30:49,006 --> 01:30:53,764
它没有内置机制在不确定时说“我不知道”。
It doesn't have a built in mechanism to say, I don't know, when it's uncertain.

922
01:30:54,222 --> 01:31:00,420
它只会生成看起来更可能的内容，即使这种可能性是建立在不稳固的基础上的。
It just generates whatever seems more probable, even if that probability is based on shaky ground.

923
01:31:01,038 --> 01:31:05,828
生成式人工智能旨在激发你的创造力并加速你的项目。
Generative AI is here to spark your creativity and turbocharge your projects.

924
01:31:06,382 --> 01:31:14,628
无论你是艺术家、作家，还是只是想让内容更出彩的人，这些工具就像是你在创意世界里的新闺蜜。
Whether you are an artist, a writer, or just someone looking to jazz up your content, these tools are like your new BFF in the creative world.

925
01:31:15,182 --> 01:31:16,868
现在我们来聊聊工具。
Now let's talk about tools.

926
01:31:17,326 --> 01:31:23,236
这些工具让生成式人工智能感觉像魔法一样，我们将在本视频中进行探索。
These are gadgets that make generative AI feel like magic, and we will be exploring this in this video.

927
01:31:23,822 --> 01:31:25,604
首先是 ChatGPT。
First is ChatGPT.

928
01:31:26,062 --> 01:31:28,740
ChatGPT 是由 OpenAI 开发的。
ChatGPT was developed by OpenAI.

929
01:31:29,038 --> 01:31:34,948
它是一个顶尖的语言模型，以其对话能力和多样化的应用而闻名。
It is a state-of-the-art language model renowned for its conversational abilities and versatile applications.

930
01:31:35,534 --> 01:31:37,540
第二个是 Microsoft Copilot。
Second, Microsoft Copilot.

931
01:31:37,902 --> 01:31:44,516
它可以在你每天使用的各种应用中运行，比如 Word、Excel、PowerPoint、Outlook 和 Teams。
It works inside apps you already use every day, like Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Teams.

932
01:31:45,006 --> 01:31:51,556
Copilot 可以帮你撰写文档、理解数据、处理重复性任务，并让你更快地完成工作。
Copilot helps you write documents, understand your data, handle repetitive tasks, and get things done faster.

933
01:31:51,950 --> 01:31:55,620
接下来是 Claude，这是由 Anthropic 开发的 AI 助手。
Next, Claude, an AI assistant made by Anthropic.

934
01:31:56,014 --> 01:32:03,332
Claude 以其周全、清晰的回答而闻名，非常擅长写作、分析和解决复杂问题。
Claude is known for thoughtful, clear responses and is great at writing, analysis, and solving complex problems.

935
01:32:03,854 --> 01:32:12,292
最后但同样重要的是 Google Bard，现在被称为 Gemini，它是 Google 的创新 AI 平台，可以无缝处理文本
Last but not least, Google Bard, now known as Gemini, is Google's innovative AI platform which seamlessly navigates through text,

936
01:32:12,640 --> 01:32:17,380
代码、音频、图像和视频，具备多模态等能力。
code, audio, image, video with capabilities like multimodality.

937
01:32:17,806 --> 01:32:28,100
在整个视频中，我们将深入探讨这些工具中的每一个，揭示它们的功能、应用以及在生成式 AI 世界中提供的无限可能。
Throughout this video, we will dive into each of these tools, uncovering their functionalities, applications, and the limitless possibilities they offer in the world of generative AI.

938
01:32:28,782 --> 01:32:32,196
提示工程既是一门艺术，也是一门科学。
Prompt engineering is as much an art as it is a science.

939
01:32:32,814 --> 01:32:34,404
这是一句非常有创意的话。
A very creative line.

940
01:32:34,862 --> 01:32:39,200
等我们理解了什么是真正的提示工程后，我们再来讨论这一点。
We'll come back to this once we understand what is actually prompt engineering.

941
01:32:39,758 --> 01:32:44,560
提示工程由两个词组成：提示和工程。
Prompt engineering is made up of two words, prompt and engineering.

942
01:32:45,166 --> 01:32:53,220
提示不过是给 LLM 或生成式模型提供的一套详细的准则或指令，用于完成某项任务。
Prompt is nothing but a detailed set of guidelines or instructions given to the LLM or generative model to do a task.

943
01:32:53,742 --> 01:33:06,404
工程则是通过迭代开发特定任务的提示词，使生成式模型或 LLM 能输出你所期望的完美或接近完美的成果。
Engineering is developing, iteratively, a task-specific prompt to enable the generative models or LLMs to output a perfect or near-perfect outcome that you have focused for.

944
01:33:06,862 --> 01:33:10,756
所以如果你看到提示工程是一个迭代过程。
So if you see prompt engineering is an iterative process.

945
01:33:11,280 --> 01:33:11,840
怎么理解？
How?

946
01:33:12,462 --> 01:33:15,748
首先是你脑子里产生的一个想要实现什么的想法。
First is the idea that comes to you that you want this.

947
01:33:16,334 --> 01:33:17,764
然后你有一个提示词。
Then you have a prompt.

948
01:33:18,062 --> 01:33:19,300
你设计一个提示词。
You design a prompt.

949
01:33:19,694 --> 01:33:20,932
接着会有结果。
Then there are results.

950
01:33:21,230 --> 01:33:27,600
你把它交给你的模型，比如 ChatGPT，然后你得去测试，获取反馈，对吧？
You give that to your model, your chat GPT, and then you have to test, you have a feedback, right?

951
01:33:28,014 --> 01:33:31,300
所以基本上它就是一个过程，一个迭代过程。
So basically it's a process, an iterative process.

952
01:33:32,078 --> 01:33:37,988
现在，一旦你有了提示词和结果，你可能并不太满意这个结果。
Now, once you have the prompt and you have the results, you might not be very much satisfied with the result.

953
01:33:38,478 --> 01:33:48,000
这就是你要去开发或者与你的 ChatGPT、与你的模型进行对话的地方，去强化模型以给你一个好的结果
This is where you develop or you have a conversation with your chat GPT, with your model, and enforce or reinforce the model to give you a good result,

954
01:33:48,302 --> 01:33:50,596
一个好的输出，也就是你想要的那个。
a good output, which is what you want.

955
01:33:51,054 --> 01:33:58,564
例如，如果你有一个关于协同生成的任务，现在特定的问题陈述可以通过多种方法来解决。
For example, if you have a task on cogeneration, now a specific problem statement can be solved through various methods.

956
01:33:59,022 --> 01:34:01,956
比如，你想输出回文。
For example, you want to output palindrome.

957
01:34:02,382 --> 01:34:04,708
回文可以通过暴力破解来实现。
Palindrome can be done by brute force.

958
01:34:05,262 --> 01:34:09,200
回文也可以通过递归方法、也就是递归来实现。
Palindrome can also be done by recursive method, recursion.

959
01:34:09,440 --> 01:34:15,396
例如，当你给 ChatGPT 一个提示词时，它首先会给你一个暴力破解的方法。
For example, when you give ChatGPT a prompt, it will first give you a brute force method.

960
01:34:16,078 --> 01:34:25,668
你必须不断地去指令、尝试或提供提示词给 ChatGPT，这样它才能为你提供优化后的代码版本。
You have to keep on instructing and providing an attempt or providing a prompt to ChatGPT so that it gives you an optimized version for your code.

961
01:34:26,414 --> 01:34:28,836
这是一个代码生成的例子。
This is an example for code generation.

962
01:34:29,550 --> 01:34:32,676
同样，假设你正在进行内容创作。
Similarly, suppose you have content creation.

963
01:34:33,102 --> 01:34:39,492
你想创作内容，而且这些内容是面向特定受众的。
You want to create content, and your content that you want to create is directed towards a specific target audience.

964
01:34:40,174 --> 01:34:46,404
现在，当你给 Chat GPT 输入提示词时，它给出的结果可能并不理想。
Now, when you give Chat GPT a prompt, the results it will show you might not be satisfying enough.

965
01:34:47,054 --> 01:34:52,324
你必须通过多次迭代告诉 Chat GPT 或你的生成式模型你想要什么。
You have to tell your Chat GPT or your generative model iteratively what you want.

966
01:34:52,910 --> 01:34:53,892
给它们反馈。
Give them feedback.

967
01:34:54,446 --> 01:34:57,444
例如，如果你没得到满意的输出。
For example, you have not received a good output.

968
01:34:57,902 --> 01:35:05,636
你会告诉 Chat GPT，比如：这不是我要的，请根据我的目标受众生成结果。
What you will tell your Chat GPT, for example, this is not what I want, please generate the output based on my target audience

969
01:35:06,062 --> 01:35:08,400
或者根据我提供的反馈来调整，对吧？
or based on my feedback provided, right?

970
01:35:08,846 --> 01:35:11,716
这就是你的反馈或测试发挥作用的地方。
That's where your feedback or test comes into picture.

971
01:35:12,110 --> 01:35:14,960
你必须与生成式模型进行对话。
You have to have a conversation with your generative model.

972
01:35:15,438 --> 01:35:21,412
或者在这种情况下，如果你对 Chat GPT 进行持续的反馈。
Or in this case, if you say, Chat GPT, give them feedback, constant feedback.

973
01:35:21,742 --> 01:35:26,960
告诉它好还是坏，你想修改哪些具体部分，对吧？
It is good, it is bad, it is what specific part you want to be changed, right?

974
01:35:27,470 --> 01:35:29,732
所有这些都是一个迭代过程。
All these things are an iterative process.

975
01:35:30,126 --> 01:35:39,716
这就是为什么我们说提示工程是基于你为特定任务提供的准则或详细指令的迭代过程。
That's why we say prompt engineering is an iterative process based on the guidelines or the detailed set of instructions that you provide for a specific task.

976
01:35:40,334 --> 01:35:41,600
现在让我们往回看一点。
Now let's go back a bit.

977
01:35:41,998 --> 01:35:47,524
我们在开始讲提示工程时说过，它既是一门艺术，也是一门科学。
We said when we started about prompt engineering that it is as much an art as it is a science.

978
01:35:48,142 --> 01:35:49,284
它是如何成为一种艺术的呢？
How is it an art?

979
01:35:50,670 --> 01:35:57,764
它是一种艺术，因为当你构思一个创意并写下提示词时，体现的是你的创造力。
It is an art because when you conceive an idea and when you write a prompt, it is your creativity which comes into picture.

980
01:35:58,158 --> 01:36:06,416
然而，科学部分体现在你向生成式模型、或者 LLM，也就是这里的 Chat GPT，
However, the science part comes in when you provide your generative model, or LLM, or in this case, Chat GPT,

981
01:36:06,734 --> 01:36:08,804
提供提示词并获得结果时。
the prompt and it gives you the result.

982
01:36:09,262 --> 01:36:12,772
因为在后端，存在一种被称为生成式模型的机制。
Because in the back end, there is something called generative models.

983
01:36:13,166 --> 01:36:22,336
其中包含不同的 Transformer 或架构，数十亿个参数在起作用来为你提供这些结果。
There is something called different transformers or architectures that are going into picture where billions of parameters are playing a role to give you this result.

984
01:36:22,798 --> 01:36:24,736
这就是它的科学部分。
That becomes your science part of it.

985
01:36:25,102 --> 01:36:29,540
这就是为什么提示工程是艺术与科学的结合。
That's why prompt engineering is a combination of both an art and science.

986
01:36:30,190 --> 01:36:38,244
既然你已经理解了什么是提示工程，让我们来看看提示工程的核心要素：即提示词。
Now that you have understood what is prompt engineering, let's go and see the vital, the main element of prompt engineering, that is prompts,

987
01:36:38,638 --> 01:36:42,852
没有它，生成式模型或 Chat GPT 就无法工作。
without which generative model, chat GPT will not work.

988
01:36:43,566 --> 01:36:49,412
提示词主要由两个部分组成，即参数和结构。
Prompts are constituted or they contain two parts majorly, that is parameters and structure.

989
01:36:49,998 --> 01:36:53,732
你的提示词中，结构是什么，参数又是什么？
What will be the structure and what will be the parameters of your prompts there?

990
01:36:54,158 --> 01:36:57,924
在设计时，你必须思考如何获得最优的结果。
When you design it, you have to think so that you have an optimized result.

991
01:36:58,350 --> 01:37:03,812
现在结构是我们要重点讨论的内容，至于参数，让我来解释一下。
Now structure is one thing that we'll talk more about, and parameters, here let me explain.

992
01:37:04,302 --> 01:37:06,468
我只挑选了几个参数。
I have only selected a few parameters.

993
01:37:06,766 --> 01:37:07,908
你可以去查更多。
You can search more.

994
01:37:08,302 --> 01:37:10,820
影响提示词效果的参数还有很多。
There are more parameters on which prompts work.

995
01:37:11,342 --> 01:37:19,076
这里我们主要强调三个参数，分别是温度、Top P 和最大长度。
Majorly here we are highlighting only three parameters, that is temperature, top P, and max underscore length.

996
01:37:19,694 --> 01:37:24,612
温度是指当你给提示词提供这个参数时，所产生的随机性。
Temperature is the randomness that comes into picture when you provide that parameter to your prompt.

997
01:37:25,166 --> 01:37:33,572
它的范围是 0 到 1，如果你希望模型更具创意，生成更有创意的回答或结果，
It ranges from 0 to 1, and if you want your model to be creative and generate creative answers or generate creative outcomes,

998
01:37:34,030 --> 01:37:39,044
你的范围或者说你可以把温度设置为 0.7 到 0.8。
your range or you set your temperature to 0.7 to 0.8.

999
01:37:39,790 --> 01:37:49,956
然而，在像代码生成这样的任务中，你不需要创意，所以如果你不想要创意，也可以把温度设为 0。
However, in tasks such as code generation, you don't need creativity, so you can set your temperature to 0 also, where you do not want creativity.

1000
01:37:50,446 --> 01:37:53,572
现在，Top P 其实和温度有点类似。
Now, top P is actually kind of the same as temperature.

1001
01:37:53,870 --> 01:37:55,460
它也涉及到创造力。
It also has creativity.

1002
01:37:55,982 --> 01:37:59,044
Top P 是模型从中选择时的最高概率。
Top P is top probability that it selects from.

1003
01:37:59,534 --> 01:38:03,556
所以你有一个生成式模型，它根据你的提示词生成结果。
So you have a generative model, it generates results based on your prompt.

1004
01:38:04,174 --> 01:38:06,148
现在可能会有很多种结果。
Now there can be n number of results.

1005
01:38:06,638 --> 01:38:09,636
那么这个模型如何决定给你的输出内容呢？
How does that model decide what to put as an output for you?

1006
01:38:10,222 --> 01:38:12,388
这时候，Top P 就派上用场了。
Here, top P comes into picture.

1007
01:38:12,878 --> 01:38:16,816
Top P 越高，你得到的不同创意答案就越多，对吧？
More the top P, more you have different creative answers, right?

1008
01:38:17,230 --> 01:38:19,908
所以，事实类内容用低值，多样性要求高的用高值。
So low for factual, high for diverse.

1009
01:38:20,526 --> 01:38:22,116
最后一个是最大长度。
Last is max length.

1010
01:38:22,510 --> 01:38:25,668
同样，它的作用是控制你的响应长度。
Again, it is written, manage your response length.

1011
01:38:26,190 --> 01:38:30,084
这个参数还能用来控制你生成式模型的成本。
This parameter is to control the cost of your generative model as well.

1012
01:38:30,798 --> 01:38:33,668
到现在，你应该理解什么是提示工程了。
So now you have understood what is prompt engineering.

1013
01:38:33,998 --> 01:38:37,700
什么是提示词，以及你的提示词包含哪两个主要组成部分？
What is a prompt, and what are the two main components of your prompt?

1014
01:38:38,176 --> 01:38:40,548
那就是参数和结构。
That is, parameter and structure.

1015
01:38:41,038 --> 01:38:43,172
现在让我们来看看一个优秀提示词的组成部分。
Now let's see components of a good prompt.

1016
01:38:43,630 --> 01:38:55,856
我们所谓的优秀提示词，是指你的 Chat GPT 或生成式模型能给你提供好的输出、好的结果，并且你不需要频繁给它反馈。
What we mean by good prompt is that your chat GPT, your generative model gives you a good output, your good outcome, and you have fewer feedbacks for your chat GPT or generative model.

1017
01:38:56,334 --> 01:38:57,124
现在来看。
Now let's see.

1018
01:38:57,422 --> 01:39:01,988
第一个，或者我说是前两个，是上下文和指令。
The first, or I would say the first two, are context and instruction.

1019
01:39:02,414 --> 01:39:05,476
这两个可以互换，取决于你想如何设计你的提示词。
These are interchangeable, how you want to design your prompt.

1020
01:39:05,696 --> 01:39:10,980
如果你愿意，你也可以在提示词中先放指令，再放上下文。
If you want, you keep instruction first and then context in your prompt, you can do the same.

1021
01:39:11,822 --> 01:39:16,388
如果你想先放上下文再放指令，也可以这样做。
If you want to keep the context first and then instruction, you can do the same.

1022
01:39:17,230 --> 01:39:21,188
上下文是你想要提供给模型的额外信息。
Context is additional information that you want to provide to your model.

1023
01:39:21,838 --> 01:39:25,892
指令是你希望模型执行的具体任务。
Instruction is a specific task that you want your model to perform.

1024
01:39:26,542 --> 01:39:29,156
例如，如果你想总结一段文字。
For example, if you want to summarize some text.

1025
01:39:29,742 --> 01:39:31,056
这就是你的指令。
That is your instruction.

1026
01:39:31,374 --> 01:39:32,356
总结你的文本。
Summarize your text.

1027
01:39:32,846 --> 01:39:34,148
总结这段文字。
Summarize this text.

1028
01:39:34,830 --> 01:39:37,156
上下文就是你为什么要进行总结。
Context is why you want to summarize.

1029
01:39:37,582 --> 01:39:39,460
你想达到的结果是什么？
What is the outcome you want to achieve?

1030
01:39:40,014 --> 01:39:48,292
比如回到特斯拉的例子，你提供了一个总结的指令，但上下文是你要一份商业报告。
For example, going back to Tesla, there you are providing an instruction to summarize, but the context is that you want a business report.

1031
01:39:48,910 --> 01:39:54,656
从一份商业报告中，你想知道的是 2020 年到 2023 年的利润，对吧？
From a business report, you want what is the profit from 2020 to 2023, right?

1032
01:39:55,182 --> 01:39:57,380
这就是你需要设定的上下文。
So that is the context that you need to set.

1033
01:39:57,838 --> 01:39:58,916
你为什么要这个？
Why do you want this?

1034
01:39:59,278 --> 01:40:00,388
为什么需要它？
Why is it needed?

1035
01:40:00,782 --> 01:40:02,372
接下来是输入数据。
Next is the input data.

1036
01:40:02,734 --> 01:40:04,036
你的输入数据是什么？
What is your input data?

1037
01:40:04,398 --> 01:40:12,420
以特斯拉为例，输入数据就是你提供给 Chat GPT 的商业报告或相关文章。
For the example, Tesla example, the input data is your business report or business article that you will provide to Chat GPT.

1038
01:40:12,718 --> 01:40:17,956
输出指示是关于你想要的输出内容、形式和方式。
An output indicator is what, how, what and how you want as an output.

1039
01:40:18,414 --> 01:40:21,892
例如，你希望输出结果是 CSV 格式。
For example, you want in a CSV format your output.

1040
01:40:22,478 --> 01:40:26,820
假设你想用表格形式，或者图形化展示。
Suppose you want in a tabular format, or you want in a graphical format.

1041
01:40:27,278 --> 01:40:31,108
所以你必须说明你想要什么样的输出内容或什么样式的输出。
So you have to tell what kind of output or what format of output you want.

1042
01:40:31,662 --> 01:40:34,244
这就是一个好的提示词的四个组成部分。
So these are the four components of a good prompt.

1043
01:40:34,798 --> 01:40:43,268
如果你的提示词包含这四点，就能让你的生成式模型、也就是 Chat GPT，给你提供更好且更优质的结果。
If your prompt consists of these four things, you are enabling your generative model, your Chat GPT, to give you better and good results.

1044
01:40:43,790 --> 01:40:45,092
现在我们来看一个例子。
Now let's see an example.

1045
01:40:45,838 --> 01:40:47,972
这里我们将看到情感分析。
Here we will see sentiment analysis.

1046
01:40:48,494 --> 01:40:49,892
我们正在设定上下文。
We are setting up a context.

1047
01:40:50,382 --> 01:40:52,708
上面写着，扮演一名分析师。
It is written, act as an analyst.

1048
01:40:53,166 --> 01:40:59,876
你是在要求你的 Chat GPT 扮演一个在 OTT 平台工作的分析师。
You're acting as you are asking your chat GPT to act like an analyst working for an OTT platform.

1049
01:41:00,302 --> 01:41:07,204
你是在告诉 Chat GPT，你需要根据消费者提供的反馈来进行情感分析。
You are saying your Chat GPT that you will have to perform sentiment analysis based on the feedback provided by the consumers.

1050
01:41:07,854 --> 01:41:10,244
你正在为一家 OTT 平台工作。
You are working for an OTT platform.

1051
01:41:10,574 --> 01:41:14,596
你的消费者就是观看你电影和网络剧的用户。
Your consumers are the users that are seeing your movies, your web series.

1052
01:41:15,150 --> 01:41:19,748
现在，你需要对他们提供的反馈进行情感分析。
Now the feedback that they provide, on that you have to do sentiment analysis.

1053
01:41:20,334 --> 01:41:23,588
这就是你提供给 Chat GPT 的上下文。
This is the context that you are giving to your chat GPT.

1054
01:41:24,110 --> 01:41:29,668
通过提供这些信息，你的 Chat GPT 就知道需要从分析师的角度去思考。
Now, giving this, your chat GPT knows that they need to think from an analyst perspective.

1055
01:41:30,094 --> 01:41:32,132
它们需要进行情感分析。
They need to do sentiment analysis.

1056
01:41:32,718 --> 01:41:34,416
接下来是指令。
Now, second is instruction.

1057
01:41:34,766 --> 01:41:45,604
你要求 ChatGPT 将反馈分类为中性、负面和正面，也就是在告诉 Chat GPT 什么才算正面。
You are saying to ChatGPT to classify the feedback into neutral, negative, positive, where you are instructing or telling your chat GPT that what is positive.

1058
01:41:46,126 --> 01:41:48,580
正面意味着你的消费者是你的支持者。
Positive means your consumer is your promoter.

1059
01:41:48,942 --> 01:41:50,756
负面意味着他们是反对者。
Negative means they are demoter.

1060
01:41:51,214 --> 01:41:54,276
中性意味着他们既不是支持者也不是反对者。
Neutral means they are neither promoter nor demoter.

1061
01:41:54,606 --> 01:41:56,452
他们对你的内容持中立态度。
They are neutral towards your content.

1062
01:41:56,974 --> 01:42:02,724
这就是你给出的指令，告诉 Chat GPT 或生成式模型需要做什么。
This is the instruction that you give what the chat GPT or what generative model needs to do.

1063
01:42:03,150 --> 01:42:05,508
这就是它正在做的事情：分类。
This is what it is doing, classifying.

1064
01:42:05,934 --> 01:42:09,028
接下来是你的输入数据和输出指示。
Next is your input data and your output indicator.

1065
01:42:09,390 --> 01:42:11,588
在那之前，我们先看一个例子。
Before that, let's see an example.

1066
01:42:11,982 --> 01:42:20,548
一个好的提示词，当你提供一个好的提示词时，如果你给生成式模型提供示例，在这里我们使用的是 Chat GPT。
A good prompt, while you are giving a good prompt, if you give examples for your generative model, here in this case we are using Chat GPT.

1067
01:42:21,038 --> 01:42:27,460
如果你给它们一个例子，它们会从这个例子中学习，并根据你的输入数据来给出输出。
If you give them an example, they will learn from this example and train your input data to give the output.

1068
01:42:28,398 --> 01:42:30,532
这里我们提供了两个例子。
Here we have given two examples.

1069
01:42:31,854 --> 01:42:32,612
反馈。
Feedback.

1070
01:42:33,358 --> 01:42:37,028
第一个反馈是：我觉得这部剧还可以。
First feedback is, I think the series was okay.

1071
01:42:37,934 --> 01:42:43,172
第二个反馈是：剧中每个角色的演技都很棒。
Second feedback is the acting of each character in the series was awesome.

1072
01:42:44,174 --> 01:42:46,656
所以，我认为这部剧还可以。
So I think the series was okay.

1073
01:42:47,054 --> 01:42:49,124
它把这个“还可以”识别为中性。
It took this okay as neutral.

1074
01:42:49,678 --> 01:42:51,876
所以这是一个情感：中性。
So this is a sentiment, neutral.

1075
01:42:52,430 --> 01:42:55,684
这里，它把“棒极了”识别为正面。
Here, awesome, it took as positive.

1076
01:42:56,078 --> 01:42:58,436
所以你的情感判定变成了正面。
So your sentiment becomes positive.

1077
01:42:59,406 --> 01:43:04,868
现在你的输入数据是：这部剧的剧情重复且糟糕透顶。
Now your input data is the storyline for the series was repetitive and abysmal.

1078
01:43:05,422 --> 01:43:08,164
而这里的输出指示是：情感。
And your output indicator here is sentiment.

1079
01:43:08,846 --> 01:43:10,532
这个内容的感情倾向是什么？
What is the sentiment for this?

1080
01:43:11,118 --> 01:43:16,036
你正在询问 Chat GPT，整个提示词的情感判定是什么。
You're asking your chat GPT what will be the sentiment of this entire prompt.

1081
01:43:16,686 --> 01:43:24,132
这就是你提供的上下文，告诉 ChatGPT 扮演分析师并进行情感分析。
That is your context that you have given, which tells ChatGPT to act as an analyst and do sentiment analysis.

1082
01:43:24,878 --> 01:43:33,124
它给出了一个指令来对提供的反馈——也就是你的输入数据——进行分类，将其分为正面、
It gives an instruction to classify the feedback provided, that is your input data, and classify that feedback into positive,

1083
01:43:33,376 --> 01:43:34,756
负面和中性。
negative, and neutral.

1084
01:43:36,016 --> 01:43:44,324
这里你还提供了相应的示例，让 ChatGPT 能理解、学习并据此行动。
And here you are giving examples for the same so that your ChatGPT can understand, learn, and then act accordingly.

1085
01:43:45,006 --> 01:43:48,260
现在，这条特定反馈的输出结果是“负面”。
Now the output for this particular feedback is negative.

1086
01:43:48,782 --> 01:43:55,268
所以如果你把这段内容复制粘贴到你的 Chat GPT 中，它会给这条句子返回“负面”的结果。
So if you copy-paste this into your chat GPT, it gives you an output as negative for this sentence.

1087
01:43:55,886 --> 01:43:59,056
这就是你应该这样写提示词的方法，很好。
So this is how you should write your prompt, which is good.

1088
01:43:59,278 --> 01:44:08,004
这些都是构成一个优秀提示词的良好组件，能让 ChatGPT 生成的输出结果准确无误，方便你后续处理。
These are the components, good components, for your prompt, so that the output that Chat GPT generates for you is exact for you to work upon.

1089
01:44:08,526 --> 01:44:11,972
这就是我们对优秀提示词组成部分的理解。
So this is what we understood about components of a good prompt.

1090
01:44:12,590 --> 01:44:23,044
既然你已经了解了优秀提示词的不同组成部分，接下来让我们看看一个实用的清单，在设计高效提示词以获得更好结果时可以参考。
Now that you have seen what are the different components of a good prompt, let's have a look at a good checklist that you can keep in mind while designing an effective prompt for better results.

1091
01:44:23,598 --> 01:44:25,860
第一个是定义目标。
So the first one is defining the goal.

1092
01:44:26,478 --> 01:44:31,588
告诉 ChatGPT 你具体想要做什么，这就叫定义目标。
Telling ChatGPT what exactly you want to do, that is called defining the goal.

1093
01:44:32,270 --> 01:44:34,340
接下来是明确格式。
Next is detail out the format.

1094
01:44:34,958 --> 01:44:39,044
格式是指你希望 Chat GPT 为你提供的输出格式。
Format is output format that you want Chat GPT to provide you.

1095
01:44:39,502 --> 01:44:49,776
例如，就像我之前提到的，它可以是表格、段落、列表、CSV，任何你想要的，而且你还可以按优先级排序
For example, as I told you previously, it can be table, paragraph, list, CSVS, anything that you want, and you can give it in a priority order

1096
01:44:49,936 --> 01:44:50,256
来要求它。
also.

1097
01:44:50,574 --> 01:44:55,748
如果你正在处理这类内容，可以要求 Chat GPT 按优先级顺序提供。
Ask ChatGPT to give you in a priority order if you are working on such content.

1098
01:44:56,110 --> 01:44:57,732
接下来是创建角色。
Next is creating a role.

1099
01:44:58,318 --> 01:45:06,340
如果你还记得我们之前讨论提示词组成部分时提到的那个例子，我们在上下文里写了“扮演一名分析师”。
If you remember the previous prompt that we discussed while learning about components of a good prompt, we told as a context act like an analyst.

1100
01:45:07,022 --> 01:45:15,172
这就是在创建角色，让 Chat GPT 根据你要求的那个角色来分配任务或处理信息。
That is creating a role so that ChatGPT assigns or processes based on your request, based on that role that you are have asked.

1101
01:45:15,726 --> 01:45:20,964
接下来是明确受众是谁，或者澄清目标受众。
Next is clarity on who the audience is, or clarify who the audience is.

1102
01:45:21,582 --> 01:45:29,668
基本上，你是在告诉 Chat GPT：请根据我服务的受众群体来生成输出。
Basically, you are telling ChatGPT please generate the output based on the demography of my audience whom I am catering to.

1103
01:45:30,222 --> 01:45:35,172
如果你在创作内容，它可以是初级、中级或高级水平。
It can be beginner level, intermediate, advanced if you are creating any content.

1104
01:45:36,046 --> 01:45:42,020
如果你在编写代码，可以根据受众提供基础级、功能性或专家级的代码。
If you are creating code, it can be foundational, functional, expert based on the audience.

1105
01:45:42,606 --> 01:45:52,100
此外，如果你是一名老师并使用 Chat GPT，你可以指定：我希望从六年级学生的视角来教授分数概念。
It can also, if you're a teacher and you are using Chat GPT, you can specify, I want to teach fractions from a sixth-class learner perspective.

1106
01:45:52,704 --> 01:46:01,424
或者如果你想创作内容，或者你在处理某些事情时想让某人理解某个特定概念，例如：
Or if you want to create a content, or if you are working on something and you want to make someone understand that particular concept, for example,

1107
01:46:01,806 --> 01:46:04,388
我希望一个 10 岁的孩子能理解什么是提示词。
I want a 10-year-old to understand what is prompt.

1108
01:46:04,910 --> 01:46:07,588
我该如何让那个特定的学习者明白呢？
How would I make that particular learner understand?

1109
01:46:08,046 --> 01:46:16,612
这种明确性，当你把目标受众放入提示词中时，它会生成定制化的反馈，
That kind of clarity, that kind of clarifications, when you put in your prompt what is your target audience, it will generate tailored feedbacks,

1110
01:46:16,878 --> 01:46:18,628
也就是为你量身定制的提示词输出。
tailored outputs for your prompt.

1111
01:46:19,054 --> 01:46:20,804
接下来是提供上下文。
Next is giving context.

1112
01:46:21,422 --> 01:46:31,908
基本上，就是在你的提示词中给 Chat GPT 提供所有可能的额外信息，从而让它明确你请求的目的
Basically, you are giving every possible additional information for Chat GPT in your prompt so that the purpose of your request is clarified to Chat GPT

1113
01:46:32,238 --> 01:46:34,820
并让它生成出你想要的内容。
and the response that it generates is what you want.

1114
01:46:35,342 --> 01:46:37,028
接下来是提供示例。
Next is giving examples.

1115
01:46:37,550 --> 01:46:47,264
我们在之前的环节中了解到，在理解各个组成部分时，提供示例可以训练你的 Chat GPT，或者让它明白你想要什么
We saw in the previous components while we were understanding components that giving example trains your chat GPT or makes it understand that what you want

1116
01:46:47,598 --> 01:46:50,244
并从中学习以产出准确的结果。
and it learns from it to produce accurate results.

1117
01:46:50,798 --> 01:46:52,932
接下来是指定风格。
Next is specifying the style.

1118
01:46:53,326 --> 01:46:56,612
如果你是在为品牌工作，这可以是沟通风格。
It can be communication style if you are working with a brand.

1119
01:46:57,006 --> 01:47:04,484
它可以是你品牌的运作方式，比如非正式或正式的沟通风格，你想怎么做？
It can be how your brand works, communication style such as informal, formal, what do you want to do?

1120
01:47:04,974 --> 01:47:06,724
这样它给出的回复就更符合你的需求。
So it's suitable for your response.

1121
01:47:07,310 --> 01:47:09,252
接下来是定义范围。
Next is defining the scope.

1122
01:47:09,678 --> 01:47:18,372
当你用具体要求来勾勒范围时，除了提供上下文和示例，ChatGPT 还会在这些参数范围内运行。
When you outline the scope with specifications, besides giving context and examples, ChatGPT operates within those parameters.

1123
01:47:18,798 --> 01:47:20,580
比如温度。
For example, temperature.

1124
01:47:21,198 --> 01:47:28,464
当你告诉它，我想要更有创意，我的温度是这个值，我希望我的 top P 是这个值，对吧？
When you are telling, I want to be creative, my temperature is this, I want my top P to be this, right?

1125
01:47:29,166 --> 01:47:32,068
你是在为你的 Chat GPT 定义范围。
You are defining the scope for your Chat GPT.

1126
01:47:32,878 --> 01:47:34,212
应用限制条件。
Applying restrictions.

1127
01:47:34,798 --> 01:47:42,564
限制条件就是你要求的长度，也就是输出长度或你想要的标记长度。
Restrictions becomes your what is supposing length that you want, the output length, the token length that you want.

1128
01:47:43,246 --> 01:47:43,504
A。
A.

1129
01:47:44,014 --> 01:47:47,044
这里有一个限制，但你想的是什么？
There is a restriction, but what is that you want?

1130
01:47:47,502 --> 01:47:55,428
当你应用这些限制时，这些约束会为 Chat GPT 生成相关的回复建立正确的边界。
When you apply those restrictions, those constraints will create right boundaries for Chat GPT to produce relevant responses.

1131
01:47:56,046 --> 01:47:59,044
所以所有这些都是你可以记住的清单。
So all these are checklists that you can keep in mind.

1132
01:47:59,502 --> 01:48:06,724
再次强调，这些清单中的所有要点都围绕我们已经见过的优秀提示词的所有组成部分。
Again, these all pointers in your checklist revolve around all the components of a good prompt that we have already seen.

1133
01:48:07,118 --> 01:48:14,500
但作为一份清单，你可以记住：好的，这些是我在设计提示词时可以遵循的要点。
But as a checklist, you can keep in mind that, okay, these are my pointers which I can follow when I'm designing my prompt.

1134
01:48:15,022 --> 01:48:17,092
这就是你如何写出一个好的提示词。
So this is how you can write a good prompt.

1135
01:48:17,486 --> 01:48:20,836
在技术的每几年里，有些东西不仅仅是变得更好。
Every few years in technology, something doesn't just get better.

1136
01:48:21,070 --> 01:48:22,468
它跨越了一个门槛。
It crosses a threshold.

1137
01:48:22,798 --> 01:48:26,436
它不再感觉像是一个工具，而是开始感觉像一个合作伙伴。
It stops feeling like a tool and starts feeling like a collaborator.

1138
01:48:27,150 --> 01:48:30,628
从基础计算器到电子表格的跨越就是一个门槛。
The jump from basic calculators to spreadsheets was a threshold.

1139
01:48:31,182 --> 01:48:34,468
从纸质地图到 GPS 的跨越也是一个门槛。
The jump from physical maps to GPS was a threshold.

1140
01:48:35,534 --> 01:48:39,716
Chat GPT 第五版代表了 AI 领域的这样一个时刻。
Chat GPT version 5 represents one of those moments in AI.

1141
01:48:40,590 --> 01:48:42,788
并不是因为它更快，虽然它确实变快了。
Not because it's faster, though it is.

1142
01:48:43,664 --> 01:48:55,780
也不仅仅是因为它更聪明，虽然它确实也变聪明了，而是因为它从根本上扩展了 AI 的理解和能力范围，从一个基于文本的助手变成了更完整的存在，
Not just because it's smarter, though it is that too, but because it fundamentally expands what AI can understand and do, moving from a text-based assistant to something far more complete,

1143
