The simplest way to picture it, think of Google Docs, but with an AI co-writer sitting right beside you.

1373
02:08:53,934 --> 02:09:02,244
它不只是在评论框里提供建议，而是主动帮助你构建结构、强化论点、润色语言，
Not just dropping suggestions into a comment box, but actively helping you build structures, strengthen arguments, tighten language,

1374
02:09:02,542 --> 02:09:05,956
并将整篇作品打磨成精美且专业的成品。
and shape the entire piece into something polished and professional.

1375
02:09:06,670 --> 02:09:11,460
你写，ChatGPT 优化；你指引，ChatGPT 调整。
You write, ChatGPT improves, you redirect, ChatGPT adjusts.

1376
02:09:12,302 --> 02:09:17,572
文档在不断进化，而且在每一个环节，你都对最终产出拥有完全的控制权。
The document evolves, and at every point you stay in full control of the final output.

1377
02:09:18,126 --> 02:09:21,188
这是一个实际操作中的具体例子。
Here's a concrete example of what that looks like in practice.

1378
02:09:21,966 --> 02:09:25,188
你正在写一篇关于 AI 对医疗行业影响的报告。
You're writing a report on the impact of AI and healthcare.

1379
02:09:25,774 --> 02:09:33,668
在普通对话中，你会生成一个草稿，当你想要修改时，得往回翻对话流去找到它，然后把它粘贴回来，
In regular chat, you would generate a draft, scroll back through the thread to find it when you wanted to revise it, paste it back in,

1380
02:09:34,032 --> 02:09:37,860
请求更改，然后不断重复这个循环。
request changes, and repeat that cycle over and over.

1381
02:09:38,286 --> 02:09:41,828
在 Canvas 中，文档始终就在你面前。
In Canvas, the document is always right there in front of you.

1382
02:09:42,350 --> 02:09:47,652
你选中一个薄弱的段落并说：强化这个论点并增加一个支持性的统计数据。
You highlight a weak paragraph and say, strengthen this argument and add a supporting statistic.

1383
02:09:48,718 --> 02:09:55,268
ChatGPT 会在文档中直接修改那个特定部分，而其他内容保持不变。
ChatGPT edits that specific section in line in the document while the rest stays exactly as it was.

1384
02:09:55,950 --> 02:10:00,804
你进行检查，保留有用的部分，在需要的地方进一步完善，然后继续推进。
You review it, keep what works, push further where needed, and move forward.

1385
02:10:01,614 --> 02:10:05,668
这是一种本质上不同且显著更好的写作体验。
That is a fundamentally different and significantly better writing experience.

1386
02:10:06,286 --> 02:10:09,092
Canvas 对某些人群来说特别有价值。
Canvas is especially valuable for a few people.

1387
02:10:09,774 --> 02:10:10,948
让我们看看是哪些人。
Let's see who those are.

1388
02:10:11,406 --> 02:10:18,692
它是为那些正在写论文、案例研究或学位论文，需要结构化、循序渐进的草拟支持的学生准备的。
It's for students who are writing essays, case studies, or dissertations who need structured, progressive drafting support.

1389
02:10:19,662 --> 02:10:27,492
也是为在时间压力下制作报告、提案或面向客户的文件的专业人士，以及创作剧本的创作者，
For professionals producing reports, proposals, or client-facing documents under time pressure, for creators working on scripts,

1390
02:10:27,984 --> 02:10:31,588
文章、课程内容或长篇叙事的创作者。
articles, course content, or long-form storytelling.

1391
02:10:31,984 --> 02:10:36,516
任何需要产出实质性且精炼的内容，而不仅仅是快速回答的人。
Anyone who needs to produce something substantial and polished, not just a quick answer.

1392
02:10:37,198 --> 02:10:39,460
Canvas 的实际操作，如何使用它。
Canvas in practice, how to use it.

1393
02:10:40,750 --> 02:10:42,304
我们将逐步演示。
We will see step by step.

1394
02:10:42,702 --> 02:10:44,164
第一步是打开 Canvas。
First step is open Canvas.

1395
02:10:44,686 --> 02:10:48,900
在侧边栏或聊天界面中寻找 Canvas 选项。
Look for the Canvas option in your sidebar or within the chat interface.

1396
02:10:49,550 --> 02:10:56,004
如果你的账号支持，你会看到它作为一个独立于标准聊天环境的专用工作区。
If it's available on your account, you will see it as a dedicated workspace separate from your standard chat environment.

1397
02:10:56,590 --> 02:10:59,492
第二步，从提示词开始或直接书写。
Step two, start with a prompt or write directly.

1398
02:11:00,046 --> 02:11:01,124
你有两种方式。
You have two ways.

1399
02:11:01,518 --> 02:11:10,116
你可以直接在 Canvas 工作区中输入自己的内容，或者给 Chat GPT 一个起始提示词来生成初稿。
Either begin typing your own content directly into the Canvas workspace or give Chat GPT a starting prompt to generate the first draft.

1400
02:11:10,990 --> 02:11:19,264
为一份关于可再生能源在减少碳排放中作用的报告写一段结构化的、600字的引言，语气正式，
Write a structured 600-word introduction for a report on the role of renewable energy in reducing carbon emissions, formal tone

1401
02:11:19,502 --> 02:11:20,932
面向商业受众。
aimed at a business audience.

1402
02:11:21,678 --> 02:11:29,828
输出结果是一个实时可编辑文档，而不是聊天消息，所以你可以立即把它当作一篇作品来处理。
The output appears as a live editable document, not a chat message, so you can immediately begin working with it as a piece of writing.

1403
02:11:30,224 --> 02:11:31,780
协同精炼。
Refine collaboratively.

1404
02:11:32,238 --> 02:11:34,724
这正是 Canvas 体现真正价值的地方。
This is where Canvas earns its real value.

1405
02:11:35,182 --> 02:11:39,108
你可以同时在多个层面上与你的文档进行互动。
You can engage with your document at multiple levels simultaneously.

1406
02:11:39,566 --> 02:11:41,828
Canvas 在每一个层面都能得到优化。
Canvas is refined at every level.

1407
02:11:42,382 --> 02:11:43,556
段落级别的修改。
Section level edits.

1408
02:11:44,206 --> 02:11:45,956
选择一个特定的段落。
Select a specific paragraph.

1409
02:11:46,510 --> 02:11:48,932
这对于普通受众来说太专业了。
This feels too technical for a general audience.

1410
02:11:49,582 --> 02:11:51,780
在不丢失核心要点的前提下简化它。
Simplify it without losing the key point.

1411
02:11:53,198 --> 02:11:54,180
结构化反馈。
Structured feedback.

1412
02:11:54,702 --> 02:11:57,252
这份文档的整体逻辑通顺吗？
Does the overall flow of this document make sense?

1413
02:11:57,934 --> 02:12:00,068
建议给这些章节提供一个更好的排序。
Suggest a better order for those sections.

1414
02:12:01,038 --> 02:12:02,244
扩充内容。
Expanding content.

1415
02:12:02,734 --> 02:12:04,516
第二部分太简略了。
The second section is too brief.

1416
02:12:05,262 --> 02:12:07,652
增加两个支撑点来完善它。
Develop it with two additional supporting points.

1417
02:12:08,366 --> 02:12:09,956
语气和风格调整。
Tone and style adjustments.

1418
02:12:10,542 --> 02:12:13,924
用更自信、更有说服力的语气重写结论。
Rewrite the conclusion in a more confident, persuasive tone.

1419
02:12:14,798 --> 02:12:21,764
全文润色，检查整篇文章的清晰度和一致性，并标出任何感觉薄弱的地方。
Full document polish, review the entire piece for clarity and consistency, and highlight anything that feels weak.

1420
02:12:22,446 --> 02:12:32,164
所有的修改都在文档本身进行，让你的工作保持整洁、直观且可追踪，而不是分散在冗长的对话记录中。
Every change happens within the document itself, keeping your work clean, visible, and trackable rather than fragmented across a long conversation thread.

1421
02:12:32,878 --> 02:12:35,264
最后一步就是准备好后导出。
Last step is nothing but export when ready.

1422
02:12:35,438 --> 02:12:42,148
一旦你的文档达到要求的标准，就将其导出到 Word 或 Google Docs 进行最终排版。
Once your document reaches the standard you need, export it to Word or Google Docs for final formatting.

1423
02:12:43,054 --> 02:12:45,860
引用处理或提交前的准备。
Citation work or submission preparation.

1424
02:12:46,670 --> 02:12:48,356
网络搜索是什么？
Web search, what is it?

1425
02:12:48,750 --> 02:12:49,828
它为什么重要？
Why does it matter?

1426
02:12:50,958 --> 02:12:59,300
让我们回到介绍中提到的第二个场景，因为它揭示了 AI 模型运作方式的一个核心点，以及为什么这很重要。
Let's go back to that second scenario from our introduction because it points to something fundamental about how AI models work and why it matters.

1427
02:13:00,142 --> 02:13:07,172
包括 ChatGPT 在内的每一个语言模型，都是基于截止到特定时间点收集的数据进行训练的。
Every language model, including ChatGPT, is trained on data collected up to a specific point in time.

1428
02:13:07,694 --> 02:13:09,572
这被称为它的知识截止日期。
That's called its knowledge cutoff.

1429
02:13:10,190 --> 02:13:13,156
模型所知道的一切，都是在那个日期之前学到的。
Everything the model knows, it learned before that day.

1430
02:13:13,902 --> 02:13:18,276
过了那个点之后，就模型而言，就没有发生过任何事情。
After that point, as far as the model is concerned, nothing has happened.

1431
02:13:18,990 --> 02:13:24,100
没有新闻，没有新的研究，没有更新的价格，也没有近期的事件。
No news, no new research, no updated prices, no recent events.

1432
02:13:25,102 --> 02:13:29,380
从它的视角来看，世界在过去的某个固定时刻就停止了。
The world stopped from its perspective at a fixed moment in the past.

1433
02:13:30,318 --> 02:13:32,708
对于很多事情来说，这完全没问题。
For many things, that's completely fine.

1434
02:13:33,102 --> 02:13:40,484
解释一个概念、帮你写作、解决逻辑问题，这些都不需要参考今天的头条新闻。
Explaining a concept, helping you write, working through a logic problem, none of that meets today's headlines.

1435
02:13:41,486 --> 02:13:49,188
但只要你的问题涉及任何当前信息，比如现在的新闻动态、某只股票今天的走势趋势，
But the moment your question involves anything current, what's happening in the news right now, what a stock is trending at today,

1436
02:13:49,742 --> 02:13:57,444
或者是明天是否会下雨，或者上个月政策发生了什么变化，默认模型就无法给你准确的帮助。
whether it's going to rain tomorrow, or what changed in a policy last month, the default model simply cannot help you accurately.

1437
02:13:57,966 --> 02:14:00,036
网络搜索彻底改变了这一点。
Web search changes that entirely.

1438
02:14:00,622 --> 02:14:04,484
联网搜索让 Chat GPT 能够实时连接到互联网。
Websearch connects Chat GPT to the live internet in real time.

1439
02:14:05,390 --> 02:14:14,832
当你问一个需要当前信息的问题时，它会去搜索网络，检索相关内容，并将其带入你的对话中，
When you ask a question that needs current information, it goes to and searches the web, retrieves what's relevant, and brings it back into your conversation,

1440
02:14:15,150 --> 02:14:17,860
为你提供基于当下事实的答案。
giving you answers grounded in what's true today.

1441
02:14:18,158 --> 02:14:21,316
但这里有一个关键的区别，不仅仅是切换到谷歌搜索。
But here's the important distinction from just switching to Google.

1442
02:14:21,998 --> 02:14:24,964
当你使用搜索引擎时，你得到的是一串链接。
When you use a search engine, you get a list of links.

1443
02:14:25,646 --> 02:14:33,444
你还得一个一个点开，阅读内容，判断哪个来源最可靠，提取相关信息，
You still have to open each one, read through the content, figure out which source is most reliable, extract what's relevant,

1444
02:14:33,774 --> 02:14:35,556
然后自己把答案拼凑出来。
and piece together your own answer.

1445
02:14:36,142 --> 02:14:40,036
而当 ChatGPT 使用网络搜索时，它会为你完成所有这些步骤。
When ChatGPT uses Web Search, it does all of that for you.

1446
02:14:40,718 --> 02:14:49,316
它会检索信息，进行评估，并给出一个清晰、直接的对话式回答，其中已经包含了它找到的内容。
It retrieves the information, evaluates it, and delivers a clear, direct conversational answer that already incorporates what it found.

1447
02:14:50,126 --> 02:14:58,116
你将获得搜索引擎的实时触达能力，并结合 AI 理解所获信息的语言智能。
You will get the real-time reach of a search engine combined with the language intelligence of an AI that knows how to make sense of what it finds.

1448
02:14:59,278 --> 02:15:01,604
当你需要时，网络搜索能提供最大的价值。
Web search adds the most value when you need.

1449
02:15:02,062 --> 02:15:03,684
比如突发新闻和时事。
Breaking news and current events.

1450
02:15:04,750 --> 02:15:07,072
这周 G20 峰会发生了什么？
What happened at the G20 summit this

1451
02:15:07,072 --> 02:15:09,156
实时数据和数字。
week? Live data and figures.

1452
02:15:09,870 --> 02:15:13,252
现在的 USD 对 INR 的汇率是多少？
What is the USD to INR exchange rate right now?

1453
02:15:13,934 --> 02:15:14,884
天气预报。
Weather forecasts.

1454
02:15:15,854 --> 02:15:17,924
这周末班加罗尔的天气怎么样？
What's the weather in Bangalore this weekend?

1455
02:15:18,606 --> 02:15:20,676
最新的产品或技术更新。
Recent product or technology updates.

1456
02:15:21,422 --> 02:15:23,844
最新版 Android 发布了哪些新功能？
What are the new features in the latest Android release?

1457
02:15:24,878 --> 02:15:35,268
快速变动的议题、政策变化、市场波动、选举结果、体育赛事，任何上个月的答案可能就过时的内容。
Fast moving topics, regulatory changes, market movements, election outcomes, sports results, anything where last month's answers might already be wrong.

1458
02:15:35,790 --> 02:15:39,364
网络搜索与深度研究，知道该用哪一个。
Web search versus deep research, knowing which to use.

1459
02:15:40,398 --> 02:15:43,940
既然这两个工具都涉及连接互联网，这是一个很合理的问题。
Since both tools involve going to the internet, it's a fair question.

1460
02:15:44,846 --> 02:15:46,436
什么时候用这一个？
When do you use one versus?

1461
02:15:47,310 --> 02:15:47,792
什么时候用那个？
The other?

1462
02:15:48,430 --> 02:15:56,068
网络搜索用于快速获取当前事实和实时数据，而深度研究用于复杂的跨多源分析和报告。
Web search is used for quick current facts and live data, whereas deep research is used for complex multi-source analysis and reports.

1463
02:15:56,526 --> 02:16:00,036
说到速度，网络搜索的结果非常快。
When it comes to speed, web search is fast in results.

1464
02:16:00,526 --> 02:16:05,700
它能在几秒钟内给出结果，但深度研究的设计初衷就是更慢、但更全面。
It gives results in seconds, but deep research is slower but more thorough by design.

1465
02:16:06,478 --> 02:16:16,420
在输出风格方面，网络搜索是简洁的直接回答，而深度研究则是跨多个来源的结构化综合。
When it comes to output style, in web search it is concise and it is a direct answer, but in deep research it is structured synthesis across multiple sources.

1466
02:16:17,262 --> 02:16:28,292
网络搜索非常适合天气、价格、近期新闻、快速查询等场景，而深度研究则适用于政策对比、
Web search is ideal for use cases like weather, prices, recent news, quick lookups, etc., whereas deep research comes into the picture in policy comparisons,

1467
02:16:28,592 --> 02:16:30,980
学术研究和市场分析。
academic research, and market analysis.

1468
02:16:31,502 --> 02:16:32,644
需要注意什么？
What to keep in mind?

1469
02:16:33,004 --> 02:16:35,332
它需要 Plus 或企业版。
It requires Plus or Enterprise.

1470
02:16:35,852 --> 02:16:38,724
免费计划无法使用网络浏览功能。
Web browsing is not available on the free plan.

1471
02:16:39,245 --> 02:16:44,932
如果你使用的是免费账户且需要获取最新信息，升级到 Plus 是最直接的途径。
If you are on a free account and need current information, upgrading to Plus is the most direct path.

1472
02:16:45,518 --> 02:16:47,716
付费墙内容无法访问。
Paywalled content is inaccessible.

1473
02:16:48,236 --> 02:16:54,660
订阅制的媒体、有付费墙的学术期刊以及类似的资源都无法获取。
Subscription based news outlets, academic journals behind paywalls, and similar sources cannot be accessed.

1474
02:16:55,662 --> 02:16:58,980
WebSear 只能处理公开可用的信息，
WebSear works with publicly available information only,

1475
02:16:59,662 --> 02:17:02,212
速度更快，但不如深度研究全面。
faster but less comprehensive than deep research.

1476
02:17:03,214 --> 02:17:06,052
网络搜索针对速度和直接性进行了优化。
Web search is optimized for speed and directness.

1477
02:17:06,830 --> 02:17:12,611
对于需要深入分析的、复杂的、多维度的课题，深度研究会更适合你。
For nuanced, multidimensional topics that need thorough analysis, deep research will serve you better.

1478
02:17:13,262 --> 02:17:19,716
在涉及重大决策时，务必核实高风险信息，如医疗、金融和法律领域。
Verify high-stakes information for important decisions, medical, financial, legal.

1479
02:17:20,558 --> 02:17:24,772
始终将网络搜索返回的结果与权威的原始资料进行交叉比对。
Always cross-check what web search returns with authoritative primary sources.

1480
02:17:25,294 --> 02:17:29,904
AI 的总结能力很强，但关键决策仍需直接核实。
AI summarizes well, but critical decisions deserve direct verification.

1481
02:17:30,222 --> 02:17:40,624
回想一下你上一次脑子里产生灵感的时候：一个生动的场景、一个概念、或者一个你想展示给别人看但无法实现的画面，仅仅是因为你不会画画，
Think about the last time you had an idea in your head: a vivid scene, a concept, a visual you wanted to show someone but couldn't bring it to life because you didn't know how to draw,

1482
02:17:40,864 --> 02:17:42,980
不会设计，甚至不会剪辑视频。
design, or even edit the video.

1483
02:17:43,758 --> 02:17:56,611
也许你需要一个产品原型、一个演示文稿的缩略图，或者一段解释想法的短片，而你脑中的想象与实际创作能力之间的差距让你感到很受挫。
Maybe you needed a product mock-up, a thumbnail for a presentation, a short clip to explain an idea, and the gap between what you imagined and what you could actually create felt frustratingly wide.

1484
02:17:57,454 --> 02:17:59,522
如果这个差距不再存在呢？
What if that gap no longer existed?

1485
02:18:00,046 --> 02:18:09,636
如果你只需用简单的语言描述你脑海中看到的画面，AI 就能在几秒钟内为你生成精美的图像或动态视频呢？
What if you could simply describe what you see in your mind in plain language, and an AI would build it for you in seconds as a polished image or a moving video?

1486
02:18:10,540 --> 02:18:12,227
这不再是科幻小说了。
That's not science fiction anymore.

1487
02:18:12,686 --> 02:18:17,442
这正是当今的 AI 图像和视频生成工具所能实现的。
That's exactly what today's AI image and video generation tools make possible.

1488
02:18:17,870 --> 02:18:20,388
什么是 AI 图像和视频生成？
What AI image and video generation is.

1489
02:18:21,358 --> 02:18:29,892
AI 图像和视频生成是指一类可以直接根据文本提示词创建图像和视频的工具。
AI image and video generation refers to a category of tools that can create both images and videos directly from text prompts.

1490
02:18:30,894 --> 02:18:32,644
让我们用通俗易懂的话来解释一下。
Let's unpack that in plain terms.

1491
02:18:33,230 --> 02:18:37,668
这些工具是多模态的，这意味着它们可以处理多种类型的输出。
These tools are multimodal, meaning they work across multiple types of output.

1492
02:18:38,316 --> 02:18:40,516
你提供语言，它们为你呈现图像。
You give them language, they give you imagery.

1493
02:18:41,070 --> 02:18:49,252
把它们想象成高超的数字艺术家，他们研究过数百万张图片、电影、绘画和照片，
Think of them as highly skilled digital artists, ones that have studied millions of images, films, paintings, and photographs,

1494
02:18:49,870 --> 02:18:55,075
现在他们能根据你的文字描述，将其转化为符合你意图的视觉效果。
and can now take your written description and turn it into a visual that matches your intent.

1495
02:18:55,982 --> 02:19:04,644
你输入“黎明时分宁静的渔村，雾气在水面上弥漫，温暖的橙色光芒穿透云层”。
You type a quiet fishing village at dawn, fog rolling over the water, warm orange light breaking through the clouds.

1496
02:19:05,709 --> 02:19:14,144
模型会读取这些内容并将其构建出来，无论是作为一张令人惊叹的静态图像，还是一个包含动态、
The model reads that and builds it, either as a stunning still image or as a short cinematic video clip with motion,

1497
02:19:14,384 --> 02:19:15,652
光影和氛围的短篇电影片段。
light, and atmosphere.

1498
02:19:16,224 --> 02:19:20,036
不需要设计技能，不需要软件培训，只需要你的文字。
No design skills, no software training, just your words.

1499
02:19:20,846 --> 02:19:22,624
你可能听说过 DAL E3。
You may have heard of DAL E3.

1500
02:19:23,214 --> 02:19:34,980
它是目前直接内置在 Chat GPT 中的主要图像生成工具，并且仍然是目前最易获取且应用最广泛的图像生成工具之一。
It is currently the primary image generation tool built directly into Chat GPT, and it remains one of the most accessible and widely used image generation tools available today.

1501
02:19:35,918 --> 02:19:46,308
另外，该领域已扩展到视频生成。这是一个本质上更难的挑战，因为生成视频意味着要生成数百帧连贯的画面，
Separately, the field has expanded into video generation, a fundamentally harder challenge because generating video means producing hundreds of consistent frames,

1502
02:19:46,784 --> 02:19:47,556
而不仅仅是一张。
not just one.

1503
02:19:47,918 --> 02:19:57,380
AI 不仅需要让画面看起来正确，还需要在不同时间点保持光影、物理规律和动作的一致性，让运动看起来自然。
The AI doesn't just need to make something that looks right, it needs to make something that moves right with consistent lighting, physics, and motion across time.

1504
02:19:58,318 --> 02:20:06,436
这是两条截然不同且平行的路径：图像生成和视频生成，两者都在快速演进。
These are two distinct and parallel tracks, image generation and video generation, and both have continued to evolve rapidly.

1505
02:20:06,990 --> 02:20:10,564
那么 AI 图像生成在幕后究竟是如何运作的呢？
How does AI image generation actually work behind the scenes?

1506
02:20:11,566 --> 02:20:17,092
让我们来看看从你输入提示词到视觉效果呈现出的那一刻，发生了什么。
Let's look at what happens from the moment you type your prompt to the moment your visual appears.

1507
02:20:17,742 --> 02:20:19,908
第一步是场景理解。
The first one is the scene understanding.

1508
02:20:20,654 --> 02:20:26,532
模型做的第一件事是仔细阅读你的提示词，并将其分解为各个组成部分。
The first thing the model does is read your prompt carefully and break it down into its components.

1509
02:20:27,502 --> 02:20:28,868
以这个提示词为例：
Take this example prompt

1510
02:20:29,678 --> 02:20:36,964
“落日余晖下的未来城市天际线，赛博朋克风格，潮湿街道上的霓虹倒影。”
a futuristic city skyline at sunset, cyberpunk style, neon reflections on wet streets.

1511
02:20:38,318 --> 02:20:46,416
模型识别出场景（城市天际线）、时间和光影（落日、霓虹灯、倒影），
The model identifies the setting, a city skyline, the time and lighting, sunset, neon lights, reflections,

1512
02:20:46,798 --> 02:20:52,228
以及风格为赛博朋克，这暗示了特定的颜色、纹理和氛围。
and the style being cyberpunk, which implies specific colors, textures, and mood.

1513
02:20:52,942 --> 02:20:58,724
还有环境细节：潮湿的街道、增强的雨意、表面上的倒影。
The atmospheric detail, wet streets, amplified rain, reflections on surfaces.

1514
02:20:59,406 --> 02:21:07,748
它不仅仅是在读取关键词，而是在生成第一个像素之前，就在构建一个丰富的场景内部表征。
It's not just reading keywords, it's building a rich internal representation of the scene before a single pixel is generated.

1515
02:21:08,686 --> 02:21:13,060
第二步是生成，即图像是如何真正构建出来的。
The second step is generation, how the image is actually built.

1516
02:21:13,902 --> 02:21:22,468
这里变得有趣了，如果你之前听过本课程中关于 Transformer 架构的部分，你会发现一些熟悉的点。
Here's where it gets interesting, and if you followed the Transformer Architecture section earlier in this course, you will recognize something familiar.

1517
02:21:23,118 --> 02:21:28,964
现代 AI 图像生成模型（包括 DALL-E 3）使用的是一种叫做“扩散”的过程。
Modern AI image generation models, including DAO E3, use a process called diffusion.

1518
02:21:29,358 --> 02:21:35,300
它不像人类艺术家那样从零开始绘制图像，而是从相反的端点开始。
Rather than drawing an image from scratch the way a human artist would, the model starts from the opposite end.

1519
02:21:35,982 --> 02:21:44,964
它始于本质上纯粹的随机噪声——一个完全无结构的像素场，然后逐步向后推演，
It begins with what is essentially pure random noise, a completely unstructured field of pixels, and then works backwards step by step,

1520
02:21:45,422 --> 02:21:51,108
去除噪声并逐渐细化图像，直到呈现出连贯且有意义的内容。
removing the noise and progressively refining the image until something coherent and meaningful emerges.

1521
02:21:52,494 --> 02:21:55,460
每一个细化步骤都由你的文本提示词来引导。
Each refinement step is guided by your text prompt.

1522
02:21:56,078 --> 02:22:01,156
所以，在每一个阶段，模型都在自问：这看起来更像描述的内容了吗？
So at every stage the model is asking, does this look more like what was described?

1523
02:22:01,710 --> 02:22:04,324
它会不断调整，直到答案变成“是”。
And it keeps adjusting until the answer is yes.

1524
02:22:05,166 --> 02:22:09,444
执行这种细化操作的组件——去噪器，就是一个 Transformer。
The component doing that refinement, the denoiser, is a transformer.

1525
02:22:09,838 --> 02:22:15,364
也就是说，在 ChatGPT 中处理语言的相同架构，也以不同的形式存在于此。
So the same architecture that processes language in ChatGPT is also in a different form.

1526
02:22:15,822 --> 02:22:17,988
是什么让你的图像成型？
What shapes your image into existence?

1527
02:22:18,478 --> 02:22:22,660
这就是为什么这些模型有时被称为扩散 Transformer。
That's why these models are sometimes called diffusion transformers.

1528
02:22:23,534 --> 02:22:28,580
它们将扩散过程与你已经熟悉的 Transformer 架构结合在了一起。
They combine the diffusion process with the transformer architecture you already know.

1529
02:22:29,646 --> 02:22:40,388
对于视频，这个过程不是只运行一次，而是跨越数百帧，模型必须确保每一帧都与前后帧保持一致，
For video, this process runs not just once but across hundreds of frames, and the model has to ensure that each frame is consistent with the ones before and after it,

1530
02:22:40,878 --> 02:22:44,804
这样动作才会感觉自然连贯，而不是断断续续的。
so the motion feels natural and continuous rather than disjoint.

1531
02:22:46,190 --> 02:22:55,588
这就是为什么生成视频比生成图像要难得多，也是为什么视频生成工具的成熟速度目前仍快于图像工具的原因。
This is why generating a video is significantly harder than generating an image, and why video generation tools are still maturing faster than image tools.

1532
02:22:56,302 --> 02:23:04,068
最后一点，最终产出，也就是最终结果，是以一张精美的图片或一段短视频片段呈现的，
And last but not the least, the final output, the final result, is delivered as a polished image or a short video clip,

1533
02:23:04,656 --> 02:23:08,740
根据你的要求，可以是写实的、有风格化的或者电影感的。
realistic, styled, or cinematic, depending on what you asked.

1534
02:23:09,422 --> 02:23:13,060
四，现代 AI 图像和视频工具的核心功能。
Four, key features of modern AI image and video tools.

1535
02:23:13,742 --> 02:23:18,148
以下是让这一代工具在创意工作中真正强大的原因。
Here's what makes this generation of tools genuinely powerful for creative work.

1536
02:23:18,958 --> 02:23:19,780
双重输出。
Dual output.

1537
02:23:20,110 --> 02:23:22,916
最强的工具可以同时处理图像和视频。
The best tools handle both images and videos.

1538
02:23:23,438 --> 02:23:26,820
你并不总是需要针对不同的视觉格式去切换不同的平台。
You don't always need separate platforms for different visual formats.

1539
02:23:27,566 --> 02:23:28,260
风格多样性。
Style range.

1540
02:23:28,878 --> 02:23:33,028
你可以要求生成看起来像专业摄影作品的写实效果，
You can ask for photorealistic outputs that look like professional photographs,

1541
02:23:33,742 --> 02:23:41,936
或者像电影镜头的电影感镜头、卡通或插画风格、抽象艺术、水彩画，
cinematic shots that feel like movie frames, cartoon or illustrated styles, abstract art, watercolor paintings,

1542
02:23:42,176 --> 02:23:42,596
等等。
and more.

1543
02:23:43,406 --> 02:23:46,948
这些风格完全通过对你提示词的理解来控制。
The style is controlled entirely through your prompt understanding.

1544
02:23:48,206 --> 02:23:51,908
这些模型可以理解非常具体的指令。
These models can interpret highly specific instructions.

1545
02:23:52,814 --> 02:24:01,572
你可以描述反射、时间段、相机角度、运动轨迹、天气，模型会尝试遵循每一个细节。
You can describe reflections, time of day, camera angle, movement, weather, and the model will attempt to honor each detail.

1546
02:24:02,382 --> 02:24:05,572
你的提示词越精确，输出的内容就越符合你的需求。
The more precise your prompt, the more tailored your output.

1547
02:24:08,686 --> 02:24:11,652
其中许多工具都集成在更广泛的 AI 平台中。
Many of these tools work within broader AI platforms.

1548
02:24:12,302 --> 02:24:22,436
DAL E3 直接内置于 Chat GPT 中，这意味着你可以使用同一个对话来优化提示词并生成图像，而无需切换工具。
DAL E3 is built directly into Chat GPT, meaning you can use the same conversation to refine your prompt and generate your image without switching tools.

1549
02:24:23,374 --> 02:24:30,020
如果你不确定如何描述你想要的内容，可以先让 ChatGPT 帮你写一个更好的视觉提示词。
If you're not sure how to describe what you want, you can ask ChatGPT to help you write a better visual prompt first.

1550
02:24:31,246 --> 02:24:33,700
这些工具可以在什么时候、什么地方使用？
When, where can these tools be used?

1551
02:24:34,304 --> 02:24:35,652
实际应用场景。
Real world applications.

1552
02:24:36,334 --> 02:24:37,732
让我们来看看实际应用。
Let's make this practical.

1553
02:24:38,510 --> 02:24:42,304
以下是 AI 图像和视频生成真正能提供价值的领域。
Here's where AI image and video generation genuinely adds value.

1554
02:24:42,606 --> 02:24:44,164
首先是针对图像：
First thing is for images:

1555
02:24:44,846 --> 02:24:53,156
为教学内容创建视觉辅助工具和图表，为博客、书籍或演示文稿生成插图，
creating visual aids and diagrams for educational content, generating illustrations for blogs, books, or presentations,

1556
02:24:53,806 --> 02:24:56,964
在没有平面设计师的情况下制作社交媒体图形，
producing social media graphics without a graphic designer,

1557
02:24:57,678 --> 02:25:04,036
为早期构思建立产品概念模型，设计缩略图、横幅或封面艺术。
building product concept mock-ups for early stage ideation, designing thumbnails, banners, or cover art.

1558
02:25:04,910 --> 02:25:14,436
接下来是视频：创建简短的讲解视频、课程或培训材料的片段，制作用于社交平台的宣传或营销内容，
Then comes for videos: creating short explainer, clips for courses or training materials, producing promotional or marketing content for social platforms,

1559
02:25:14,894 --> 02:25:27,300
为推介或提案生成叙事性视觉效果，将难以用文字表达的概念动画化，在投入全套制作之前构建原型视频内容。
generating, storytelling visuals for pitches, or proposals, animating concepts that are difficult to explain in words alone, building prototype video content before investing in full whole production.

1560
02:25:28,366 --> 02:25:35,172
所有这些的共同点是：你用几分钟精心构思的提示词，取代了数小时的高技能人工劳动。
The common thread across all of these is you're replacing hours of skilled work with minutes of thoughtful prompting.

1561
02:25:35,790 --> 02:25:37,508
如今值得了解的工具。
The tools worth knowing today.

1562
02:25:38,446 --> 02:25:42,564
AI图像和视频生成领域已经有了显著的扩展。
The AI image and video generation landscape has expanded significantly.

1563
02:25:42,990 --> 02:25:47,620
以下是目前最相关的、正在使用的图像工具实操概览。
Here's a practical overview of the most relevant currently active tools for images.

1564
02:25:48,238 --> 02:25:57,860
第一个是 DAL E3，它直接内置在 ChatGPT 中，是任何已经使用 ChatGPT 平台的人最容易上手的切入点。
The first one is DAL E3, built directly into ChatGPT, the most accessible starting point for anyone already using the ChatGPT platform.

1565
02:25:58,318 --> 02:26:03,140
无需额外设置，在 ChatGPT Plus 及以上版本即可使用。
No additional setup required, available on ChatGPT Plus and above.

1566
02:26:03,662 --> 02:26:12,740
接下来是 Midjourney，它被广泛认为能生成目前最高质量、视觉效果最精良的 AI 图像。
Then comes Midjourney, widely regarded for producing some of the highest quality, most visually refined AI images currently available.

1567
02:26:13,486 --> 02:26:18,756
深受追求对输出结果有精细艺术控制的设计师和创意专业人士的青睐。
Favored by designers and creative professionals who want fine artistic control over their outputs.

1568
02:26:19,150 --> 02:26:28,932
Adobe Firefly，它集成了到 Adobe 的创意套件中，并且专门在获得授权的内容上进行训练，是商业用途中更安全的选择之一。
Adobe Firefly, integrated into Adobe's creative suite and specifically trained on licensed content, making it one of the safer options for commercial use.

1569
02:26:29,838 --> 02:26:31,428
非常适合那些已经在用
Ideal for anyone already.

1570
02:26:32,142 --> 02:26:33,540
Adobe 工具的人。
Working with Adobe Tools.

1571
02:26:34,254 --> 02:26:36,036
AI 视频生成工具。
AI video generation tools.

1572
02:26:36,942 --> 02:26:42,180
第一个是 Runway ML，它是最成熟的 AI 视频生成平台之一。
The first one is Runway ML, one of the most established AI video generation platforms.

1573
02:26:42,798 --> 02:26:48,068
支持文本转视频、图像转视频动画以及 AI 辅助编辑。
Supports text-to-vide, image-to-video animation, and AI-assisted editing.

1574
02:26:48,846 --> 02:26:53,188
被独立创作者、电影制作人和营销团队广泛使用。
Used by independent creators, filmmakers, and marketing teams.

1575
02:26:54,670 --> 02:27:03,236
Google V02，这是 Google 的高质量视频生成模型，能够根据
Google V02, Google's high-quality video generation model capable of producing detailed realistic video clips from

1576
02:27:03,584 --> 02:27:08,036
书写的提示词生成细节丰富的写实视频片段，并正逐步整合到 Google 的创意工具中。
written prompts, being progressively integrated into Google's creative tools.

1577
02:27:08,814 --> 02:27:19,268
Kling AI，以产出流畅且真实的动态著称，尤其是在涉及人体动作的场景中，可以通过网页端进行免费和付费试用。
Cling AI, known for producing smooth realistic motion, particularly for scenes involving human movement, available via web with free and paid trials.

1578
02:27:20,238 --> 02:27:21,252
为什么这很重要？
Why this matters?

1579
02:27:21,998 --> 02:27:29,828
在人类历史的大部分时间里，将一个想法转化为视觉效果需要深厚的技能、昂贵的工具，或者两者兼具。
For most of human history, turning an idea into a visual required either deep skill, expensive tools, or both.

1580
02:27:31,022 --> 02:27:37,124
电影制作人需要团队，设计师需要多年的培训，营销人员则需要预算。
A filmmaker needed a crew, a designer needed years of training, a marketer needed a budget.

1581
02:27:38,158 --> 02:27:41,508
AI 图像和视频生成开始改变这一切。
AI image and video generation begins to change that.

1582
02:27:42,062 --> 02:27:48,260
它将创作能力从少数人的手中转移到任何有想法并能用文字描述它的人手中。
It moves creative power from the hands of the few to anyone with an idea and the words to describe it.

1583
02:27:48,878 --> 02:27:51,716
这些工具并不是要取代艺术家或电影制作人。
These tools don't replace artists or filmmakers.

1584
02:27:52,526 --> 02:28:02,212
熟练的人类创造力依然能产出 AI 无法企及的作品，但它们确实让其他人也能参与到以前根本无法参与的创意创作中。
Skilled human creativity still produces work that AI cannot, but they do give everyone else a seat at the creative table that simply wasn't available before.

1585
02:28:02,478 --> 02:28:13,540
随着这些工具在技术、法律和伦理方面不断成熟，了解它们的强大之处以及界限所在，能让你不仅成为一个能力出众的，
And as these tools continue to mature technically, legally, and ethically, understanding both their power and their boundaries is what makes you not just a capable user,

1586
02:28:13,902 --> 02:28:15,172
而且是一个负责任的使用者。
but a responsible one.

1587
02:28:15,502 --> 02:28:20,324
使用诸如深度研究、创建图像和智能体模式等额外工具。
Use additional tools like deep research, create image, and agent mode.

1588
02:28:21,262 --> 02:28:23,524
这里有一个值得思考一下的问题。
Here's a question worth sitting with for a moment.

1589
02:28:24,110 --> 02:28:28,068
当你最初开始使用 Chat GPT 时，你是用它来做什么的？
When you first started using Chat GPT, what did you use it for?

1590
02:28:29,102 --> 02:28:35,876
可能是回答问题、起草邮件、或者总结文档之类的，而且它确实很有用。
Probably something like answering a question, drafting an email, maybe summarizing a document, and it was useful.

1591
02:28:36,238 --> 02:28:44,164
但在某个时刻，你可能会遇到瓶颈，也就是你会想：要是它能直接帮我找到最新的信息就好了，
But at some point, you might have hit a wall, a moment where you thought, I wish this could just go find the latest information for me,

1592
02:28:44,590 --> 02:28:50,884
或者我想把它变成视觉化的内容，或者我不想在任务的每一个步骤中都去引导它。
or I wish I could see this as a visual, or I wish I didn't have to guide it step by step through every part of this task.

1593
02:28:52,142 --> 02:28:54,916
事实是：这些功能确实存在。
Here's the thing: those capabilities exist.

1594
02:28:56,014 --> 02:28:58,308
它们现在就内置在 ChatGPT 中。
They are built into ChatGPT right now.

1595
02:28:58,798 --> 02:29:00,708
只是大多数人不知道它们在那儿。
Most people just don't know they are there.

1596
02:29:01,518 --> 02:29:02,852
或者不知道如何开启它们。
Or how to turn them on.

1597
02:29:04,014 --> 02:29:12,388
现在我们要介绍三个工具，它们能让 Chat GPT 从一个文本助手变成功能强大得多的工具。
Now we are going to walk through three tools that transform Chat GPT from a text assistant into something significantly more powerful.

1598
02:29:13,294 --> 02:29:18,436
第一个是深度研究，当你需要真正的当前多源情报时使用。
The first one is the deep research for when you need true current multi-source intelligence.

1599
02:29:18,894 --> 02:29:29,476
创建图像是当你需要看到一个想法而不仅仅是阅读它时使用的；我们还有智能体模式，当你想要交给一个目标并让 AI 去搞定这些步骤时使用。
Create image for when you need to see an idea, not just read about it, and we also have agent mode when you want to hand over a goal and let AI figure out these steps.

1600
02:29:30,670 --> 02:29:37,988
到本节结束时，你将清楚地知道每个工具的功能、使用时机以及如何逐步开始。
By the end of this session, you will know exactly what each tool does, when to use it, and how to get started step by step.

1601
02:29:38,702 --> 02:29:41,156
现在让我们深入了解每一个工具。
Let's dive deeper into each of these tools now.

1602
02:29:42,574 --> 02:29:44,164
第一个工具是深度研究。
The first tool is deep research.

1603
02:29:44,686 --> 02:29:45,284
它是什么？
What is it?

1604
02:29:45,774 --> 02:29:46,692
它为什么重要？
Why does it matter?

1605
02:29:47,726 --> 02:29:49,188
让我们从一个场景开始。
Let's start with a scenario.

1606
02:29:49,614 --> 02:29:57,728
你想了解欧盟的新 AI 法规与美国、英国，
You want to understand how the European Union's new AI regulations compare with what's happening in the United States, the United Kingdom,

1607
02:29:58,030 --> 02:29:59,620
以及世界其他国家的动态相比如何。
and other countries around the world.

1608
02:30:00,014 --> 02:30:09,220
这是一个变化迅速的话题，政策在不断更新，你需要一个清晰且结构良好的答案，而不仅仅是一个表面化的段落。
It's a fast-changing topic, politics are being updated regularly, and you need a clear, well-structured answer, not just a surface-level paragraph.

1609
02:30:10,126 --> 02:30:16,548
如果你在标准的 Chat GPT 会话中输入这个问题，你会得到一个基于模型所学内容的回答。
If you type that into a standard Chat GPT session, you will get a response based on what the model learned.

1610
02:30:17,934 --> 02:30:24,804
在这些训练过程中，信息可能已经过时好几个月了，它无法反映上周发布的政策公告，
During this training, the information might be several months old, it won't reflect last week's policy announcement,

1611
02:30:25,102 --> 02:30:31,332
而且它通常只从单一的推理逻辑中提取内容，而不是跨多个当前来源进行对比。
and it will typically draw from a single thread of reasoning rather than comparing across multiple current sources.

1612
02:30:32,622 --> 02:30:34,852
深度研究完全改变了这一点。
Deep research changes that entirely.

1613
02:30:35,726 --> 02:30:39,972
这是 ChatGPTS 高级网络智能功能中的深度研究。
Deep research in ChatGPTS Advanced Web Intelligence feature.

1614
02:30:40,590 --> 02:30:50,448
它不再仅仅依赖于训练数据，而是主动去互联网上搜索，按顺序进行多次搜索，从多个来源获取信息，
Instead of relying only on its training data, it actively goes out to the Internet, runs multiple searches in sequence, pulls information from several sources,

1615
02:30:50,768 --> 02:30:56,388
分析找到的内容，然后将所有内容综合成一个全面的结构化回复。
analyzes what it finds, and then synthesizes everything into a comprehensive structured response.

1616
02:30:57,486 --> 02:30:58,884
你可以这样理解两者的区别。
Think of the difference like this.

1617
02:30:59,758 --> 02:31:08,100
标准的 Chat GPT 回答就像是问一个博学的同事问题，他凭直觉给出的最佳回答。
A standard Chat GPT reply is like asking a knowledgeable colleague a question and getting their best answer off the top of their head.

1618
02:31:09,070 --> 02:31:18,020
深度研究就像是让同一个同事离开几分钟，去读四到五篇关于该主题的最新文章，进行交叉比对，
Deep research is like asking that same colleague to go away for a few minutes, read four to five recent articles on the topic, cross-reference them,

1619
02:31:18,286 --> 02:31:20,836
然后带着一份结构合理的简报回来。
and come back with the properly structured briefing.

1620
02:31:21,838 --> 02:31:29,700
第二个答案需要稍微长一点时间，但信息的质量、深度和准确性完全不在一个层级。
The second answer takes a little longer, but the quality, depth, and accuracy of information are in a completely different league.

1621
02:31:30,414 --> 02:31:34,404
这使得深度研究在学术工作中特别有价值。
That makes deep research particularly valuable for academic work.

1622
02:31:34,798 --> 02:31:38,660
当你需要多个视角和最新资料来研究某个主题时，
Researching a topic where you need multiple perspectives and recent sources,

1623
02:31:39,438 --> 02:31:48,260
无论是做出专业决策、了解市场趋势、监管变化、竞争格局，还是在快速发展的领域中，
professional decisions, understanding market trends, regulatory changes, competitor landscapes, fast-moving fields,

1624
02:31:48,688 --> 02:31:55,844
比如技术、科学、全球新闻，这些领域六个月前的情况可能就已经过时了。
technology, science, global news, where what was true six months ago may already be outdated.

1625
02:31:56,462 --> 02:32:03,172
当你需要并排评估不同选项、框架或立场时，可以进行对比分析。
Comparative analysis when you need to evaluate options, frameworks, or positions side by side.

1626
02:32:03,662 --> 02:32:05,284
接下来是逐步操作指南。
How to use it step by step.

1627
02:32:05,806 --> 02:32:07,844
第一步是启用该功能。
The first step is to enable the feature.

1628
02:32:08,302 --> 02:32:16,484
前往设置中的工具，确保已开启深度研究。除非启用，否则它不会出现在你的对话选项中。
Go to the settings, tools, and make sure deep research is turned on. It won't appear as an option in your chat unless it's enabled.

1629
02:32:17,262 --> 02:32:20,164
第二步，提出一个有实质内容的提问。
Step two, ask a substantive question.

1630
02:32:20,782 --> 02:32:24,676
当你提供一个具有一定深度的提问时，深度研究的效果最好。
Deep research works best when you give it a question with some depth to it.

1631
02:32:25,134 --> 02:32:35,268
不要只问“什么是人工智能”，而是问类似“2025年欧盟的AI法规与美国、英国及全球的AI治理框架相比如何”。
Not just what is AI, but something like how do EU AI regulations in 2025 compare with US, UK, and global AI governance frameworks.

1632
02:32:36,366 --> 02:32:41,444
你的问题越具体、层次越丰富，深度研究提供的价值就越高。
The more specific and layered your question is, the more value deep research delivers.

1633
02:32:42,830 --> 02:32:43,556
第三步。
Step 3.

1634
02:32:44,014 --> 02:32:44,804
让它开始运行。
Let it work.

1635
02:32:45,966 --> 02:32:52,004
Chat GPT 将开始搜索、交叉引用多个来源并构建回复内容。
Chat GPT will begin searching, cross-referencing multiple sources, and building its response.

1636
02:32:52,846 --> 02:32:56,164
你通常可以看到它在实时处理这些过程。
You will often see it working through the process in real time.

1637
02:32:56,942 --> 02:33:00,740
这比标准回复耗时更长，这是正常的。
This takes longer than a standard reply, and that's expected.

1638
02:33:01,134 --> 02:33:03,108
因为它正在执行大量的额外工作。
It's doing significantly more work.

1639
02:33:04,142 --> 02:33:07,684
接下来是第四步，查看你的综合报告。
Then is your step four, review your synthesized report.

1640
02:33:08,206 --> 02:33:10,180
输出的内容不会只是一个段落。
The output won't just be a paragraph.

1641
02:33:10,670 --> 02:33:21,380
它通常是一个包含上下文、对比和有来源支持的见解的多章节结构化回复，这种内容如果手动整理会耗费大量时间。
It will typically be a structured multi-section response with context, comparisons, and sourced insights, the kind of output that would take you significant time to compile manually.

1642
02:33:22,030 --> 02:33:23,044
需要注意什么？
What to keep in mind?

1643
02:33:23,406 --> 02:33:25,700
它需要 Plus 计划或更高等级的订阅。
It requires a plus plan or higher.

1644
02:33:26,894 --> 02:33:29,508
免费试用版不提供深度研究功能。
Deep research is not available on the free trial.

1645
02:33:30,350 --> 02:33:34,020
一些高级研究能力可能仅限于企业账户。
Some advanced research capabilities may be limited to enterprise accounts.

1646
02:33:34,990 --> 02:33:36,548
请检查当前的计划详情。
Check the current plan details.

1647
02:33:37,454 --> 02:33:43,492
深度研究的可用性及其包含的计划会随时间变化并不断演进。
Deep research availability and the plans it's included in have changed over time and continue to evolve.

1648
02:33:44,750 --> 02:33:51,140
在录制时，付费计划可使用该功能，但 OpenAI 会定期更新这些政策。
At the time of recording, access was available on paid plans, but OpenAI updates these policies regularly.

1649
02:33:51,918 --> 02:34:02,468
在确定你是否拥有权限之前，请在 Chat GPT 界面的设置工具中查看，或访问 OpenAI 的当前计划对比页面以获取最准确的信息。
Before assuming you do or don't have access, check settings tools in your Chat GPT interface or visit OpenAI's current plan comparison page for the most accurate information.

1650
02:34:03,246 --> 02:34:06,244
不要仅依赖你在课程或文章中看到的内容。
Don't rely solely on what you see in a course or article.

1651
02:34:07,150 --> 02:34:09,220
计划功能可以让你更快地操作。
Plan features is the space more quickly.

1652
02:34:09,582 --> 02:34:13,700
它的设计逻辑是更慢一些，但它是在实时搜索和分析。
It's slower by design, but it's searching and analyzing in real time.

1653
02:34:14,478 --> 02:34:16,964
它的回复时间比普通回复要长。
Responses take longer than a regular reply.

1654
02:34:17,486 --> 02:34:19,172
这是正常且符合预期的。
This is normal and expected.

1655
02:34:19,566 --> 02:34:21,668
它无法访问需要付费订阅的内容。
It cannot access paywalled content.

1656
02:34:22,222 --> 02:34:27,236
如果某个来源需要订阅才能阅读，深度研究就无法突破那个限制。
If a source requires a subscription to read, deep research can't get behind that wall.

1657
02:34:27,694 --> 02:34:30,244
它只能处理公开可用的信息。
It works with publicly available information.

1658
02:34:30,862 --> 02:34:38,660
在摘要中，你会得到综合后的见解和转述的内容，而不是从文章中直接提取的原文。
In summaries rather than quotes, you will get synthesized insights and paraphrased content, not verbatim extracts from articles.

1659
02:34:39,246 --> 02:34:47,428
这既是一个功能——因为它整合了信息而非仅仅复制，也是一个需要注意的限制，当你需要直接引用时。
This is both a feature because it integrates information rather than just copying it, and a limitation to be aware of when you need direct citations.

1660
02:34:48,654 --> 02:34:50,416
第二个工具是“创建图像”。
Tool two is create image.

1661
02:34:50,830 --> 02:34:52,580
它是什么？为什么它很重要？
What is it and why does it matter?

1662
02:34:53,326 --> 02:34:55,364
让我们思考一个常见的烦恼。
Let's think about a common frustration.

1663
02:34:56,046 --> 02:35:05,188
你有一个想法，也许是你想在演示中解释的一个概念，一个故事中的角色，或者是一个培训模型的视觉比喻，
You have an idea, maybe it's a concept you are trying to explain in a presentation, a character for a story, a visual metaphor for a training model,

1664
02:35:05,582 --> 02:35:09,540
或者是你在投入设计工作前想要草绘出的产品概念。
a product concept you want to sketch out before investing or design work.

1665
02:35:10,350 --> 02:35:12,548
在过去，你只有两个选择。
In the past, you had two options.

1666
02:35:13,102 --> 02:35:18,564
要么你有足够的技能自己去制作它，要么你就得等别人帮你做。
Either you had the design skills to build it yourself, or you waited for someone else to build it for you.

1667
02:35:19,342 --> 02:35:23,812
无论哪种情况，从产生想法到看到成品之间都有隔阂。
Either way, there was friction between having the idea and seeing the idea.

1668
02:35:24,430 --> 02:35:27,204
“创建图像”完全消除了这种隔阂。
Create image removes that friction entirely.

1669
02:35:27,982 --> 02:35:37,296
“创建图像”是 ChatGPT 内置的视觉生成功能，目前由 OpenAI 的图像生成模型 DAL E3 提供支持。
Create image in Chat GPT's built-in visual generation feature, currently powered by DAL E3, OpenAI's image generation model.

1670
02:35:37,870 --> 02:35:45,668
它允许你用通俗易懂的语言描述你想要的内容，并在几秒钟内直接在聊天窗口中获得高分辨率图像。
It allows you to describe what you want in plain language and receive a high-resolution image directly in your chat window in seconds.

1671
02:35:46,318 --> 02:35:52,900
不需要 Photoshop，不需要设计培训，不需要等待设计师，只需要描述就能得到结果。
No Photoshop, no design training, no waiting for a designer, just a description and a result.

1672
02:35:53,838 --> 02:35:57,892
这就是它对学习者和专业人士都非常有用的原因。
Here's what makes it genuinely powerful for learners and professionals alike.

1673
02:35:58,670 --> 02:36:01,636
当你能看到一个想法时，你的理解方式会完全不同。
When you can see an idea, you understand it differently.

1674
02:36:02,446 --> 02:36:07,844
一个流程图比三段描述相同流程的文字更容易理解。
A flow chart of a process is easier to grasp than three paragraphs describing the same process.

1675
02:36:08,686 --> 02:36:14,148
数据的视觉呈现比单纯的文字更能留在你的记忆中。
A visual representation of the data concept sticks in your memory better than text alone.

1676
02:36:15,086 --> 02:36:22,340
“创建图像”意味着你可以在需要的那一刻就生成那个视觉效果，而不是在提交设计请求几天后才拿到。
Create image means you can generate that visual the moment you need it, not days later after a design request has been processed.

1677
02:36:22,766 --> 02:36:30,692
你可以为教学内容生成图表和流程图，为演示文稿生成写实图像，或者制作模型图，
You can generate diagrams and flowcharts for educational content, photorealistic images for presentations, or mock-ups,

1678
02:36:31,040 --> 02:36:39,620
为讲故事或互动提供插画和漫画、风格化的艺术作品、水彩画、油画、赛博朋克风格，
illustrations, and cartoons for storytelling or engagement, stylized artwork, watercolor, oil painting, cyberpunk,

1679
02:36:39,920 --> 02:36:42,788
极简主义，以及更多产品概念的视觉效果。
minimalist, and more product concept visuals.

1680
02:36:43,118 --> 02:36:45,188
这些都是在任何正式设计工作开始之前就能完成的。
before any real design work begins.

1681
02:36:45,902 --> 02:36:49,316
数字内容的缩略图、横幅和封面艺术。
Thumbnails, banners, and cover art for digital content.

1682
02:36:49,742 --> 02:36:50,532
如何使用它。
How to use it.

1683
02:36:50,958 --> 02:36:52,580
我们将循序渐进地学习。
We will learn step by step.

1684
02:36:53,390 --> 02:36:56,228
第一步，开启图像生成功能。
Step one, enable image generation.

1685
02:36:56,686 --> 02:37:00,644
进入工具中的设置，并打开图像生成。
Go to Settings in the Tools and turn on Image Generation.

1686
02:37:01,198 --> 02:37:03,812
这将把图像模型连接到你的对话界面。
This connects the image model to your chat interface.

1687
02:37:04,526 --> 02:37:06,980
第二步，写一段描述性的提示词。
Step two, write a descriptive prompt.

1688
02:37:07,566 --> 02:37:11,428
输出内容的质量直接取决于你描述的质量。
The quality of your output is directly connected to the quality of your description.

1689
02:37:12,206 --> 02:37:13,316
要求越具体越好。
Be very specific.

1690
02:37:13,934 --> 02:37:21,796
与其只是“生成一张水循环图”，不如尝试“创建一个清晰的教育性水循环流程图”。
Instead of creating an image of the water cycle, try it like create a clear educational flowchart diagram of the water cycle

1691
02:37:22,094 --> 02:37:31,908
展示蒸发、凝结、降水和汇集，并带有标签、柔和的蓝色调以及简洁的信息图表风格。
showing evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection with labels, soft blue tones, and a clean infographic style.

1692
02:37:32,686 --> 02:37:41,444
你提供的关于风格、颜色、氛围、构图和用途的细节越多，结果就越符合你的预期。
The more detail you give about style, colors, mood, composition, and purpose, the closer the result will be to what you had in mind.

1693
02:37:42,414 --> 02:37:43,108
第三步。
Step 3.

1694
02:37:43,790 --> 02:37:45,092
检查并优化。
Review and refine.

1695
02:37:46,030 --> 02:37:49,316
Chat GPT 会直接在对话中生成图像。
Chat GPT generates the image directly in your chat.

1696
02:37:50,062 --> 02:37:52,068
点击放大以查看全图。
Click to enlarge it for a full view.

1697
02:37:52,846 --> 02:37:55,908
如果效果不理想，你不需要从头开始。
If it's not quite right, you don't have to start from scratch.

1698
02:37:56,974 --> 02:38:04,580
只需描述你想修改的地方，比如让它更亮一点、在顶部加个标题，或者把风格改为手绘插画。
Just describe what you would like to be changed, make it brighter, add a title at the top, change the style to a hand-drawn illustration.

1699
02:38:05,038 --> 02:38:07,364
模型会根据你的反馈重新生成。
The model will regenerate based on your feedback.

1700
02:38:07,822 --> 02:38:12,196
第四步，满意结果后下载或使用。
Step four, download or use once you are happy with the result.

1701
02:38:12,686 --> 02:38:15,620
直接下载并把它用到任何需要的地方。
Download it directly and use it wherever you need it.

1702
02:38:16,430 --> 02:38:17,828
接下来是智能体模式。
Next is agent mode.

1703
02:38:18,190 --> 02:38:20,068
它是什么，为什么重要？
What is it and why does it matter?

1704
02:38:20,622 --> 02:38:25,156
到目前为止，我们在这个环节讨论的所有内容都遵循同样的模式。
So far, everything we have talked about in this session has followed the same pattern.

1705
02:38:25,550 --> 02:38:29,860
你向 Chat GPT 发问，你提问，然后 ChatGPT 回答。
You ask Chat GPT, you ask, and then ChatGPT answers.

1706
02:38:30,318 --> 02:38:34,564
你引导每一个步骤，它响应每一次输入，并等待下一次指令。
You guide every step, it responds to each input, and waits for the next.

1707
02:38:35,406 --> 02:38:39,844
这是一个强大的工作流，但它仍然把规划的负担压在你身上。
That's a powerful workflow, but it still puts the burden of planning on you.

1708
02:38:40,590 --> 02:38:44,868
你必须知道要按什么顺序提问才能得到想要的结果。
You have to know what question to ask in what order to get to the outcome you want.

1709
02:38:45,998 --> 02:38:47,940
智能体模式完全改变了这一点。
Agent Mode flips that entirely.

1710
02:38:48,622 --> 02:38:57,572
智能体模式不是一步步回答你的问题，而是允许你给 Chat GPT 一个目标，然后看着它自己去规划步骤。
Instead of answering your question step by step, agent mode allows you to give Chat GPT a goal and then watches it figure out the steps on its own.

1711
02:38:58,542 --> 02:39:00,836
下面举一个具体的例子，让这个概念更直观点。
Here's a concrete example to make this real.

1712
02:39:01,390 --> 02:39:05,604
在没有智能体模式时，你会问：有哪些性价比高的手机？
Without agent mode, you ask, what are some good budget smartphones?

1713
02:39:06,542 --> 02:39:07,460
它会给你列出一份清单。
It gives you a list.

1714
02:39:08,270 --> 02:39:12,260
然后你再问：对比一下这三款在续航和拍照方面的表现。
Then you ask, compare the top three on battery life and camera.

1715
02:39:13,070 --> 02:39:14,052
它会进行对比。
It compares them.

1716
02:39:14,766 --> 02:39:17,124
接着你再问：现在把这些内容做成表格。
Then you ask, now put it in a table.

