2063
03:08:45,486 --> 03:08:52,324
他们的使命是构建安全、可理解且对人们真正有用的 AI 系统。
Their mission is to build AI systems that are safe, understandable, and genuinely useful to people.

2064
03:08:52,974 --> 03:08:55,456
他们旗舰的 AI 被称为 Claude。
Their flagship AI is called Claude.

2065
03:08:55,822 --> 03:09:01,124
如果你以前用过 Claude，你就知道它是一个强大的对话式 AI。
And if you have used Claude before, you know it's a powerful conversational AI.

2066
03:09:01,550 --> 03:09:04,580
但 Anthropic 不仅仅满足于一个聊天界面。
But Anthropic didn't stop at just a chat interface.

2067
03:09:05,198 --> 03:09:09,604
他们一直在观察人们在现实世界中如何实际使用他们的工具。
They kept watching how people were actually using their tools in the real world.

2068
03:09:09,998 --> 03:09:12,164
这导致了一些有趣的事情。
And that led to something interesting.

2069
03:09:12,686 --> 03:09:14,852
也就是 Claude Co-Work 出生的时刻。
The moment Claude Cowork was born.

2070
03:09:15,310 --> 03:09:18,468
这是来自 Anthropic 一个引人入胜的内部故事。
Here's a fascinating internal story from Anthropic.

2071
03:09:18,736 --> 03:09:27,812
在公司内部，市场团队和数据团队等非技术团队开始完全跳过 Claude 的常规聊天界面。
Inside the company, non-technical teams like the marketing team and the data team started skipping Claude's regular chat interface entirely.

2072
03:09:28,336 --> 03:09:34,596
相反，他们正在使用 Claude Code，这通常是一个从终端运行的开发者工具。
Instead, they were using Claude Code, which is normally a developer tool ranked from a terminal.

2073
03:09:35,136 --> 03:09:35,776
为什么？
Why?

2074
03:09:36,302 --> 03:09:47,140
因为 Claude Code 可以处理复杂的多步骤工作，比如构建内部工具或从文件中挖掘数据，而不需要用户一步步去引导它。
Because Cloud Code could handle complex multi-step work, things like building internal tools or mining data from files without the user having to guide it step by step.

2075
03:09:47,598 --> 03:09:51,716
Anthropic 注意到在公司外部也出现了同样的模式。
Anthropic noticed the same pattern happening outside the company too.

2076
03:09:52,334 --> 03:09:58,148
普通的专业人士也在尝试使用开发者工具，只为了获得更强大的 AI 辅助。
Regular professionals were trying to use developer tools just to get more powerful AI assistance.

2077
03:09:58,798 --> 03:10:02,148
就在那一刻，Anthropic 意识到这里存在一个缺口。
That's the moment Anthropic realized there's a gap here.

2078
03:10:02,606 --> 03:10:07,300
非开发人员仍然需要 Claude Code 所提供的同等强大的能力。
People who aren't developers still need the same power that Cloud Code offers.

2079
03:10:07,758 --> 03:10:09,732
他们只是需要一个更友好的包装。
They just need it in a friendlier package.

2080
03:10:10,030 --> 03:10:12,260
于是，Claude Co-Work 就诞生了。
And so Cloud Co-Work was born.

2081
03:10:13,070 --> 03:10:16,452
Claude Co-Work 并不是作为另一个 AI 产品而构建的。
Cloud CoWork wasn't built as just another AI product.

2082
03:10:16,816 --> 03:10:26,340
它是为了满足分析师、研究人员、运营团队和财务专业人士等真实用户的需求而构建的，他们都想做比聊天更多的事情。
It was built because real users like analysts, researchers, operations team, finance professionals were all trying to do more than chat.

2083
03:10:26,830 --> 03:10:32,580
他们有实际的工作需要移交，并且需要一个能够接手并完成这些工作的工具。
They had actual work to hand off, and they needed a tool that could take the work and finish it.

2084
03:10:33,134 --> 03:10:35,492
这正是 Claude Co-Work 所做的。
That's exactly what Cloud CoWork does.

2085
03:10:36,174 --> 03:10:39,460
好了，现在你知道为什么会有 Claude Co-Work 了。
Alright, so now you know why Cloud Cowork exists.

2086
03:10:39,822 --> 03:10:41,508
让我们来聊聊它到底是什么。
Let's talk about what it is.

2087
03:10:42,190 --> 03:10:46,980
Claude Co-Work 是 Anthropic 为知识型工作构建的智能体 AI 系统。
Cloud CoWork is Anthropic's agentic AI system built for knowledge work.

2088
03:10:47,438 --> 03:10:52,388
用通俗的话说，你给它一个目标，它会自己找到达成目标的方法。
In plain English, you give it a goal and it figures out how to get there on its own.

2089
03:10:53,006 --> 03:11:00,356
它能与你授权访问的本地文件和文件夹协同工作，从头到尾完成多步骤任务。
It works with local files and folders you allow access to, completing multi-step tasks from start to finish.

2090
03:11:00,846 --> 03:11:05,220
你定义结果，Claude Co-Work 则无缝处理整个过程。
You define the outcome and Claude Co-Work handles the process seamlessly.

2091
03:11:05,550 --> 03:11:07,652
它与普通聊天有什么不同？
How is it different from regular chat?

2092
03:11:08,206 --> 03:11:11,556
在普通的 Claude Chat 中，你和 Claude 是来回互动。
In regular Claude Chat, you and Claude go back and forth.

2093
03:11:11,950 --> 03:11:14,212
你输入一个问题，Claude 给出一个回答。
You type a question, Claude answers.

2094
03:11:14,606 --> 03:11:19,940
你再输入一个问题，Claude 无法进入你的文件或在你的电脑上执行操作。
You type another question, Claude can't reach into your files or do things on your computer.

2095
03:11:20,622 --> 03:11:26,852
在 Claude Co-Work 中，Claude 获得权限去读取、编辑或创建你在文件夹中选择的文件。
In Claude CoWork, Claude gets permission to read, edit, or create files in folders you choose.

2096
03:11:27,374 --> 03:11:31,312
它不仅仅是告诉你如何做某事，而是真正帮你把事情做完。
It doesn't just tell you how to do something, it actually does it for you.

2097
03:11:31,726 --> 03:11:36,512
可以这样理解：普通聊天相当于让 Claude 作为你的顾问。
Think of it this way: a regular chat is equal to Claude as your advisor.

2098
03:11:36,846 --> 03:11:41,472
Claude Co-Work 则相当于让 Claude 作为能真正干活的同事。
Claude CoWork is equal to Claude as your colleague who actually does the work.

2099
03:11:41,742 --> 03:11:45,124
让我带你了解一下 Claude Co-Work 的核心功能。
Let me walk you through the standout features of Claude Co-Work.

2100
03:11:45,472 --> 03:11:47,140
基于目标的执行。
Goal-based execution.

2101
03:11:47,502 --> 03:11:55,492
你不需要把任务拆分成步骤。你只需描述你的需求，比如“分析这个包含支出文件的文件夹并给我一份总结报告”。
You don't break the task into steps. You just describe what you want, like analyze this folder of expense files and give me a summary report.

2102
03:11:56,142 --> 03:11:58,756
而 Claude Co-Work 会自动推导出执行步骤。
And Claude CoWork figures out the steps itself.

2103
03:11:59,246 --> 03:12:01,028
接下来是本地文件访问。
Then local file access.

2104
03:12:01,550 --> 03:12:04,932
Claude 可以访问你授权给它的文件和文件夹。
Claude can access files and folders you give it permission to use.

2105
03:12:05,326 --> 03:12:12,836
它可以在你的电脑上读取文档、编辑电子表格、创建新文件、整理文件夹等操作。
It can read documents, edit spreadsheets, create new files, sort folders, and more, all on your actual computer.

2106
03:12:13,294 --> 03:12:14,912
多步骤任务处理。
Multi-step task handling.

2107
03:12:15,470 --> 03:12:18,352
Claude Co-Work 不仅仅是回答一次就停止了。
Cloud Co-Work doesn't just answer once and stop.

2108
03:12:18,798 --> 03:12:25,092
它会将复杂的工作分解成子任务，按顺序执行，并交付最终的成果。
It breaks complex work into subtasks, runs them in a sequence, and delivers a finished deliverable.

2109
03:12:25,518 --> 03:12:26,660
人工监管。
Human Oversight.

2110
03:12:26,990 --> 03:12:29,828
Claude Co-Work 在开始之前会向你展示它的计划。
Cloud CoWork shows you its plan before it starts.

2111
03:12:30,158 --> 03:12:31,072
由你来确认通过。
You approve it.

2112
03:12:31,406 --> 03:12:35,712
你可以实时查看执行步骤，也可以先离开去处理其他研究，稍后再回来查看。
You can watch the steps in real time or walk away and come back to research.

2113
03:12:36,046 --> 03:12:38,244
重大决策始终掌握在你手中。
You stay in control of the big decisions.

2114
03:12:38,592 --> 03:12:40,452
连接器与集成。
Connectors and integrations.

2115
03:12:41,006 --> 03:12:48,068
Claude Co-Work 可以通过连接器目录连接 Google Drive、Chrome 等多种外部工具。
Cloud CoWork can connect to external tools like Google Drive, Chrome, and many more through the connector catalog.

2116
03:12:48,526 --> 03:12:55,364
当没有直接连接器可用时，Claude Co-Work 甚至可以控制你的屏幕，像人类一样操作各种应用。
When a direct connector isn't available, Cloud CoWork can even control your screen to navigate apps like a human would.

2117
03:12:55,822 --> 03:12:56,592
定时任务。
Scheduling.

2118
03:12:56,878 --> 03:13:01,156
你可以设置任务自动运行，可以是周期性执行或按需执行。
You can schedule tasks to run automatically, recurring or on demand.

2119
03:13:01,518 --> 03:13:05,124
只需在任务中输入 /schedule 即可进行设置。
Just type /schedule inside a task to set it up.

2120
03:13:05,472 --> 03:13:06,148
项目管理。
Projects.

2121
03:13:06,542 --> 03:13:13,476
你可以将相关的任务归类到项目中，拥有独立的文件夹、指令和记忆的独立工作区。
You can group related tasks into projects, separate workspaces with their own files, instructions, and memory.

2122
03:13:13,870 --> 03:13:17,540
通过与桌面端配对的 Claude 移动端应用实现移动访问。
Mobile access with the Claude Mobile app paired to your desktop.

2123
03:13:17,998 --> 03:13:20,100
你可以从手机上分配任务。
You can assign tasks from your phone.

2124
03:13:20,590 --> 03:13:22,276
Claude 会在你的电脑上执行工作。
Claude works on your desktop.

2125
03:13:22,574 --> 03:13:24,592
你不需要一直坐在电脑前盯着它。
You just don't have to be sitting in front of it.

2126
03:13:24,942 --> 03:13:26,512
谁适合使用 Claude Co-Work？
Who is Claude Co-Work for?

2127
03:13:26,766 --> 03:13:32,036
Claude Co-Work 专为日常工作涉及文档、数据和文件的任何人设计。
Claude Co-Work is designed for anyone whose workday involves documents, data, and files.

2128
03:13:32,558 --> 03:13:34,020
但它不只是给开发人员用的。
But who is it a developer?

2129
03:13:34,638 --> 03:13:44,804
研究人员、分析师、运营团队、法律专业人士、财务团队、营销团队，任何处理耗时任务的人员。
Researchers, analysts, operations team, legal professionals, finance team, marketing team, anyone who spends time on tasks that are time consuming

2130
03:13:45,072 --> 03:13:46,756
这些任务通常不涉及复杂的底层技术。
but not technically complex.

2131
03:13:47,374 --> 03:13:49,316
Claude 是为你量身定制的。
Claude Co-Work is built for you.

2132
03:13:49,966 --> 03:13:57,252
到现在，你已经知道如何把任务交给 Co-Work、安排计划、连接外部工具并确保安全了。
By now you know how to delegate tasks to co-work, schedule them, connect external tools, and keep it all secure.

2133
03:13:57,774 --> 03:13:59,236
基础机制已经就绪。
The mechanics are in place.

2134
03:13:59,872 --> 03:14:06,912
这一模块的区别在于，是仅仅使用 Co-Work，还是能从 Co-Work 中获得真正的杠杆效应。
This module is the difference between someone who uses cowork and someone who gets real leverage from cowork.

2135
03:14:07,342 --> 03:14:09,476
而这种区别并不取决于功能。
And that difference isn't a feature.

2136
03:14:09,838 --> 03:14:11,236
而是取决于一系列习惯。
It's a set of habits.

2137
03:14:12,046 --> 03:14:18,500
我将带你了解那些我看到屡屡奏效的习惯，以及那些经常让人们掉坑里的错误做法。
I'm going to walk you through the habits I see working every time and the ones I see tripping people up.

2138
03:14:18,990 --> 03:14:20,676
这是本节课的计划。
Here's the plan for this session.

2139
03:14:21,198 --> 03:14:23,140
我们先从最佳实践开始。
We'll start with best practices.

2140
03:14:23,502 --> 03:14:24,420
一共八个习惯。
Eight habits.

2141
03:14:24,974 --> 03:14:28,068
这些习惯都很具体、明确，且能立即应用。
Small, specific, immediately actionable.

2142
03:14:28,494 --> 03:14:31,876
这正是区分普通用户和高级用户的关键。
That separates casual users from power users.

2143
03:14:32,494 --> 03:14:34,404
接着我们将进入故障排除环节。
Then we'll move into troubleshooting.

2144
03:14:34,766 --> 03:14:38,212
Co-Work 任务失败最常见的五种情况。
The five most common ways cowork tasks fail.

2145
03:14:38,670 --> 03:14:41,604
每种情况的表现以及对应的精确解决方案。
What each one looks like and the exact fix.

2146
03:14:41,966 --> 03:14:48,324
此外，还有一个三步诊断法，可以解决你可能遇到的 80% 的问题。
Plus a three-step diagnostic approach that'll handle 80% of the issues you'll ever encounter.

2147
03:14:48,814 --> 03:14:54,852
最后，我们将通过回顾整个过程来结束本模块和整个课程。
And we'll close the module and the course by stepping back and putting the whole journey in perspective.

2148
03:14:55,374 --> 03:14:56,484
让我们开始吧。
Let's get into it.

2149
03:14:56,910 --> 03:14:58,592
让我们从基础知识开始。
Let's start with the foundation.

2150
03:14:58,894 --> 03:14:59,716
稳操胜券。
Have it won.

2151
03:15:00,192 --> 03:15:02,724
把你的提示词当成软件一样去投入。
Invest in your prompts like they are software.

2152
03:15:03,246 --> 03:15:04,676
你的提示词是资产。
Your prompts are assets.

2153
03:15:05,326 --> 03:15:14,692
在模块 2 中生成出那个出色安全摘要的 150 字任务简报，就是一个可重复使用的资产，前提是你得把它保存下来。
The 150 word brief that produced that great safe summary in Module 2 that's a reusable asset, but only if you save it.

2154
03:15:15,438 --> 03:15:19,076
我希望你做的是建立一个个人的提示词库。
What I want you to do is start a personal prompt library.

2155
03:15:19,534 --> 03:15:25,732
它可以是一个简单的记事文件、一个 Google 文档，或者一个存放 Markdown 文件的文件夹，随便怎么弄。
It can be a simple notes file, a Google Doc, a folder of markdown files, doesn't matter.

2156
03:15:26,222 --> 03:15:30,340
每当你写出一个产出效果很棒的提示词时，就把它存下来。
Every time you write a prompt that produced a great output, save it.

2157
03:15:30,734 --> 03:15:32,196
根据它的功能来给它贴标签。
Label it by what it does.

2158
03:15:32,878 --> 03:15:40,720
几周之后，你就会拥有一个包含 20 到 30 个提示词的库，你可以直接复制粘贴、稍作修改就能重复使用。
Over a few weeks, you'll have a library of 20 or 30 prompts you can copy-paste, lightly edit, and reuse.

2159
03:15:40,880 --> 03:15:44,612
大多数人每次都要从头开始重新输入同样的提示词。
Most people retype the same prompt from scratch every time.

2160
03:15:45,102 --> 03:15:50,244
他们浪费了五分钟去重写那些他们上周就已经完善好的指令。
They waste five minutes reinventing instructions they already perfected last week.

2161
03:15:50,670 --> 03:15:52,000
别成为那种人。
Don't be that person.

2162
03:15:52,558 --> 03:15:53,440
习惯 2。
Habit 2.

2163
03:15:53,680 --> 03:15:57,700
对于任何重复性的事情，优先选择项目而非单次任务。
Prefer projects over one-off tasks for anything recurring.

2164
03:15:58,286 --> 03:16:00,420
我们在第三模块讲过项目。
We covered projects in Module 3.

2165
03:16:00,878 --> 03:16:02,404
这是效率方面的考量。
Here's the efficiency angle.

2166
03:16:02,958 --> 03:16:05,476
在 Co-work 中，单个任务是无状态的。
A single task in co-work is stateless.

2167
03:16:05,998 --> 03:16:08,132
Cloud 下次不会记得它。
Cloud doesn't remember it next time.

2168
03:16:08,654 --> 03:16:16,720
这意味着每当你运行类似的操作时，你都要重新解释你的文件夹结构、语气和格式规则，
Which means every time you run something similar, you re-explain your folder structure, your tone, your formatting rules,

2169
03:16:16,960 --> 03:16:17,700
还有你的限制条件。
your constraints.

2170
03:16:18,510 --> 03:16:21,252
在项目里，你只需要写一次这些内容。
Inside a project, you write those things once.

2171
03:16:21,870 --> 03:16:24,548
之后每一个任务都会继承它们。
At every subsequent task inherits them.

2172
03:16:25,102 --> 03:16:30,340
我的经验法则是：如果一个任务我要运行超过三次，就把它放进项目里。
My rule of thumb: if I run a task more than three times, it goes in a project.

2173
03:16:30,958 --> 03:16:36,036
这样一来，随着项目积累了更多上下文，我的提示词就会变得越来越短。
That way, my prompts get shorter and shorter as the project accumulates context.

2174
03:16:36,750 --> 03:16:38,052
现在是习惯 3。
Now habit 3.

2175
03:16:38,400 --> 03:16:41,348
要清楚什么时候该用 Co-work，什么时候该用聊天。
Know when to use cowork and when to use chat.

2176
03:16:41,934 --> 03:16:44,548
并不是每个问题都需要一个 AI 员工。
Not every question needs an AI employee.

2177
03:16:45,006 --> 03:16:47,268
有些问题只需要快速回答。
Some questions just need a quick answer.

2178
03:16:47,790 --> 03:16:52,484
如果你问 Cloud 的问题是“我该如何用记录来处理邮件地址？
If you're asking Cloud a question, how do I use records for email addresses?

2179
03:16:53,006 --> 03:16:54,240
就留在聊天标签页里。
Stay in the chat tab.

2180
03:16:54,480 --> 03:16:55,396
这样更快。
It's faster.

2181
03:16:55,790 --> 03:16:58,212
而且更省你的使用配额。
It uses less of your usage allocation.

2182
03:16:58,606 --> 03:17:06,948
Co-work 在后台运行更多操作，属于计算密集型，这意味着如果你用它来处理简单的事情，会更快达到使用限制。
Cowork is doing more under the hood, so it's compute intensive, which means you'll hit usage limit faster if you use it for simple things.

2183
03:17:07,566 --> 03:17:15,428
当涉及文件操作、调用连接器、多步骤任务或定时工作流时，才使用 Co-work。
Use cowork when there's a file operation, a connector call, a multi-step task, or a scheduled workflow involved.

2184
03:17:16,014 --> 03:17:18,532
当你只是需要把想法说出来时，用聊天。
Use chat when you just need to think out loud.

2185
03:17:18,958 --> 03:17:25,124
仅凭这一项自律——知道选择哪个工具——就能显著节省你的使用配额。
This one discipline alone, knowing which tool to pick, will stretch your usage budget significantly.

2186
03:17:25,550 --> 03:17:26,480
习惯 4。
Habit 4.

2187
03:17:26,862 --> 03:17:29,200
将相关工作批量处理到同一个会话中。
Batch related work into single sessions.

2188
03:17:29,440 --> 03:17:31,172
这和上一点有关。
This is related to the last point.

2189
03:17:31,854 --> 03:17:40,800
如果你有三件事要做，而且都涉及相同的文件，比如你正在制定第二季度的营销计划，那就把它们全部放在一个 Co-work 会话中完成，
If you have got three things to do that all touch the same files, say you're working on your Q2 marketing plan, do them all in one cowork

2190
03:17:40,960 --> 03:17:43,332
而不是分成三个独立的会话。
session rather than three separate ones.

2191
03:17:44,014 --> 03:17:48,004
在同一个会话中，Claude 已经加载了上下文。
In a single session, Cloud already has the context loaded.

2192
03:17:48,462 --> 03:17:51,364
下一个任务不需要重新阅读所有内容。
The next task is not to reread everything.

2193
03:17:51,854 --> 03:17:54,244
产出更快、更便宜且质量更高。
Faster, cheaper, and better output.

2194
03:17:54,926 --> 03:17:58,692
只有在真正切换上下文时，才开始新的会话。
Only start a new session when you're genuinely switching context.

2195
03:17:59,406 --> 03:18:00,400
习惯 5。
Habit 5.

2196
03:18:00,654 --> 03:18:03,556
始终检查计划，千万不要跳过这一步。
Always review the plan, never skip it.

2197
03:18:04,080 --> 03:18:07,492
我知道我们在整个课程中已经多次强调过这一点了。
I know we have said this multiple times across the course.

2198
03:18:08,014 --> 03:18:12,068
我再次强调是因为这是一个极高杠杆的习惯。
I'm saying it again because it is a single highest leverage habit.

2199
03:18:12,782 --> 03:18:16,900
计划预览是 Claude 在明确告诉你它即将要做什么。
The plan preview is cloud telling you exactly what it's about to do.

2200
03:18:17,358 --> 03:18:21,156
每一次都要阅读，哪怕是简单的任务。
Read it every single time, even for simple tasks.

2201
03:18:21,774 --> 03:18:27,716
我听到的那些“Claude 做出了奇怪操作”的案例，90% 都在计划阶段就能被发现。
90% of the cloud did something weird stories I heard would have been caught at the plan stage.

2202
03:18:28,462 --> 03:18:32,080
花 10 秒钟阅读可以节省 30 分钟的清理工作。
10 seconds of reading saves you 30 minutes of cleanup.

2203
03:18:32,398 --> 03:18:33,316
习惯 6。
Habit 6.

2204
03:18:33,760 --> 03:18:37,092
在提示词中明确规定不确定时的行为。
Specify if unsure behavior in your prompts.

2205
03:18:37,902 --> 03:18:41,540
这里有一个能显著提升输出质量的小技巧。
Here's a small thing that dramatically improves output quality.

2206
03:18:42,222 --> 03:18:48,036
在任何可能需要 Claude 做判断的提示词中，都要告诉它在不确定时该怎么做。
In any prompt where cloud might have to make a judgment call, tell it what to do when it's uncertain.

2207
03:18:48,558 --> 03:18:54,148
例如，如果内容无法阅读，就留空金额并标记该行。
For example, if it's received as unreadable, leave the amount blank and flag the row.

2208
03:18:54,670 --> 03:19:00,356
如果你发现不同来源的信息有矛盾，同时展示两者，而不是制造冲突。
If you find contradictory information across sources, show both and not a contradiction.

2209
03:19:00,718 --> 03:19:01,668
不要只选其中一个。
Don't pick one.

2210
03:19:02,222 --> 03:19:08,132
Claude 在不确定时的默认行为是尽力而为，这有时意味着会产生幻觉。
Default cloud behavior when uncertain is to try its best, which sometimes means hallucinating.

2211
03:19:08,686 --> 03:19:13,920
你的“若不确定”条款能给它提供一个安全的后退选项，从而保证数据完整性。
Your if unsure clause gives it a safe fallback that preserves your data integrity.

2212
03:19:14,254 --> 03:19:15,120
习惯 7。
Habit 7.

2213
03:19:15,360 --> 03:19:19,044
把第一次输出视为草稿，而不是最终交付物。
Treat the first output as a draft, not a deliverable.

2214
03:19:19,662 --> 03:19:21,188
这是一种心态问题。
This is a mindset thing.

2215
03:19:21,774 --> 03:19:29,252
新手运行一次任务，看一眼结果，如果不是完美的，就会觉得 Co-work 不好用并放弃。
New users run a task once, look at the output, and if it's not perfect, they decide cowork doesn't work and give up.

2216
03:19:29,966 --> 03:19:40,068
经验丰富的用户运行一次任务，看一眼结果，然后立即跟进：让第二部分更长点，按重要程度重新排列类别，
Experienced users run a task once, look at the output, and immediately follow up with make section two longer, reorder the categories by importance,

2217
03:19:40,334 --> 03:19:43,140
在底部加个表格对比三个选项。
add a table at the bottom, comparing the three options.

2218
03:19:44,014 --> 03:19:46,340
Claude 在迭代中表现最佳。
Cloud is at its best in iteration.

2219
03:19:46,798 --> 03:19:48,772
第一次输出是初稿。
The first output is a rough cut.

2220
03:19:49,166 --> 03:19:52,964
在你反馈后的第二次输出才是真正的交付物。
The second output after your feedback is a real deliverable.

2221
03:19:53,582 --> 03:19:55,268
不要接受质量低下的输出。
Don't accept bad output.

2222
03:19:55,584 --> 03:19:56,164
进行修改。
Revise.

2223
03:19:56,654 --> 03:19:57,444
习惯 8。
Habit 8.

2224
03:19:57,744 --> 03:20:01,220
为了 Claude 的运行，也要保持文件夹整洁，而不只是为了你自己。
Keep your folders clean for cloud's sake, not just yours.

2225
03:20:01,966 --> 03:20:03,972
这里有一件大多数人没意识到的事情。
Here's something most people don't realize.

2226
03:20:04,366 --> 03:20:09,572
当你让 Claude 处理某个文件夹时，该文件夹的结构会影响输出的质量。
When you point cloud at a folder, the structure of that folder affects the quality of the output.

2227
03:20:10,030 --> 03:20:15,268
一个文件命名模糊且混乱的文件夹会让 Claude 更费力去判断里面是什么。
A messy folder with cryptic file names makes cloud work harder to figure out what's there.

2228
03:20:15,758 --> 03:20:21,060
一个组织良好、文件名描述清晰的文件夹能让 Claude 更快地给出准确结果。
A well-organized folder with descriptive file names lets cloud be accurate faster.

2229
03:20:21,550 --> 03:20:27,172
所以我们在第三模块中做的文件整理工作，不仅仅是为了让你省心。
So the file organization work we did in module 3, that's not just about your peace of mind.

2230
03:20:27,470 --> 03:20:30,692
这是为了给你的 AI 合作伙伴提供一个整洁的工作空间。
It's about giving your AI coworker a clean workspace.

2231
03:20:31,214 --> 03:20:34,084
AI 在整洁的工作空间里也能表现得更好。
They AI better work in clean workspaces too.

2232
03:20:34,702 --> 03:20:37,796
本节的最后一件事，监控你的使用情况。
Last thing for this section, monitor your usage.

2233
03:20:38,318 --> 03:20:42,660
Co-Work 任务比普通任务消耗更多的计划配额。
Cowork tasks consumes more of your plans allocation than regular tasks.

2234
03:20:43,150 --> 03:20:47,620
如果你打算大量依赖 Co-work，请定期检查你的使用设置。
If you're going to lean on cowork heavily, check your usage settings periodically.

2235
03:20:48,078 --> 03:20:49,636
看看你的标记都在去向何方。
See where your tokens are going.

2236
03:20:49,998 --> 03:20:52,772
如果你消耗得太快，请调整你的习惯。
Adjust your habits if you're burning through them too fast.

2237
03:20:52,944 --> 03:21:04,068
高效使用 Co-work 的目标不是尽可能多地使用它。而是将其用于能产生最大杠杆作用的任务，而将其他所有内容留在聊天中或手动处理。
The goal of efficient cowork usage isn't to use it as much as possible. It's to use it on the task where it produces the most leverage and to leave everything else in chat or do it manually.

2238
03:21:04,878 --> 03:21:07,748
现在我们来谈谈当事情出错时该怎么做。
Now let's talk about what to do when things go wrong.

2239
03:21:08,334 --> 03:21:14,980
既然你已经安装了 Co-work，让我带你快速参观一下界面，让你知道每个功能具体在哪里。
Now that you have installed co-work, let me take you on a quick tour of the interface so you know where exactly everything lives.

2240
03:21:15,662 --> 03:21:18,628
在这一课中，我不会教你如何使用其中的任何功能。
I'm not going to teach you how to use anything in this lesson.

2241
03:21:18,990 --> 03:21:21,668
我们将在课程的其余部分详细讲解这些内容。
We'll do that in detail across the rest of our course.

2242
03:21:22,318 --> 03:21:28,740
这只是为了让我稍后说“点击计划”或“打开项目”时，你知道具体去哪里找。
This is just so that when I say click schedule or open a project later, you know exactly where to look.

2243
03:21:29,678 --> 03:21:31,364
这就是我们的 Claude 界面。
So this is our Claude interface.

2244
03:21:31,726 --> 03:21:36,708
在最顶部，你会看到三个选项卡：聊天、Co-work 和代码。
At the very top, you'll see three tabs, chat, cowork, and code.

2245
03:21:37,166 --> 03:21:42,404
这些是该应用中 Co-work 的三种模式，我们之前在模块中已经对比过了。
These are the three modes of cowork in this app, which we already compared earlier in the module.

2246
03:21:42,926 --> 03:21:47,588
我们将课程的剩余部分都在 CoWork 选项卡中进行，所以我点击 CoWork。
We are going to spend the rest of the course in the CoWork tab, so I'll click CoWork.

2247
03:21:48,334 --> 03:21:50,384
左侧是你的侧边栏。
So on the left side is your sidebar.

2248
03:21:50,638 --> 03:21:52,260
这是你的导航中心。
This is your navigation hub.

2249
03:21:52,718 --> 03:21:55,364
你在 Co-work 中做的所有操作都可以从这里进入。
Everything you do in co-work gets to it from here.

2250
03:21:55,758 --> 03:21:58,308
让我带你从上到下过一遍里面包含的内容。
Let me walk you through what's in it top to bottom.

2251
03:21:58,734 --> 03:22:01,284
顶部是新任务选项。
At the top you have new task option.

2252
03:22:01,614 --> 03:22:03,584
这是开始一个新任务的方法。
This is how you start a fresh task.

2253
03:22:03,886 --> 03:22:07,904
点击这里，描述你想完成的内容，Co-work 就会接手后续操作。
Click here, describe what you want done, and cowork takes it from there.

2254
03:22:08,064 --> 03:22:10,500
在整个课程中，我们会多次用到这个功能。
We'll do this many times throughout the course.

2255
03:22:11,598 --> 03:22:14,148
接下来是下方的项目选项。
Now below that you have projects option.

2256
03:22:14,894 --> 03:22:18,500
项目是用于持续工作的专用工作区。
Projects are dedicated workspaces for ongoing work.

2257
03:22:18,958 --> 03:22:24,228
每个项目都有自己的文件、指令和记忆。
Each one has its own files, its own instructions, and its own memory.

2258
03:22:24,750 --> 03:22:26,628
我们将在本模块中建立一个。
We'll build one in this module.

2259
03:22:27,630 --> 03:22:29,092
接下来是计划任务。
Next, scheduled.

2260
03:22:29,584 --> 03:22:33,284
这是显示你设置的所有周期性任务的地方。
This is where any recurring task you have set up shows up.

2261
03:22:33,742 --> 03:22:37,956
比如每日简报、周报，以及自动运行的任务。
Daily briefs, weekly reports, automations that run on their own.

2262
03:22:38,862 --> 03:22:40,612
然后是实时产出物。
Then live artifacts.

2263
03:22:41,070 --> 03:22:44,068
这是 Co-Work 生成交互式输出的地方。
This is where Cowork generates interactive outputs.

2264
03:22:44,590 --> 03:22:47,904
比如仪表板或动态文档都会显示在这里。
Things like dashboards or live documents show up here.

2265
03:22:48,206 --> 03:22:51,460
当我们进入更丰富的应用场景时，你会看到它的实际效果。
You'll see this in action when we get to richer use cases.

2266
03:22:52,174 --> 03:22:53,700
现在是派发选项。
Now dispatch option.

2267
03:22:54,094 --> 03:22:56,132
目前这个功能还在测试阶段。
Currently, this is in beta phase.

2268
03:22:56,654 --> 03:23:02,500
这是为了处理在你不在线时也能完成并反馈的任务。
This is for handling tasks off and getting them back even when you're not actively at the app.

2269
03:23:02,894 --> 03:23:04,580
我们稍后会简单提一下。
We'll touch on it briefly later.

2270
03:23:05,230 --> 03:23:07,492
然后是自定义选项。
And then we have customized option.

2271
03:23:07,950 --> 03:23:18,784
在这里你可以按照自己的习惯来设置 Co-work，比如全局指令、文件夹访问权限、连接器，以及所有影响 Co-Work
This is where you set up co-work the way you look at it, like global instructions, folder access, connectors, all the personal preferences that shape how cowork

2272
03:23:18,944 --> 03:23:19,684
为你服务的个人偏好。
works for you.

2273
03:23:20,206 --> 03:23:23,780
现在来看看主面板，也就是中间较大的区域。
Now let's look at the main panel, the bigger area in the middle.

2274
03:23:24,174 --> 03:23:26,372
这是实际工作发生的地方。
This is where the actual work happens.

2275
03:23:26,830 --> 03:23:30,180
目前你看到的是带有友好提示的空白状态。
Right now you're seeing the empty state with a friendly prompt.

2276
03:23:30,606 --> 03:23:32,388
注意一下列表之外的内容。
Let's note something off your list.

2277
03:23:32,974 --> 03:23:36,740
还有一个输入框，上面写着：今天我能帮你点什么？
And as an input box that says, How can I help you today?

2278
03:23:37,358 --> 03:23:39,264
这就是你输入任务的地方。
This is where you'll type your task.

2279
03:23:39,598 --> 03:23:42,628
你在这一写的内容就是 Co-work 处理的任务内容。
Whatever you write here is what co-work tasks on.

2280
03:23:43,022 --> 03:23:50,784
左侧的加号图标可以让你添加文件、图片、文档，或者任何需要 Co-work 查看的内容。
Now the plus icon on the left side lets you attach files, images, documents, whatever cowork needs to look at.

2281
03:23:51,214 --> 03:23:55,108
右边的麦克风可以让你用语音输入任务，而不是手动打字。
The microphone on the right lets you dictate the task instead of typing it.

2282
03:23:55,566 --> 03:23:58,532
在输入框下方，有三个快速控制选项。
Below the input, you have got three quick controls.

2283
03:23:59,054 --> 03:24:00,868
首先是“在项目中工作”。
First, work in a project.

2284
03:24:01,230 --> 03:24:03,024
这会设置任务的模式。
This sets the mode for the task.

2285
03:24:03,278 --> 03:24:05,380
右边是一个模型选择器。
And on the right, a model selector.

2286
03:24:05,742 --> 03:24:09,412
在这里你可以选择由哪个 Co-work 模型来处理任务。
This is where you can choose which cowork model handles the task.

2287
03:24:09,774 --> 03:24:15,904
这里有 OPIS 4.7、Sonnet 4.6 和 Haiku 4.5。
So you have OPIS 4.7, Sonnet 4.6, Haiku 4.5.

2288
03:24:16,366 --> 03:24:20,324
这里还有更多模型选项，比如 Opus 4.6。
And here you have more model options like Opus 4.6.

2289
03:24:20,878 --> 03:24:23,332
稍后我们会简单聊聊如何选择模型。
We'll talk briefly about model choices later.

2290
03:24:23,630 --> 03:24:28,836
让我给你们看看从提示工程到委派在实际操作中到底有什么区别。
Let me show you what the shift from prompting to delegating actually looks like in practice.

2291
03:24:29,518 --> 03:24:38,192
如果我在聊天标签页，输入“我该如何重命名下载文件夹中名为 AI Agents in 电子商务 的文件”时，
If I'm in the chat tab and I type how do I rename a file named AI Agents in e-commerce located in my downloads folders,

2292
03:24:38,510 --> 03:24:40,996
Claude 会给我提供一个分步骤的指南。
Claude will give me a step-by-step guide.

2293
03:24:41,550 --> 03:24:47,684
它会告诉我该点哪里或者如何写个简单的脚本，这很有用，但我还是得自己动手操作。
It will tell me where to click or how to write a quick script, which is helpful, but I still have to do the work.

2294
03:24:48,206 --> 03:24:55,792
现在，如果我切换到 Co-work 并说“重命名下载文件夹里的文件”，Claude 就不会解释怎么做。
Now, if I switch to co-work and I say rename the file in my downloads folder, Claude doesn't explain how.

2295
03:24:56,078 --> 03:24:57,312
Claude 直接就去做了。
Claude just does it.

2296
03:24:57,552 --> 03:24:59,364
现在我来做一个演示。
Now I'll show you a demo.

2297
03:24:59,758 --> 03:25:05,252
让我给你们看看从提示工程到委派在实际操作中到底有什么区别。
Now let me show you what the shift from prompting to delegating actually looks like in practice.

2298
03:25:05,934 --> 03:25:11,460
把聊天标签页和 Co-work 标签页并排打开，或者在它们之间切换。
So open the chat tab and co-work tab side by side or toggle between them.

2299
03:25:11,982 --> 03:25:18,372
我现在在聊天标签页，我的下载文件夹里有一个叫 AI Agents in 电子商务 的文件夹。
So I'm in my chat tab now and in my downloads I have a folder named AI Agents in e-commerce.

2300
03:25:18,862 --> 03:25:21,636
我想把这个文件夹重命名为 AI Agents。
I want to rename this folder to AI Agents.

2301
03:25:22,126 --> 03:25:30,404
所以在这里我输入：如何将下载文件夹中名为 AI Agents in 电子商务 的文件重命名为 AI Agents？
So here I'll type how do I rename a file titled AI Agents in e-commerce located in my downloads folder to AI Agents?

2302
03:25:30,958 --> 03:25:37,712
这就是我的输出结果。要重命名下载文件夹中的文件，步骤取决于你的操作系统。
So here is my output. So to rename a file in your downloads folder, the steps depend on your operating system.

2303
03:25:38,030 --> 03:25:41,028
这就是操作步骤，但我还是得自己动手去弄。
And here are the steps, but I still have to do the work.

2304
03:25:41,518 --> 03:25:43,232
现在我切换到 Co-work。
Now I'll switch to cowork.

2305
03:25:43,854 --> 03:25:49,540
这里我把“如何”这部分删掉，因为在这里我不需要问它怎么做。
Here I'll just delete the how do I part because here I won't ask how do I.

2306
03:25:49,872 --> 03:26:00,836
相反，我直接说“将下载文件夹中名为 AI Agents in 电子商务 的文件重命名为 AI Agents”，然后按回车。
Instead, I'll just say rename a file titled AI Agents in e-commerce located in my downloads folder to AI Agents and I'll click enter.

2307
03:26:01,262 --> 03:26:02,372
看看会发生什么。
Let's see what happens.

2308
03:26:03,022 --> 03:26:05,476
我目前还没有权限访问你的下载文件夹。
I don't have access to your downloads folder yet.

2309
03:26:05,774 --> 03:26:08,164
让我加载工具来请求访问权限。
Let me load the tool to request access.

2310
03:26:08,846 --> 03:26:14,180
这里我有拒绝或授予权限的控制权，所以我点击允许。
So here I have the control to deny or give access, so I'll click allow.

2311
03:26:14,734 --> 03:26:19,588
你看，电子商务中的 AI 智能体被重命名为 AI 智能体了。
See, renamed AI Agents in e-commerce is renamed to AI Agents.

2312
03:26:20,046 --> 03:26:20,964
让我们确认一下。
Let's confirm.

2313
03:26:21,358 --> 03:26:22,672
这就是我们之前的文件。
So this was our file.

2314
03:26:22,926 --> 03:26:25,284
现在它被重命名为 AI 智能体了。
Now it's renamed to AI Agents.

2315
03:26:25,742 --> 03:26:30,148
好了，让我们用 DONE 框架来创建第一个正式任务。
Alright, let's create our first real task using the Done framework.

2316
03:26:30,766 --> 03:26:31,952
我开始全新的操作。
I'm starting fresh.

2317
03:26:32,238 --> 03:26:36,100
你可以看到我正在 Clone 桌面应用的 Co-work 选项卡中。
You can see I'm in the Co-work tab of the Clone Desktop app.

2318
03:26:36,750 --> 03:26:39,712
在左上角，有一个新任务按钮。
In the top left corner, there's a new task button.

2319
03:26:40,014 --> 03:26:40,672
点击它。
Click it.

2320
03:26:41,102 --> 03:26:42,352
进入新对话选项卡。
So New Chat tab.

2321
03:26:42,830 --> 03:26:44,900
这会打开一个干净的对话输入框。
This opens a clean chat input.

2322
03:26:45,326 --> 03:26:48,036
这就是我要给我的 AI 员工下达任务简报的地方。
This is where I'm going to brief my AI employee.

2323
03:26:48,430 --> 03:26:52,868
但在我输入任何内容之前，让我先展示一下我桌面上的准备工作。
But before I type anything, let me show you what I have ready on my desktop.

2324
03:26:53,358 --> 03:26:56,516
我有一个名为 Q1 Sales Data 的文件夹。
So I have a folder named Q1 Sales Data.

2325
03:26:57,006 --> 03:27:01,924
里面有 12 个 Excel 文件，每一个对应我团队的一名销售代表。
Inside there are 12 Excel files, one for each sales rep on my team.

2326
03:27:02,318 --> 03:27:07,172
每个文件都包含他们第一季度的交易、收入和成交率。
Each file has their deals, revenue, and close rate for the first quarter.

2327
03:27:07,598 --> 03:27:08,432
我的目标是？
My goal?

2328
03:27:08,846 --> 03:27:16,548
我想要一份单一的总结文档，显示出表现最好的前三名、最差的后三名以及团队的整体平均水平。
I want a single summary document that shows me the top three performers, the bottom three, and an overall team average.

2329
03:27:17,006 --> 03:27:20,836
初学者可能会输入类似“总结销售数据”这样的内容。
A beginner would type something like summarize to sales data.

2330
03:27:21,198 --> 03:27:23,652
那是提示工程，而不是委派。
That's prompting, that's not delegating.

2331
03:27:24,078 --> 03:27:26,756
让我展示一下我们如何用 DONE 框架来操作。
Let me show you how we do it with the DUN framework.

2332
03:27:27,182 --> 03:27:29,220
现在我打开我的 Co-work 选项卡。
So now I'll open my cowork tab.

2333
03:27:29,614 --> 03:27:36,592
我现在输入：在 Q1 Sales Data 文件夹中创建一个名为 Q1 Sales Summary 的 Word 文档。
So here I'm typing create a Word document called Q1 Sales Summary in the Q1 Sales Data folder.

2334
03:27:36,814 --> 03:27:42,180
我已经给文件命名了，设定了格式，并告诉了它保存在哪里。
So I have named the file, I have set the format, I have told it where to save.

2335
03:27:42,638 --> 03:27:45,380
这已经比大多数人的操作要具体多了。
That's already more specific than most people get.

2336
03:27:45,678 --> 03:27:47,300
现在我来添加结构。
Now I'm adding structure.

2337
03:27:47,726 --> 03:27:55,300
我输入：该文档应包含三个部分：表现最好的前三名、表现最差的后三名以及团队平均水平。
I'll type the document should have three sections, top three performers, bottom three performers, and team average.

2338
03:27:55,758 --> 03:28:00,292
对于每一位成员，列出他们的姓名、总收入和成交率。
For each performer, list their name, total revenue, and close rate.

2339
03:28:00,878 --> 03:28:04,676
现在 Claude 清楚地知道最终产物长什么样了。
Now Claude knows exactly what the finished artifact looks like.

2340
03:28:05,102 --> 03:28:06,628
接下来是上下文。
Next, context.

2341
03:28:07,086 --> 03:28:11,012
我会输入：源文件是那个文件夹里的 12 个 Excel 文件。
I'll type the source files are the 12 Excel files in that folder.

2342
03:28:11,470 --> 03:28:16,512
每个文件的名称都是按销售代表命名的。收入列的名称叫 closed one。
Each file is named after the sales rep. The revenue column is called closed one.

2343
03:28:17,422 --> 03:28:20,452
成交率这一列的名称叫 win percentage。
The close rate column is called win percentage.

2344
03:28:20,974 --> 03:28:21,952
看到我刚才的操作了吗？
See what I did there?

2345
03:28:22,286 --> 03:28:28,832
我告诉了 Claude 数据在哪里，告诉了它各列的名称，去除了歧义。
I told Claude where the data is, I told it what the columns are called, I removed ambiguity.

2346
03:28:29,072 --> 03:28:32,772
这很重要，因为 Claude 将会打开每一个文件。
This matters because Claude is going to open each of those files.

2347
03:28:33,294 --> 03:28:36,868
如果我不告诉它要看哪些列，它可能会猜错。
If I don't tell it what columns to look at, it might guess wrong.

2348
03:28:37,294 --> 03:28:40,676
它可能会选到流水线收入而不是成交收入。
It might pick up pipeline revenue instead of closed one.

2349
03:28:41,102 --> 03:28:43,472
上下文能帮你避免糟糕的输出。
Context saves you from bad output.

2350
03:28:43,632 --> 03:28:44,996
最后是约束条件。
Finally, constraints.

2351
03:28:45,294 --> 03:28:48,804
我会输入：不要修改原始 Excel 文件。
I'll type do not modify the original Excel files.

2352
03:28:49,230 --> 03:28:53,312
不要在 Q1 销售数据文件夹之外创建任何文件。
Do not create any files outside the Q1 sales data folder.

2353
03:28:53,550 --> 03:28:58,752
如果任何 Excel 文件缺失数据，请在文档中标记出来，而不是去猜测。
If any of the Excel files are missing data, flag it in the document instead of guessing.

2354
03:28:58,992 --> 03:28:59,908
一共三个约束条件。
Three constraints.

2355
03:29:00,272 --> 03:29:04,112
每一个约束都能防止我预见到的特定问题。
Each one prevents a specific problem I could imagine going wrong.

2356
03:29:04,352 --> 03:29:07,684
现在，在提交之前，让我们一起看一下整体内容。
Now, before submitting, let's look at the whole thing together.

2357
03:29:08,142 --> 03:29:12,548
整个提示词大约有 150 个单词，这没问题。
The entire prompt is about 150 words, and that's fine.

2358
03:29:12,878 --> 03:29:14,592
事实上，这正是重点所在。
In fact, that's the point.

2359
03:29:15,022 --> 03:29:21,156
当你给新员工布置他们从未做过的工作时，你会花五分钟来解释它。
When you're briefing a new employee on a task they have never done before, you would take five minutes to explain it.

2360
03:29:21,550 --> 03:29:24,964
你不会只给他们一句话就指望他们能完美完成。
You would not give them one sentence and expect perfect work.

2361
03:29:25,326 --> 03:29:27,012
对待 Co-work 也要同样的操作。
Treat cowork the same way.

2362
03:29:27,406 --> 03:29:28,752
所以我要按回车键了。
So I'll click enter.

2363
03:29:28,912 --> 03:29:29,872
看看会发生什么。
Watch what happens.

2364
03:29:30,286 --> 03:29:31,952
Claude 不会直接就开始工作。
Claude doesn't just start working.

2365
03:29:32,334 --> 03:29:34,192
Claude 会先向我展示它的计划。
Claude shows me its plan first.

2366
03:29:34,574 --> 03:29:35,872
让我们等一下输出结果。
Let's wait for the output.

2367
03:29:36,032 --> 03:29:37,892
好，现在来看看发生了什么。
Okay, now let's see what happens.

2368
03:29:38,350 --> 03:29:42,884
Claude 想在一个文件夹里进行 Co-work，所以它在要求我选择文件夹。
Claude would like to co-work in a folder, so it's asking me to select folder.

2369
03:29:43,054 --> 03:29:44,228
所以我点这里。
So I'll click here.

2370
03:29:44,718 --> 03:29:49,312
我希望在 Q1 销售数据文件夹中操作，所以我选择那个文件夹。
I want this in Q1 sales data folder, so I'll select that folder.

2371
03:29:49,550 --> 03:29:50,532
看看会发生什么。
Watch what happens.

2372
03:29:51,086 --> 03:29:52,832
Claude 不会直接开始工作。
Claude doesn't just start working.

2373
03:29:52,992 --> 03:29:55,044
Claude 会先向我展示它的计划。
Claude shows me its plan first.

2374
03:29:55,472 --> 03:29:56,644
这非常关键。
This is critical.

2375
03:29:57,102 --> 03:29:58,052
看这些步骤。
See these steps.

2376
03:29:58,478 --> 03:30:01,092
Claude 在说，这是我即将要做的操作。
Claude is saying, here's what I'm about to do.

2377
03:30:01,934 --> 03:30:06,724
看这里，我们可以看到任务的进度，比如正在盘点 Excel 文件。
See here, we can see the progress of the task like inventorying Excel files.

2378
03:30:07,214 --> 03:30:10,660
从每个文件中提取「成交量」和「胜率」。
Extract Closed 1 and win percentage from each file.

2379
03:30:10,990 --> 03:30:13,220
计算前三名和后三名。
Compute top three, bottom three.

2380
03:30:13,838 --> 03:30:16,512
每一个步骤，每一项进展我们都能在这里看到。
Every step, every progress we can see here.

2381
03:30:16,878 --> 03:30:19,428
在它运行的时候，我想谈谈截止日期。
While it's working, I want to talk about deadlines.

2382
03:30:19,886 --> 03:30:27,716
Co-Work 没有像项目管理中那样要求的截止日期字段，但你可以在提示词中加入相关内容来设定一个事实上的截止日期。
Cowork doesn't have a deadline field the way project management told us, but you can set a de facto deadline by including it in your prompt.

2383
03:30:28,206 --> 03:30:34,500
你可以说，我需要在接下来的 10 分钟内完成这个，或者这个需要在我 2 点的会议前准备好。
You can say, I need this done in next 10 minutes, or this needs to be ready for my 2 o'clock meeting.

2384
03:30:34,926 --> 03:30:36,032
为什么这很重要？
Why does that matter?

2385
03:30:36,334 --> 03:30:38,788
因为它告诉 Claude 如何在质量和速度之间做权衡。
Because it tells Claude how to make trade-offs.

2386
03:30:39,246 --> 03:30:43,524
如果是两分钟的截止日期，Claude 可能会跳过一些验证步骤。
If it's a two-minute deadline, Claude might skip some validation steps.

2387
03:30:44,014 --> 03:30:47,652
如果是四个小时的截止日期，它可能会对数据进行两次交叉检查。
If it's a four-hour deadline, it might cross-check the numbers twice.

2388
03:30:48,206 --> 03:30:51,108
你是在给它分配关于质量与速度的预算。
You are giving it a budget for quality versus speed.

2389
03:30:51,566 --> 03:30:55,364
你还可以利用截止日期来描述链式工作流中的顺序。
You can also use deadlines to describe sequence in a chained workflow.

2390
03:30:55,662 --> 03:30:59,872
比如，先总结这个，然后在完成后，把它翻译成西班牙语。
Like first summarize this, then after that's done, translate it into Spanish.

2391
03:31:00,206 --> 03:31:01,712
Claude 理解先后顺序。
Claude understands order.

2392
03:31:02,062 --> 03:31:04,512
任务完成了。让我打开输出结果。
The task is done. Let me open the output.

2393
03:31:04,878 --> 03:31:06,112
这就是我的文件夹。
So this is my folder.

2394
03:31:06,318 --> 03:31:10,436
现在你可以看到我有一个名为「第一季度销售总结」的 Word 文档。
Now you can see I have a Word document named Q1 Sales Summary.

2395
03:31:10,766 --> 03:31:11,524
我把它打开。
I'll open it.

2396
03:31:11,854 --> 03:31:13,072
这就是我的文档。
So this is my document.

2397
03:31:13,390 --> 03:31:20,036
这里有表现最好的前三名、最差的后三名，还有团队平均值以及数据质量备注。
So I have top three performers, bottom three performers, and team average and also data quality notes.

2398
03:31:20,622 --> 03:31:23,492
所有 12 个源工作簿都已成功读取。
All 12 source workbooks were read successfully.

2399
03:31:23,822 --> 03:31:29,060
在「成交量」或「胜率」列中未发现缺失值。
No missing values were found in the closed, one, or win percentage columns.

2400
03:31:29,294 --> 03:31:34,628
而且每个文件中的总计行与底层交易行的重新求和结果一致。
And the total row in each file matched a fresh sum of the underlying deal rows.

2401
03:31:35,374 --> 03:31:37,540
这正是我想要的结果。
This is exactly what I asked for.

2402
03:31:37,902 --> 03:31:41,412
注意看，这些是我的原始 Excel 文件。
And notice here, these are my original Excel files.

2403
03:31:41,774 --> 03:31:43,312
就像它们没被动过一样。
Like these are untouched.

2404
03:31:43,502 --> 03:31:44,672
约束条件起作用了。
The constraint worked.

2405
03:31:44,974 --> 03:31:48,036
我想通过这个练习让大家学到的一点是：
Here's what the lesson I want you to take from this exercise.

2406
03:31:48,558 --> 03:31:51,620
Claude 输出的质量并不取决于 Claude 本身。
The quality of Claude's output is not about Claude.

2407
03:31:51,854 --> 03:31:52,868
而是取决于任务简报。
It's about the brief.

2408
03:31:53,390 --> 03:31:56,132
你的简报写得越好，交付物就越出色。
The better you brief, the better the deliverable.

2409
03:31:56,750 --> 03:31:58,148
把精力花在提示词上。
Spend your time on the prompt.

2410
03:31:58,574 --> 03:32:04,228
在点击「开始」前花三分钟思考，能帮你省去后面 30 分钟的重复运行。
Three minutes of thinking before you hit Let's Go will save you 30 minutes of reruns later.

2411
03:32:04,654 --> 03:32:13,092
所以我快速总结一下：定义 DONE，提供上下文，设定约束，检查计划，然后让它运行。
So I say quick recap: define done, give context, set constraints, review the plan, let it run.

2412
03:32:13,710 --> 03:32:20,548
剧本是针对那些需要多次执行、但不一定有固定时间表的任务的重复使用模板。
A playbook is a reusable template for a task you run more than once, but not necessarily on a fixed schedule.

2413
03:32:21,326 --> 03:32:22,564
你可以这样理解。
Think about it this way.

2414
03:32:23,054 --> 03:32:26,724
定时任务是：每周五做这个。
A schedule task is every Friday, do this.

2415
03:32:27,438 --> 03:32:31,844
剧本是：每当我需要做这个时，就触发它。
A playbook is whenever I need to do this, just trigger it.

2416
03:32:32,718 --> 03:32:34,564
定时任务是基于时间的。
Schedule tasks are time-based.

2417
03:32:35,214 --> 03:32:37,060
剧本是基于事件的。
Playbooks are event-based.

2418
03:32:37,934 --> 03:32:40,644
我举几个例子让它更具体点。
Let me give you examples to make this concrete.

2419
03:32:41,390 --> 03:32:43,012
新客户入驻。
Onboarding a new client.

2420
03:32:43,630 --> 03:32:46,272
你并不是每周五才接一个新客户。
You don't onboard a new client every Friday.

2421
03:32:46,512 --> 03:32:48,324
而是在你签下合同时才进行入驻。
You onboard them when you sign one.

2422
03:32:48,718 --> 03:32:53,572
但每当你这样做时，都会执行完全相同的 12 个步骤。
But when you do, you run the exact same 12 step process every week.

2423
03:32:54,158 --> 03:33:01,444
欢迎邮件、CRM 入录、创建文件夹、安排启动会议、合同文件。
Welcome email, CRM entry, folder creation, kickoff meeting scheduled, contract file.

2424
03:33:01,966 --> 03:33:03,232
这就是一个剧本。
That's a playbook.

2425
03:33:04,206 --> 03:33:05,828
在周一结账。
Closing the books on Monday.

2426
03:33:06,158 --> 03:33:11,108
你一个月做一次，但从 CoWork 的角度来看，周一并不算是一个固定的时间表。
You do it once a month, but Monday isn't really a fixed schedule in the co-work sense.

2427
03:33:11,950 --> 03:33:14,596
当你决定这个月结束时，你就触发它。
You trigger it when you decide the month is closed.

2428
03:33:14,958 --> 03:33:16,388
这就是一个剧本。
That's a playbook.

2429
03:33:17,198 --> 03:33:18,916
准备销售电话。
Preparing for a sales call.

2430
03:33:19,534 --> 03:33:28,804
当有新线索出现在你的日程表上时，你想要一份包含他们公司背景、近期新闻以及你们最后一次往来邮件的单页资料。
When a new lead lands on your calendar, you want a one pager with their company background, recent news, and your last email exchanged with them.

2431
03:33:29,582 --> 03:33:30,596
看到规律了吗？
See the pattern?

2432
03:33:31,022 --> 03:33:34,884
任务相同，触发条件不同，没有固定的时间表。
Same task, different trigger, no fixed schedule.

2433
03:33:35,662 --> 03:33:39,012
构建剧本的最佳方式是使用项目。
The best way to build a playbook is to use a project.

2434
03:33:39,630 --> 03:33:48,132
项目是一个工作区，并与具有自己文件、连接器、指令和记忆的 CoWork 一起运行。
A project is a workspace and co-work with its own files, its own connectors, its own instructions, and its own memory.

2435
03:33:48,942 --> 03:33:50,084
让我创建一个。
Let me create one.

2436
03:33:50,926 --> 03:33:53,328
现在我将创建一个新项目。
So now I'll create a new project.

2437
03:33:53,678 --> 03:33:58,084
我点击这个项目选项，然后点击新建项目。
I'll click this project option and I'll click new project.

2438
03:33:58,702 --> 03:34:06,308
这里有不同的选项，比如从头开始、导入项目，或者使用现有的文件夹。
And here are different options like Start from Scratch, Import a Project, or maybe use an existing folder.

2439
03:34:06,926 --> 03:34:08,836
我选择从头开始。
I'll click Start from Scratch.

2440
03:34:09,518 --> 03:34:12,772
在项目名称处，我输入“新客户入职”。
At Project Name, I'll give onboarding a new client.

2441
03:34:13,326 --> 03:34:19,236
在其中，我将给它一套指令，基本上就是剧本本身。
And inside this, I'm going to give it a set of instructions, basically the playbook itself.

2442
03:34:20,046 --> 03:34:24,516
这些指令描述了该项目每次运行时要做什么。
These instructions describe what this project does every time it runs.

2443
03:34:25,102 --> 03:34:26,788
所以我会输入类似这样的内容。
So I'll type something like this.

2444
03:34:27,502 --> 03:34:30,660
这个项目负责处理新客户的入职流程。
So this project handles onboarding for new clients.

2445
03:34:31,534 --> 03:34:34,500
该项目中的每个任务都应执行四件事。
Every task in this project should do four things.

2446
03:34:35,214 --> 03:34:42,596
1. 在我们的客户目录中创建一个客户文件夹，并包含合同、沟通和交付物的子文件夹。
Create a client folder in our client's directory with subfolders for contracts, communication, and deliverables.

2447
03:34:43,278 --> 03:34:46,660
2. 起草一封发给新客户的欢迎邮件。
2. Draft a welcome email addressed to the new client.

2448
03:34:47,566 --> 03:34:51,620
3. 将草稿作为文本文件保存在沟通文件夹中。
Save the draft as a text file in the communications folder 3.

2449
03:34:52,910 --> 03:34:58,048
4. 在交付物子文件夹中创建一个 Word 文档作为启动会议议程。
Create a kickoff agenda as a Word document in the Deliverables subfolder 4.

2450
03:34:58,208 --> 03:35:03,044
更新主客户列表表格，填入新客户的名称和开始日期。
Update the Master Client list spreadsheet with the new client's name and start date.

2451
03:35:03,502 --> 03:35:05,892
这就是剧本，一共四个步骤。
So that's the playbook, four steps.

2452
03:35:06,606 --> 03:35:10,436
现在每当我获得一个新客户时，我只需进入这个项目。
Every time now when I get a new client, I just come into this project.

2453
03:35:10,958 --> 03:35:19,328
在这里，我输入一行简短的内容，比如“新客户是 ACME Corporation，今日签署合同”
Here I'll come and I'll type a one-liner like new client is maybe ACME Corporation, Contact Sign Today,

2454
03:35:19,694 --> 03:35:23,652
然后 Claude 会运行整个剧本，并填入 ACME 的详细信息。
and Clone runs the whole playbook with ACME's details filled in.

2455
03:35:24,366 --> 03:35:33,188
现在我在这里输入“新客户是 ACME Corporation，今日签署合同”，然后按回车键。
So now I'll just type here, like new client is ACME Corporation, Contact Sign Today, and I'll click enter.

2456
03:35:33,710 --> 03:35:34,884
让我们看看发生了什么。
Let's see what happens.

2457
03:35:35,662 --> 03:35:36,996
这就是我们的输出结果。
So we have our output.

2458
03:35:37,358 --> 03:35:40,132
好的，我们这里有三个文件。
Okay, so we have three files here.

2459
03:35:40,608 --> 03:35:50,724
第一个是欢迎邮件草稿，这是我们的欢迎邮件；接下来是启动议程，这是会议的启动议程；
One, the welcome email draft, so this is our welcome email, and now then I have kickoff agenda, this is the meeting kickoff agenda,

2460
03:35:51,088 --> 03:35:53,284
然后是主客户列表。
and then master client list.

2461
03:35:53,966 --> 03:36:04,516
它显示主客户列表还不存在，所以我创建了一个包含客户名称和开始日期列的表格，并把 ACME 公司及其开始日期添加了进去。
And it's telling the master client list didn't exist yet, so I created it with client name and start date columns and added ACME Corporation with the start date.

2462
03:36:05,262 --> 03:36:09,956
联系人文件夹是空的，你可以把签署好的合同放进去。
The contact folder is empty and ready for you to drop the signed contract in.

2463
03:36:10,382 --> 03:36:14,564
好了，这就是我们的输出结果，它已经保存在我的系统中了。
Okay, so this is our output and this is saved in my system.

2464
03:36:15,118 --> 03:36:19,556
在文档部分，我为 Claude 创建了一个专门的文件夹。
So here in the document sections, I have a dedicated folder for clone.

2465
03:36:20,078 --> 03:36:23,808
在这里，在项目下方，可以看到新客户的入职流程。
Here, under projects, I can see onboarding a new client.

2466
03:36:24,366 --> 03:36:27,108
这就是客户 ACME 公司。
So this is the client's ACME Corporation.

2467
03:36:27,470 --> 03:36:32,708
这里有详细信息，比如沟通记录、合同和交付物。
And here I have the details like communications, contracts, and deliverables.

2468
03:36:33,262 --> 03:36:35,044
这是我的启动议程。
So this is my kickoff agenda.

2469
03:36:35,438 --> 03:36:36,768
这是我的合同。
This is my contract.

2470
03:36:37,102 --> 03:36:40,388
这个文件夹现在是空的，还有沟通记录。
This folder is empty now, and communication.

2471
03:36:40,814 --> 03:36:44,676
这是欢迎邮件正文，这是主客户列表。
This is the welcome email text, and this is the master client list.

2472
03:36:45,294 --> 03:36:50,768
现在，如果你想与团队共享这个剧本，Claude 有一个功能叫插件。
Now, if you want to share this playbook with your team, Kovark has a feature called plugins.

2473
03:36:51,374 --> 03:36:58,084
插件可以将工作流打包成一个包，团队中的其他人就可以安装并使用。
Plugins bundle up the workflow into a package that other people on your team can install and use.

2474
03:36:58,798 --> 03:37:07,248
我现在不打算从头开始构建插件，但我希望你了解它的存在，因为一旦你建立了一个运行非常出色的剧本，
I'm not going to build a plugin from scratch now, but I want you to know it exists because once you have built a playbook that works really well,

2475
03:37:07,502 --> 03:37:13,444
你就可以把它打包，团队中的每个人都能按照相同的标准执行相同的过程。
you can package it up and everyone on your team runs the same process with the same standards.

2476
03:37:14,094 --> 03:37:20,932
任何管理车队、经营小型运输业务或仅仅是申报报销差旅费的人都经历过这种情况。
Anyone who manages a fleet, runs a small transport business, or even just claims travel on tax has lived this.

2477
03:37:21,550 --> 03:37:23,268
你们得记纸质账本。
You keep a paper diary.

2478
03:37:23,726 --> 03:37:29,892
每一次行程，日期、车辆编号、目的地、距离等信息都要手写记录下来。
Every trip, date, vehicle number, destination, distance, etc. gets scribbled in.

2479
03:37:30,446 --> 03:37:37,636
到月底时，必须有人把所有内容录入到电子表格中，以便进行计费、报销或填报。
At the end of the month, somebody has to type all of it into a spreadsheet so it can be billed, reimbursed, or filled.

2480
03:37:38,062 --> 03:37:40,036
这简直是枯燥的代名词。
It's the definition of tedious.

2481
03:37:40,558 --> 03:37:44,484
同样的字迹，同一个地方可能有五种不同的写法。
The handwriting is the same place, gets written five different ways.

2482
03:37:44,910 --> 03:37:54,052
车辆编号模糊不清，日期混在一起，而注册号中只要错一个数字，财务就会找你核实。
Vehicle numbers smudge, dates blur into each other, and one wrong digit in a registration number means accounting comes back asking questions.

2483
03:37:54,894 --> 03:37:58,564
如果你维护过任何类型的日志，你就知道这种痛苦。
If you maintain a logbook of any kind, you know this pain.

2484
03:37:59,054 --> 03:38:07,012
两页的记录，要打 45 分钟字，让人头痛不已，而且至少有一条记录你得反复去读，
Two pages of entries, 45 minutes of typing, a splitting headache, and at least one entry you have to go back and reread

2485
03:38:07,264 --> 03:38:10,308
因为你分不清那是字母 B 还是数字 8。
because you can't tell if that's a B or an 8.

2486
03:38:10,926 --> 03:38:13,540
我们要一举把这个自动化。
We are going to automate this in one shot.

2487
03:38:14,064 --> 03:38:16,356
这是我行程日志中的一页。
This is a page from my trip diary.

2488
03:38:17,134 --> 03:38:20,324
所以这里你可以看到总共有 16 条记录。
So here you can see 16 entries in total.

2489
03:38:20,718 --> 03:38:30,884
每一行代表一次行程，左列是日期，中间是车辆注册号，右边是我访问地点的简写代码。
Each row is a trip, the date in the left column, the vehicle registration number in the middle, and a shorthand code for the places I visited in the right.

2490
03:38:31,406 --> 03:38:37,504
所以这里分别是 NBR、NDPM 和 ULLY。
So here, NBR, NDPM, and ULLY.

2491
03:38:38,606 --> 03:38:44,944
NBR 是 Nilambur，这是 Nadapuram，这是 Uliari。
NBR is Nilambur, and this is Nadapuram, and this is Uliari.

2492
03:38:45,326 --> 03:38:47,108
这里可以看到距离。
And here you can see the distance.

2493
03:38:47,758 --> 03:38:51,744
对于 Nilambur，每趟行程都是 177。
For Nilambur, every trip it's 177.

2494
03:38:52,398 --> 03:38:58,980
对于 Nadapuram 是 174，而 Uliari 是 128。
For Nadapuram, it's 174, and for Uliari it's 128.

2495
03:38:59,504 --> 03:39:03,076
所以每条路线的距离我心里都有数。
So the distance for each route is something I know in my head.

2496
03:39:03,406 --> 03:39:06,020
我在每一行旁边都标注了一些内容。
I note something written next to every row.

2497
03:39:06,224 --> 03:39:08,260
我只是在这里写了一个地方。
I just wrote in one place here.

2498
03:39:08,718 --> 03:39:10,276
这只是一个例子。
This is just an example.

2499
03:39:10,624 --> 03:39:13,344
想象一下我有成千上万行这样的数据。
Imagine me having thousands of such rows.

2500
03:39:13,504 --> 03:39:16,708
这只有 16 行手写笔记。
This is only 16 rows of handwritten notes.

2501
03:39:17,294 --> 03:39:20,420
想象一下有成千上万行这样的手写记录。
Imagine having thousands of such handwritten rows.

2502
03:39:21,070 --> 03:39:23,172
让我给你们看看 Co-work 能做什么。
So let me show you what cowork can do.

2503
03:39:23,790 --> 03:39:25,024
我打开 Co-work。
I'll open co-work.

2504
03:39:25,486 --> 03:39:29,700
现在点击这个加号图标，选择文件或照片。
Now in this plus icon, I'll select art files or photos.

2505
03:39:30,286 --> 03:39:32,836
从我的下载文件夹里，选这张图片。
And from my downloads, this is the image.

2506
03:39:33,230 --> 03:39:34,180
我把它上传上去。
I'll attach this.

2507
03:39:34,990 --> 03:39:36,516
在这里粘贴我的提示词。
Here I'll paste my prompt.

2508
03:39:37,166 --> 03:39:38,340
这就是我的提示词。
So this is my prompt.

2509
03:39:38,734 --> 03:39:46,660
我要仔细写这个任务简报，因为这类任务如果不明确说明，模型就没法猜到你的意思。
Here I'm going to brief this carefully because this is exactly the kind of task where the model can't guess what you mean unless you've done it.

2510
03:39:47,214 --> 03:39:49,988
这是我手写旅行日记中的一页。
So this is a page from my handwritten trip diary.

2511
03:39:50,446 --> 03:39:55,012
读取页面上的每一条记录，并从每行中提取以下字段。
Read every entry on the page and extract the following fields from each row.

2512
03:39:55,502 --> 03:40:03,044
我需要日期、车辆注册号、地点代码，以及根据我即将提供的代码对应的完整地名。
I need date, vehicle registration number, place code, and a full place name based on the code I'm about to give you.

2513
03:40:03,726 --> 03:40:11,744
所以这里我会详细说明，比如 NBR 代表 Nilumber，公里数是 177。
So here I'm giving in detail like NBR means it's Nilumber, and the kilometers is 177.

2514
03:40:12,366 --> 03:40:18,692
而 NDBR 表示它不是 Purim，公里数是 174。
And NDBR means it's not a Purim, and the kilometers would be 174.

2515
03:40:19,150 --> 03:40:21,024
还有 Uli 是 Ulieri。
And Uli is Ulieri.

2516
03:40:21,550 --> 03:40:23,524
我把所有细节都写在这里。
Every details I'm giving here.

2517
03:40:23,886 --> 03:40:29,220
并且我要求它创建一个名为 triplog 2026 的 Excel 文件。
And I'm asking it to create an Excel file called triplog 2026.

2518
03:40:29,774 --> 03:40:32,740
我想要的所有细节，我都输入在这里。
And all the details which I want, I type here.

2519
03:40:33,230 --> 03:40:40,996
最后，我需要一个汇总行，用有效的求和公式计算公里数列的总和，而不是硬编码的数字。
And at the end, I need a total row that sums the kilometers column using a working sum formula, not a hard-coded number.

2520
03:40:41,454 --> 03:40:51,428
现在进行整洁的格式化：带底色的加粗表头、交替的行阴影、冻结表头行，以及我提供的所有细节。
Now format it cleanly, bold headers on a colored fill, alternating row shading, frozen header row, and all the details I have given here.

2521
03:40:51,982 --> 03:41:01,744
作为约束条件，如果手写体中的车辆编号不明确，比如你不确定的数字或可能有两个含义的字母，
As constraints, I'm giving if any vehicle number is ambiguous in the handwriting, like a digit you are not sure about, a letter that could be one of two things.

2522
03:41:01,984 --> 03:41:09,924
请还是按你最准确的判断填入该行，并在最后标出你不确定的行，以便我进行抽查。
Put the row in anyway with your best read and call out which rows you are uncertain about at the end so I can spot check them.

2523
03:41:10,894 --> 03:41:12,900
不要去猜测距离。
Do not guess at distances.

2524
03:41:13,264 --> 03:41:15,684
只使用我提供的这三个数值。
Only use the three values I gave you.

2525
03:41:16,078 --> 03:41:19,268
不要虚构我代码簿中不存在的地点代码。
Do not invent place codes that are in my code book.

2526
03:41:19,790 --> 03:41:21,796
这就是我详细的提示词。
So this is my detailed prompt.

2527
03:41:22,094 --> 03:41:23,904
这任务简报挺长的，对吧？
That's a long brief, right?

2528
03:41:24,238 --> 03:41:28,452
必须这么写，因为我们要让它识别手写内容。
And it has to be because we are asking for visual reading of handwriting.

2529
03:41:28,944 --> 03:41:34,532
解析结构化但凌乱的日志、应用查找表，这些要求都是合理的。
Parsing of a structured but messy log, applying a lookup table are justified.

2530
03:41:35,024 --> 03:41:41,700
生成一个带有有效公式且对模糊条目有回退方案的格式化 Excel 文件。
Generating a formatted Excel file with a working formula and a foldback plan for ambiguous entries.

2531
03:41:42,478 --> 03:41:47,812
如果我省略了其中任何一项要求，输出结果都会变差。
Every one of those requirements, if I skipped it, would produce a worse output.

2532
03:41:48,526 --> 03:41:52,740
如果我不提供代码簿，地点列就只会显示代码。
If I didn't give the code book, the place column would just be the codes.

2533
03:41:53,326 --> 03:41:59,908
如果我不要求使用有效的求和公式，它就会给出一个手动输入的数字，一旦我增加新行，这个总数就不会更新。
If I didn't say working some formula, I would get a typed in number that breaks if I add a new row.

2534
03:42:00,494 --> 03:42:06,564
如果我不要求标记模糊的行，我就得手动检查全部 16 行了。
If I didn't ask for ambiguous rows to be flagged, I would be checking all 16 by hand.

2535
03:42:07,246 --> 03:42:08,708
看，现在正在运行。
See, it's running now.

2536
03:42:09,102 --> 03:42:18,084
这个任务比纯文本任务要花点时间，因为 Claude 实际上在查看照片，并逐条读取手写内容。
This one takes a bit longer than a pure text task because Claude is actually looking at the photo and reading the handwriting at one entry at a time.

2537
03:42:18,766 --> 03:42:19,780
给它一分钟时间。
Let's give it a minute.

2538
03:42:20,174 --> 03:42:22,304
在等待的时候，我来解释一下现在发生了什么。
While we wait, here's what's happening.

2539
03:42:22,670 --> 03:42:24,036
Claude 打开了图片。
Claude opens the image.

2540
03:42:24,270 --> 03:42:30,564
它识别出结构，包括日期列、车辆列以及每一行的地点列。
It identifies the structure, the date column, the vehicle column, the place column for each row.

2541
03:42:31,022 --> 03:42:32,804
它在转录手写内容。
It transcribes the handwriting.

2542
03:42:33,134 --> 03:42:38,564
它将地点代码与我提供的代码簿进行交叉比对，并查出距离。
It cross-references the place code against the code book I provided and looks up the distance.

2543
03:42:39,118 --> 03:42:41,092
然后它开始组装电子表格。
Then it assembles the spreadsheet.

2544
03:42:41,550 --> 03:42:42,784
我的输出结果准备好了。
My output is ready.

2545
03:42:43,118 --> 03:42:44,944
我点这里查看输出。
I'll click here to view the output.

2546
03:42:45,166 --> 03:42:53,104
如你所见，我们有 16 行数据，这里有序号、行程日期、车辆编号、地点
So as you can see, we have 16 rows, and here we have serial number, trip date, vehicle number, place

2547
03:42:53,424 --> 03:42:55,684
代码、地点以及公里数。
code, place, and kilometers.

2548
03:42:56,366 --> 03:42:59,344
车辆编号是 KL 和 Ka 的混合。
The vehicle number is a mix of KL and Ka.

2549
03:43:00,334 --> 03:43:05,316
此外，地点代码已映射到完整名称，并从代码簿中填入了距离。
Also, place codes map to full names and distances filled in from the code book.

2550
03:43:05,774 --> 03:43:08,164
在最底部，你可以看到总计。
And at the down bottom you can see the total.

2551
03:43:08,750 --> 03:43:12,132
这是一个可用的求和公式，不是手动输入的数字。
This is a working sum formula, not a number typed in.

2552
03:43:12,558 --> 03:43:17,188
是真正的公式，这意味着如果我以后增加一行，总数会自动更新。
An actual formula, which means if I add a row later, the total updates.

2553
03:43:17,614 --> 03:43:21,220
这两天的距离是 2612 公里。
2612 kilometers for these two days.

2554
03:43:21,806 --> 03:43:23,940
现在我回到 Claude 界面。
Now I'll go back to Claude interface.

2555
03:43:24,398 --> 03:43:26,564
注意对话末尾的消息。
Notice the message at the end of the chat.

2556
03:43:27,054 --> 03:43:32,964
所以这里，Claude 标记了车辆编号和行号，比如那些手写内容模糊的行。
So here, Claude flagged vehicle numbers and the row number, like rows where the handwriting was ambiguous.

2557
03:43:33,454 --> 03:43:37,424
请核对这些内容，以便我手动检查并确认。
Please port check these so I can manually check and confirm.

2558
03:43:37,774 --> 03:43:39,236
它把这些地方都标记出来了。
It has flagged these things.

2559
03:43:39,662 --> 03:43:41,664
这就是约束条件在起作用。
That's the constraint doing its job.

2560
03:43:42,062 --> 03:43:43,504
它并没有在默默猜测。
It didn't silently guess.

2561
03:43:43,694 --> 03:43:47,332
它给出了最可能的读数，并告诉我哪些行需要核实。
It put its best read in and told me which rows to verify.

2562
03:43:47,758 --> 03:43:53,444
到这一步，我只需要打开原始照片，对照日志核实标记出的行。
And what I do at this point is open the original photo and check flagged rows against the diary.

2563
03:43:53,902 --> 03:44:01,988
这大约需要一分钟，所以处理这段行程日志、提示词、执行和核对的总时间只需几分钟。
This takes about a minute, so the total time for this trip log, prompt, execution, port check was only a few minutes.

2564
03:44:02,478 --> 03:44:05,988
现在有几点重要提示，供你们自己尝试时参考。
And now a few important notes for when you try this yourself.

2565
03:44:06,574 --> 03:44:08,804
首先，照片质量很重要。
First, photo quality matters.

2566
03:44:09,230 --> 03:44:15,716
在光线良好的情况下拍摄清晰的标记页面，比拍一张褶皱且有角度偏差的照片更容易获得准确读数。
A clear photo of a flagged page in good light will give you cleaner reads than a crumpled photo at an angle.

2567
03:44:16,206 --> 03:44:21,412
如果一页纸能看到展开的双面内容，请分别拍摄每一页。
If a page has both sides of a spread visible, photograph each page separately.

2568
03:44:21,934 --> 03:44:24,356
更好的输入意味着更少的标记行。
Better input means fewer flagged rows.

2569
03:44:24,974 --> 03:44:26,944
第二，关键在于代码本。
Second, the codebook is the trick.

2570
03:44:27,118 --> 03:44:34,948
之所以这次成功，是因为我告诉了 Claude NDBR 和 U L L Y 的含义以及对应的距离。
The reason this worked is that I told Claude what NDBR and U L L Y mean and what the distances are.

2571
03:44:35,470 --> 03:44:40,708
如果我把这些内容留在模糊的缩写里，得到的也会是模糊的缩写。
If I had left those in ambiguous shorthand, I would have got back ambiguous shorthand.

2572
03:44:41,646 --> 03:44:50,276
日志中任何个人代码、车辆类型、驾驶员首字母或路线缩写，都要在提示词里写清楚。
Anything in your logbook that's a personal code, vehicle types, driver initials, route abbreviations, spell it out in the prompt.

2573
03:44:50,830 --> 03:44:53,092
第三，为自己建立一个模板。
Third, build a template for yourself.

2574
03:44:53,614 --> 03:45:02,532
我刚才使用的那个提示词，包括准确的措辞、代码本、列清单和约束条件，都保存在项目或笔记里。
The prompt I just used, the exact wording, the codebook, the column list, the constraints, save that in a project or your notes.

2575
03:45:03,118 --> 03:45:11,012
下个月当你拍摄新的两页日志时，只需粘贴同样的提示词，上传新照片，就搞定了。
Next month, when you photograph the next two diary pages, you paste the same prompt, attach the new photo, and you're done.

2576
03:45:11,310 --> 03:45:18,304
第四，如果你每周或每月都做这个操作，可以把它变成一个定时任务，比如每周日晚 6 点。
Fourth, if you do this every week or every month, turn it into a scheduled task every Sunday at 6 p.m.

2577
03:45:18,798 --> 03:45:23,904
在日志文件夹中查看新的日志照片，并把它们添加到当前的行程日志中。
Look in the logbook folder for any new diary photos and append them to the running trip log.

2578
03:45:24,654 --> 03:45:26,724
这样电子表格就永远是更新的。
Now the spreadsheet is always current.

2579
03:45:27,024 --> 03:45:33,636
说实话，单是这个工作流就能体现产品的价值，因为它解决了每个小运营商都需要的功能。
This single workflow honestly sells the product on its own because it takes something every small operator needs.

2580
03:45:34,190 --> 03:45:38,064
将手写内容解码并填入电子表格，这种感觉非常棒。
Typing handwritten decodes into a spreadsheet and makes it feel good.

2581
03:45:38,286 --> 03:45:40,544
让我们从最核心的问题开始。
Let's start with the most important question.

2582
03:45:40,846 --> 03:45:42,276
什么是 Claude Code？
What is Claude Code?

2583
03:45:42,542 --> 03:45:47,396
简单来说，Claude Code 是由 Anthropic 开发的一款智能体化编程工具。
At its simplest, Claude Code is an agentic coding tool built by Anthropic.

2584
03:45:47,790 --> 03:45:55,184
但我们来拆解一下“智能体”这个词，因为它是理解它与以往产品有何不同关键所在。
But let's unpack that word, agenc, because it's the key to understanding why this is different from anything that came before.

2585
03:45:55,470 --> 03:45:58,084
你用过的绝大多数编程工具都是被动响应的。
Most coding tools you've used are reactive.

2586
03:45:58,510 --> 03:46:00,772
你提问，它们回答。
You ask a question, they answer it.

2587
03:46:01,262 --> 03:46:03,684
你选中一个函数，它们解释它。
You highlight a function, they explain it.

2588
03:46:04,270 --> 03:46:06,852
你输入一行代码，它们建议下一行。
You type a line, they suggest the next one.

2589
03:46:07,470 --> 03:46:09,872
它们在等待你引导每一个步骤。
They wait for you to lead every single step.

2590
03:46:10,190 --> 03:46:11,684
Claude Code 不同。
Claude code is different.

2591
03:46:12,014 --> 03:46:19,392
它是智能体化的，这意味着它可以接收一个目标——也就是你描述的高层目标——然后自主去执行。
It's agentic, meaning it can take a goal, a high-level goal that you describe, and then act on it autonomously.

2592
03:46:19,790 --> 03:46:22,564
它不需要你手把手地带它走过每一个步骤。
It doesn't wait for you to hold its hand through every step.

2593
03:46:22,926 --> 03:46:31,268
它会读取你的代码库，理解结构，规划方案，在多个文件中进行更改，并运行你的测试，
It reads your code base, understands the structure, plans an approach, makes changes across multiple files, runs your tests,

2594
03:46:31,598 --> 03:46:35,268
看到哪里失败了就去修复，然后再次运行测试。
sees what failed, fixes it, and runs the tests again.

2595
03:46:35,758 --> 03:46:38,272
它会一直这样做，直到任务完成为止。
And it does all of this until the job is done.

2596
03:46:38,574 --> 03:46:40,032
你可以这样理解其中的区别。
Think of the difference this way.

2597
03:46:40,366 --> 03:46:46,020
传统的编程助手就像一个非常聪明的同事，能回答你提出的任何问题。
A traditional coding assistant is like a very smart colleague who will answer any question you ask.

2598
03:46:46,478 --> 03:46:52,832
而 Claude Code 更像一名初级开发人员，你可以把整个任务交给它，并说：这是我需要的东西。
Claude Code is more like a junior developer you can hand an entire task to and say, here's what I need.

2599
03:46:53,198 --> 03:46:55,524
你去搞定它，完成后再来找我。
Figure it out and come back to me when it's done.

2600
03:46:55,854 --> 03:46:57,188
现在来看看它运行在什么地方。
Now here's where it lives.

2601
03:46:57,582 --> 03:47:04,324
Claude Code 在你的终端、集成开发环境以及 GitHub 和 Slack 等集成中运行。
Claude Code operates in your terminal, in your IDE, and through integrations like GitHub and Slack.

2602
03:47:04,846 --> 03:47:13,472
它运行在你的终端，理解你的代码库，并通过处理常规任务、解释复杂代码来帮你提高编码速度，
It lives in your terminal, understands your code base, and helps you code faster by handling routine tasks, explaining complex code,

2603
03:47:13,710 --> 03:47:17,540
并且通过自然语言指令来管理 Git 工作流。
and managing Git workflows, all through natural language commands.

2604
03:47:18,318 --> 03:47:26,672
有一点至关重要：与在你输入时提示下一行或函数的代码补全工具不同，Claude
And one critical thing to understand: unlike code completion tools that suggest the next line or function as you type, Claude

2605
03:47:26,912 --> 03:47:29,028
Code 是在项目层面运行的。
Code operates at the project level.

2606
03:47:29,518 --> 03:47:38,404
它会读取整个代码库，跨多个文件制定计划，执行更改，运行测试，并针对失败的情况进行迭代。
It reads the full code base, plans across multiple files, executes changes, runs tests, and iterates on failures.

2607
03:47:38,958 --> 03:47:45,572
作为开发者，你只需定义目标并审查结果，而不是去引导每一个具体步骤。
As a developer, you define the goal and review the result, rather than guiding every individual step.

2608
03:47:46,094 --> 03:47:53,156
这种从逐步辅助到目标级委派的转变，正是 Claude Code 的核心所在。
That shift from step-by-step assistance to goal level delegation is the heart of what Claud Code is.

2609
03:47:53,392 --> 03:48:02,180
好了，既然你已经知道什么是 Claude Code 了，我想说明一下在初次接触 Anthropic
Okay, so now that you know what Cloud Code is, I want to address something that trips almost everyone up when they first encounter Anthropics

2610
03:48:02,352 --> 03:48:03,044
产品系列时，几乎所有人都容易搞混的一点。
product lineup.

2611
03:48:03,598 --> 03:48:08,196
有三种不同的 Claude 产品，它们听起来都挺相关的。
There are three different Claud products and they all kind of sound related.

2612
03:48:08,814 --> 03:48:15,236
你可以这样理解：Chat 用于思考，Code 用于构建，而 Co-Work 用于执行。
Think of it this way: chat is for thinking, code is for building, and cowork is for doing.

2613
03:48:15,598 --> 03:48:22,192
让我把每一个都讲清楚，搞清楚这些区别能帮你避免很多困惑。
Let me walk through each one clearly because understanding this distinction will save you a lot of confusion.

2614
03:48:22,574 --> 03:48:25,092
Claude Chat，对话层。
Claude Chat, the conversational layer.

2615
03:48:25,486 --> 03:48:32,512
Claude 是 Anthropic 的 AI 助手，可以通过 Claude.ai 的网页或移动端界面使用。
Claude is Anthropics AI assistant, available as a web and mobile chat interface at Claude.ai.

2616
03:48:33,102 --> 03:48:39,972
它能处理通用任务，比如写作、分析、编程辅助、研究和头脑风暴。
It handles general purpose tasks like writing, analysis, coding help, research, and brainstorming.

2617
03:48:40,302 --> 03:48:42,912
这是大多数人最先接触到的 Claude 版本。
This is the Claude most people encounter first.

2618
03:48:43,246 --> 03:48:49,764
你在浏览器或手机上打开它，输入信息，它做出回应，你们来回交流。
You open it in a browser or on your phone, you type a message, it responds, and you go back and forth.

2619
03:48:50,030 --> 03:48:54,660
Claude Chat 的核心特征是：你主导每一个步骤。
The key characteristic of Claude Chat is that you are driving every step.

2620
03:48:55,054 --> 03:48:59,716
你提问，查看回复，然后决定下一步做什么。
You ask questions, you review responses, you decide what to do next.

2621
03:49:00,238 --> 03:49:08,356
Claude Chat 在思考问题、起草内容、进行研究和获取解释方面非常强大。
Claude Chat is incredibly powerful for thinking through problems, drafting content, doing research, and getting explanations.

2622
03:49:08,878 --> 03:49:16,548
但除了你手动上传的内容外，它无法访问你的本地文件，也无法在现实世界中采取自主行动。
But it has no access to your local files beyond what you manually upload, and it can't take autonomous action in the world.

2623
03:49:17,038 --> 03:49:19,300
它的工作流简单且是循环的。
The workflow is simple and circular.

2624
03:49:19,598 --> 03:49:24,068
你输入提示词，Claude 通过对话界面做出回应，然后你进行迭代。
You prompt, Claude responds through a chat interface, and you iterate.

2625
03:49:24,430 --> 03:49:30,432
你可以把它想象成一个可以和你聊任何话题的聪明同事，但他们隔着一层玻璃窗。
Think of it as a brilliant colleague you can talk to about anything, but they're on the other side of a glass window.

2626
03:49:30,702 --> 03:49:36,324
你们可以整天交流想法，但他们无法跨越过来在你的环境中实际去干活。
You can exchange ideas all day, but they can't reach through and actually do things in your environment.

2627
03:49:37,134 --> 03:49:40,292
Claude Code，开发者自主层。
Cloud Code, the developer autonomy layer.

2628
03:49:41,038 --> 03:49:43,652
这正是本课程的核心内容。
This is what this entire course is about.

2629
03:49:44,206 --> 03:49:47,876
Claude Code 是为开发者构建的命令行编程智能体。
Cloud Code is a command line coding agent built for developers.

2630
03:49:48,334 --> 03:49:52,068
它运行在你的终端里，或者通过 VS Code 扩展运行。
It runs in your terminal or via a VS Code extension.

2631
03:49:52,654 --> 03:49:59,684
你描述一个问题，Claude Code 会读取你的整个代码库，从而在完整的项目上下文中进行操作。
You describe a problem, and Cloud Code reads your entire code base so it can operate with full project context.

2632
03:50:00,494 --> 03:50:05,636
它能处理重构、调试、编写测试以及 Git 工作流。
It handles refactoring, debugging, test writing, and git workflows.

2633
03:50:06,382 --> 03:50:10,532
与 Chat 的根本区别在于项目层面的自主性。
The fundamental difference from chat is autonomy at the project level.

2634
03:50:11,086 --> 03:50:19,664
你给 Claude Code 一个目标而不是一个问题，它会去朝着那个目标努力，并自行决定如何达成。
You give Cloud Code a goal, not a question, and it goes and works toward that goal, making its own decisions about how to get there,

2635
03:50:19,982 --> 03:50:23,424
只有在遇到不确定或有风险的情况时，它才会向你确认。
checking in with you when something is uncertain or risky.

2636
03:50:23,822 --> 03:50:34,020
通过 Claude.md 配置文件，你可以教会它项目的规范、模式和限制，让它按团队要求的标准来写代码。
With the Claud.md configuration file, you can teach it your project's conventions, patterns, and constraints, so it writes code the way your team expects.

2637
03:50:34,702 --> 03:50:38,564
它不仅仅是感知到代码，而是对你的整个代码库了如指掌。
It's not just code aware, it becomes your code base aware.

2638
03:50:38,926 --> 03:50:42,212
Claude Co-Work，工作流自动化层。
Claude Cowork, the workflow automation layer.

2639
03:50:42,894 --> 03:50:47,108
Co-Work 是最新加入的，也是最让人困惑的一个。
Co-work is the newest addition and the one that confuses people the most.

2640
03:50:47,886 --> 03:51:00,004
Anthropic 将其描述为针对你其他工作的 Claude Code。它是一个智能体化的桌面助手，通过图形用户界面来自动化文件管理和重复性任务。
Anthropic describes it as Claude Code for the rest of your work. It's an agentic desktop assistant that automates file management and repetitive tasks through a graphical user interface.

2641
03:51:00,718 --> 03:51:09,700
你描述一个目标，Claude 负责规划、执行并交付完成的工作、格式化的文档以及组织好的文件系统，
You describe an outcome and Claude plans, executes, and delivers finished work, formatted documents, organized file systems,

2642
03:51:10,158 --> 03:51:14,144
带有可用公式的电子表格，以及综合后的研究报告。
spreadsheets with working formulas, and synthesized research.

2643
03:51:14,510 --> 03:51:19,108
Claude Code 的关键区别在于目标用户和交互界面。
The critical distinction from Cloud Code is the target user and the interface.

2644
03:51:19,950 --> 03:51:21,892
Co-work 是简单易用的选项。
Co-work is the easy option.

2645
03:51:22,158 --> 03:51:27,268
它就在 Claude 桌面应用里，不需要任何设置或安装。
It lives right inside the Cloud Desktop app with no setup, no installation.

2646
03:51:27,790 --> 03:51:29,904
Claude Code 是进阶的高级选项。
Cloud code is the power option.

2647
03:51:30,254 --> 03:51:34,704
你需要在本地安装它，从终端运行，并由你自己进行配置。
You install it locally, run it from your terminal, and configure it yourself.

2648
03:51:35,022 --> 03:51:41,956
Anthropic 推出 Co-work 很大程度上是因为 Claude Code 的设置对非开发人员来说可能太 intimidating（令人望而生畏）。
Anthropic seems to have created cowork largely because Claud Code setup can be intimidating for non-developers.

2649
03:51:42,702 --> 03:51:51,584
Co-work 在一个与广域互联网隔离且受保护的虚拟机中运行，而 Claude Code 则更开放、可配置性更高。
Co-work runs in a virtual machine that is isolated and protected from the wider internet, whereas claud code is more open and configurable.

2650
03:51:51,950 --> 03:51:56,304
这种开放性带来了更强大的功能，但也意味着更多的责任。
With that openness comes more power, but also more responsibility.

2651
03:51:56,750 --> 03:52:03,364
所以简单来说，举个实际例子：如果你需要讨论重构策略，用 chat。
So to put it really simply with a real example, if you need to talk through a refactoring strategy, use chat.

2652
03:52:04,110 --> 03:52:08,544
如果你需要在整个代码库中执行那个重构，就用 code。
If you need to execute that refactor across your code base, use code.

2653
03:52:09,166 --> 03:52:17,264
如果你的运营经理需要从三个源文件中生成一份格式化的 Excel 报告，且不需要操作终端，那就用 Co-work。
If your operations manager needs to generate a formatted Excel report from three source files without touching a terminal, use cowork.

2654
03:52:17,678 --> 03:52:22,788
如今很大一部分 AI 使用中的阻碍并非仅仅来自模型质量问题。
A large percentage of AI friction today doesn't come from model quality alone.

2655
03:52:23,150 --> 03:52:25,892
而是源于将工作分配到了错误的工具上。
It comes from routing the work to the wrong tool.

2656
03:52:26,638 --> 03:52:33,904
了解该选择哪个工具本身就是一项技能，而且这项技能在整个课程以及以后都会对你很有帮助。
Understanding which surface to reach for is itself a skill, and one that will serve you throughout this course and beyond.

2657
03:52:34,286 --> 03:52:42,224
在接下来的课程中，我们将进入 Claude Code 的领域，因为那是开发者的主战场，也是最强大、
For the rest of this course, we're firmly in clawed code territory because that's where developers live, and that's where the most powerful,

2658
03:52:42,544 --> 03:52:45,156
精准且可扩展的工作发生的领域。
precise, and extensible work happens.

2659
03:52:45,870 --> 03:52:51,904
但了解 Co-work 和 chat 的定位，能帮你全面理解 Anthropic 构建的整个体系。
But knowing where cowork and chat sit helps you understand the full picture of what Anthropic has built.

2660
03:52:52,064 --> 03:52:56,228
好了，既然我们知道了它是什么，现在来聊聊它为什么重要。
Okay, so now that we know what it is, let's talk about why it matters.

2661
03:52:56,558 --> 03:53:00,388
我希望在这里给你一个真实的答案，而不仅仅是些流行词汇。
And I want to give you a real answer here, not just buzzwords.

2662
03:53:01,294 --> 03:53:03,104
软件开发面临一个问题。
Software development has a problem.

2663
03:53:03,374 --> 03:53:06,544
这不是人才短缺问题，而是规模问题。
It's not a talent problem, it's a scale problem.

2664
03:53:07,054 --> 03:53:15,620
对可用软件、自动化工具、内部工具、面向客户的产品、集成、数据流水线的需求
The demand for working software, automations, internal tools, customer facing products, integrations, data pipelines

2665
03:53:15,984 --> 03:53:20,100
已经完全超过了能够构建这些产品的工程师数量。
has completely outpaced the number of engineers available to build it.

2666
03:53:20,750 --> 03:53:26,116
现在，无论属于哪个行业，每家公司在某种程度上都是一家软件公司。
Every company, regardless of industry, is now a software company in some way.

2667
03:53:26,478 --> 03:53:30,340
而且大多数公司根本无法通过单纯招聘来解决积压的任务。
And most of them simply cannot hire their way out of the backlog.

2668
03:53:31,150 --> 03:53:34,948
Claude Code 同时从两个方向解决了这个问题。
Cloud Code addresses this in two directions simultaneously.

2669
03:53:35,566 --> 03:53:39,492
对于经验丰富的工程师，它去除了机械性的开销。
For experienced engineers, it removes the mechanical overhead.

2670
03:53:39,918 --> 03:53:47,556
重复的重构、样板代码、调试循环、文档编写，所有这些都可以交给它来处理。
The repetitive refactors, the boilerplate, the debugging loops, the documentation, all of that gets delegated.

2671
03:53:48,014 --> 03:53:57,476
工程师可以处于更高的维度，专注于架构和产品思维，而不是陷入到实现细节中。
Engineers can operate at a much higher level, focusing on architecture and product thinking rather than getting bogged down in implementation details.

2672
03:53:58,126 --> 03:54:02,820
在 Anthropic 公司内部，大部分代码现在都是由 Claude Code 编写的。
At Anthropic itself, the majority of code is now written by Cloud Code.

2673
03:54:03,342 --> 03:54:11,440
工程师专注于架构、产品思维和持续编排，并行管理多个智能体，
Engineers focus on architecture, product thinking, and continuous orchestration, managing multiple agents in parallel,

2674
03:54:11,662 --> 03:54:15,812
提供方向，并做出决定来塑造最终构建的内容。
giving direction, and making the decisions that shape what gets built.

2675
03:54:16,142 --> 03:54:19,972
对于非工程人员来说，Claude Code 是真正的变革性工具。
For non-engineers, Cloud Code is genuinely transformational.

2676
03:54:20,558 --> 03:54:28,900
对于没有工程背景的开发者来说，Claude Code 提供了一个直到最近才存在的软件开发切入点。
For builders without an engineering background, Cloud Code is an entry point to software development that simply didn't exist until recently.

2677
03:54:29,454 --> 03:54:37,476
产品经理、创始人和运营团队现在只需用通俗语言描述结果，就能构建出可用的工具。
Product managers, founders, and operations teams are now building working tools just by describing outcomes in plain language.

2678
03:54:37,998 --> 03:54:39,620
而且数据也支持这一点。
And the numbers back this up.

2679
03:54:40,270 --> 03:54:47,040
RAMP 将 Claude Code 集成到他们的开发工作流中，并将故障排查时间缩短了 80%。
RAMP integrated Claud Code into their development workflow and cut incident investigation time by 80%.

2680
03:54:48,110 --> 03:54:57,508
销售、风险和财务等非工程团队现在使用自然语言查询数据仓库，而不是编写 SQL。
Non-engineering teams across sales, risk, and finance now query their data warehouse using natural language instead of writing SQL.

2681
03:54:58,126 --> 03:55:04,580
在 Racketton，新功能的平均交付时间从 24 个工作日缩短到了 5 天。
At Racketton, the average delivery time for new features dropped from 24 working days to 5.

2682
03:55:05,166 --> 03:55:06,852
这些不是微小的提升。
These are not marginal gains.

2683
03:55:07,278 --> 03:55:10,852
这些是足以改变公司组织架构的数据。
These are the kinds of numbers that change how companies are structured.

2684
03:55:11,182 --> 03:55:12,880
这就是 Claude Code 如此重要的原因。
That's why Claude Code matters.

2685
03:55:13,040 --> 03:55:14,340
现在让我们进入实操环节。
Now let's get practical.

2686
03:55:14,734 --> 03:55:17,092
你究竟能用 Claude Code 做些什么？
What can you actually do with Claude Code?

2687
03:55:17,838 --> 03:55:25,188
我想带大家了解四个主要的应用领域，因为这将决定你如何在自己的工作中思考如何使用它。
I want to walk you through four major application areas because this shapes how you'll think about using it in your own work.

2688
03:55:26,382 --> 03:55:28,932
应用领域 1：自动化。
Application Area 1, automation.

2689
03:55:29,678 --> 03:55:31,044
这是最重要的一个。
This is the big one.

2690
03:55:31,598 --> 03:55:36,388
想想软件工作流中所有那些必要但枯燥的任务。
Think about all the tasks in a software workflow that are necessary but tedious.

2691
03:55:37,230 --> 03:55:45,120
设置 CI/CD 流水线、编写数据库迁移、为新服务生成样板代码，
Setting up CI slash CD pipelines, writing database migrations, generating boilerplate for new services,

2692
03:55:45,454 --> 03:55:47,044
管理 Git 工作流。
managing Git workflows.

2693
03:55:47,694 --> 03:55:49,860
Claude Code 可以处理所有这些。
Cloud code can handle all of this.

2694
03:55:50,478 --> 03:55:54,020
你描述你想要的自动化，它就会去执行。
You describe the automation you want and it executes it.

2695
03:55:54,798 --> 03:56:02,340
你可以配置一次例程，它就可以按计划运行、通过 API 调用或响应特定事件来运行。
You can configure a routine once and it runs on a schedule, from an API call or in response to an event.

2696
03:56:03,150 --> 03:56:06,884
这是去除了重复部分的软件工程。
This is software engineering with the repetitive parts removed.

2697
03:56:08,302 --> 03:56:11,300
应用领域 2：编程辅助。
Application Area 2, coding assistance.

2698
03:56:12,014 --> 03:56:16,548
这是一个经典的用例，但它比简单的自动补全要深入得多。
This is the classic use case, but taken much further than autocomplete.

2699
03:56:17,390 --> 03:56:26,628
当你处理一个不是你写的庞大代码库时，Claude Code 可以为你导航，追踪依赖关系，解释模块如何连接，
When you're working in a large code base you didn't write, Claude Code can navigate it for you, tracing dependencies, explaining how modules connect,

2700
03:56:26,960 --> 03:56:29,828
并找出执行特定任务所需的正确文件。
identifying the right files for specific tasks.

2701
03:56:30,446 --> 03:56:38,560
它能读取文档文件，识别特定任务的相关文件，解释数据流水线的依赖关系，
It reads documentation files, identifies relevant files for specific tasks, explains data pipeline dependencies,

2702
03:56:38,894 --> 03:56:44,196
并帮助新团队成员理解哪些上游数据源提供给仪表板。
and helps new team members understand which upstream sources feed into dashboards.

2703
03:56:45,006 --> 03:56:49,188
这可以取代传统的数据目录和可发现性工具。
This can replace traditional data catalogs and discoverability tools.

2704
03:56:50,286 --> 03:56:51,876
应用领域 3。
Application Area 3.

2705
03:56:52,320 --> 03:56:54,980
开发环境中的内容生成。
Content generation in a development context.

2706
03:56:55,566 --> 03:56:57,440
这不仅仅是营销文案。
This isn't just a marketing copy.

2707
03:56:57,806 --> 03:57:05,680
在开发语境下，内容生成意味着自动从代码中生成文档、编写测试用例，
In a dev context, content generation means generating documentation automatically from code, writing test cases,

2708
03:57:05,966 --> 03:57:11,460
生成错误信息和面向用户的字符串，起草技术规范。
producing error messages and user-facing strings, drafting technical specifications.

2709
03:57:12,174 --> 03:57:21,284
Claude Code 可以读取你的代码库并根据上下文生成所有这些内容，不是泛泛而谈，而是针对你实际的代码进行专门调整。
Clawed code can read your code base and generate all of this contextually, not generically, but specifically tuned to your actual code.

2710
03:57:22,222 --> 03:57:23,908
应用领域 4。
Application Area 4.

2711
03:57:24,270 --> 03:57:25,508
业务工作流。
Business workflows.

2712
03:57:26,126 --> 03:57:28,708
这是最常让人们感到惊讶的一项。
This is the one that often surprises people.

2713
03:57:29,166 --> 03:57:37,600
原本由少数工程师掌握的关于系统和架构的深层知识，现在通过 Claude 可以让整个团队共享。
Deep knowledge of systems and architecture that was previously held by a few engineers becomes accessible to the whole team with Claude

2714
03:57:37,760 --> 03:57:38,116
代码。
Code.

2715
03:57:38,734 --> 03:57:48,000
业务团队、销售、财务、运营部门都在使用 Claude Code 来构建自己的轻量级工具，查询内部数据库，
Business teams, sales, finance, operations, are using Claude Code to build their own light tooling, query internal databases,

2716
03:57:48,302 --> 03:57:53,476
并自动化那些以前需要提交开发申请并等待两周才能完成的工作流。
and automate workflows that previously required a developer ticket and a two week wait.

2717
03:57:54,414 --> 03:58:00,964
“我有一个工具的想法”和“我拥有这个工具”之间的障碍已经消失了。
The barrier between I have an idea for a tool and I have the tool has collapsed.

2718
03:58:01,184 --> 03:58:07,908
大多数使用 AI 编程工具的人，包括经验丰富的开发人员，都把它们当成黑盒。
Most people who use AI coding tools, including experienced developers, treat them like a black box.

2719
03:58:08,302 --> 03:58:10,944
你输入一些内容，然后得到一些结果。
You type something in, something comes out.

2720
03:58:11,246 --> 03:58:16,004
你要么用它，要么不用，而你完全不知道中间发生了什么。
You use it or you don't, and you have no idea what happened in between.

2721
03:58:16,398 --> 03:58:23,972
这种做法在某些情况下行得通，但在另一些时候不行。直到 Claude 给你的代码看起来完全正确，但却隐藏着细微的 Bug 时。
That works until it doesn't. Until Claude gives you code that looks completely right but has a subtle bug baked in.

2722
03:58:24,494 --> 03:58:29,956
直到一段长对话突然丢失了五分钟前的上下文时。
Until a long conversation suddenly loses track of context it had five minutes ago.

2723
03:58:30,446 --> 03:58:35,876
直到一个精心设计的提示词给了你模糊的结果，而你期望的是精确的内容时。
Until a well-crafted prompt gives you something vague when you expect something precise.

2724
03:58:36,622 --> 03:58:42,500
在所有这些时刻，把 Claude 当成黑盒的人只会耸耸肩然后重试。
In all of those moments, people who treat Claude as a black box just shrug and try again.

2725
03:58:42,926 --> 03:58:47,076
他们没有办法诊断、调整或改进正在发生的情况。
They have no way to diagnose, adjust, or improve what's happening.

2726
03:58:47,534 --> 03:58:51,748
那些真正理解架构的人，他们的调试方式不同。
The people who do understand the architecture, they debug differently.

2727
03:58:52,110 --> 03:58:53,572
他们的提示词也不同。
They prompt differently.

2728
03:58:53,966 --> 03:58:56,036
他们设计的工作流也不同。
They design their workflows differently.

2729
03:58:56,430 --> 03:58:58,944
他们不与工具对抗，而是与它协作。
They don't fight the tool, they work with it.

2730
03:58:59,246 --> 03:59:03,172
Claude 系统架构概览，高层视角。
Overview of Cloud System Architecture, the high-level view.

2731
03:59:03,374 --> 03:59:05,668
让我们先从宏观层面开始。
Let's start by zooming all the way out.

2732
03:59:06,190 --> 03:59:13,604
当你使用 Claude Code 时，你可能会想象自己是在直接与运行在某处服务器上的巨大大脑对话。
When you use Cloud Code, you might imagine that you're talking directly to some giant brain sitting on a server somewhere.

2733
03:59:14,254 --> 03:59:18,628
这种直觉是合理的，但现实情况比这要复杂得多。
It's a reasonable intuition, but the reality is more layered than that.

2734
03:59:19,150 --> 03:59:22,596
理解这些层级将对你非常有帮助。
And understanding those layers will serve you enormously.

2735
03:59:23,374 --> 03:59:34,980
Claude Code 通过客户端-服务器架构运行，它在你的开发机器上本地运行，同时与 Anthropic 的 API 通信来进行实际的 AI 处理。
Cloud Code operates through a client-server architecture that runs locally on your developer machine while communicating with Anthropics API for the actual AI processing.

2736
03:59:35,630 --> 03:59:43,748
所以这里有两个截然不同的世界：在你机器上发生的一切，以及在 Anthropic 云端发生的一切。
So there are two distinct worlds at play here: everything happening on your machine and everything happening in Anthropics Cloud.

2737
03:59:44,078 --> 03:59:52,544
在你的机器上，Claude Code 执行大量的确定性的非 AI 工作，比如读取文件、管理权限，
On your machine, Cloud Code is doing a lot of deterministic non-AI work, reading your files, managing permissions,

2738
03:59:52,878 --> 03:59:58,404
进行工具调用路由，跟踪对话状态，并执行安全边界。
routing tool calls, tracking conversation state, and enforcing safety boundaries.

2739
03:59:59,246 --> 04:00:05,444
在 Claude Code 的代码库中，只有大约 1.6% 是真正的 AI 决策逻辑。
Only about 1.6% of Cloud Code's code base is actual AI decision logic.

2740
04:00:05,934 --> 04:00:14,784
剩下的 98.4% 是确定性的基础设施、权限网关、上下文管理、工具路由，
The remaining 98.4% is deterministic infrastructure, permission gates, context management, tool routing,

2741
04:00:14,958 --> 04:00:16,064
以及恢复逻辑。
and recovery logic.

2742
04:00:16,302 --> 04:00:18,500
这个数字值得我们停下来思考一下。
That's a number worth sitting with for a moment.

2743
04:00:18,894 --> 04:00:22,084
AI 大脑实际上只是一个相对很小的部分。
The AI brain is actually a relatively small piece.

2744
04:00:22,606 --> 04:00:30,704
工程上的复杂性存在于它周围的系统中，即信息如何被收集、组织、打包、发送，
The engineering complexity lives in the systems around it, how information is gathered, organized, packaged, sent,

2745
04:00:30,958 --> 04:00:32,708
接收并执行。
received, and acted upon.

2746
04:00:33,422 --> 04:00:37,316
理解这些系统是成为高级用户的关键。
Understanding those systems is what makes you a power user.

2747
04:00:37,742 --> 04:00:41,028
该系统分解为七个主要组件。
The system decomposes into seven main components.

2748
04:00:41,678 --> 04:00:50,304
从用户界面层（即你的终端或集成开发环境），到接口层，再到智能体循环，到权限
The user interface layer, which is your terminal or IDE, to the interfaces layer, to the agent loop, to the permission

2749
04:00:50,624 --> 04:00:57,956
系统，到工具层，到状态和持久化，最后是执行环境。
system, to the tools layer, to state and persistence to, and finally the execution environment.

2750
04:00:58,382 --> 04:01:01,060
把它想象成一场组织良好的接力赛。
Think of it like a well-organized relay race.

2751
04:01:01,518 --> 04:01:10,624
你把接力棒（也就是你的请求）交给第一名跑者，它经过每一个站点，在每一步都被处理和丰富，
You hand a baton, your request, to the first runner, and it passes through each station, getting processed and enriched at each step

2752
04:01:10,862 --> 04:01:13,508
直到最终结果交到你手中。
before the final output is handed back to you.

2753
04:01:13,904 --> 04:01:16,064
没有任何一个站点承担所有工作。
No single station does everything.

2754
04:01:16,366 --> 04:01:18,384
每个环节都有非常具体的工作。
Each has a very specific job.

2755
04:01:18,544 --> 04:01:22,820
在学习这个模块时，需要记住的一个核心架构见解是：
The key architecture insight to hold on to as we go through this module

2756
04:01:23,470 --> 04:01:25,664
Claude Code 不仅仅是一个模型。
Claude Code is not just a model.

2757
04:01:25,934 --> 04:01:29,860
它是一个模型加上围绕它构建的复杂框架。
It is a model plus a sophisticated harness built around it.

2758
04:01:30,574 --> 04:01:33,988
模型负责推理，而框架负责处理其他所有事情。
The model reasons, the harness does everything else.

2759
04:01:34,702 --> 04:01:45,028
正是这个框架让模型在真实的开发环境中变得安全、可预测且强大。现在，让我们用具体的术语来追踪请求在流水线中的流转。
And the harness is what makes the model safe, predictable, and powerful in a real developer environment. Now let's trace a request through that pipeline in concrete terms.

2760
04:01:45,742 --> 04:01:52,196
我想带你详细了解从你按下回车键到 Claude 做出响应的每一个瞬间发生了什么。
I want to walk you through exactly what happens from the moment you press enter to the moment Claude responds.

2761
04:01:53,454 --> 04:01:54,224
第一步。
Step 1.

2762
04:01:54,478 --> 04:01:55,684
输入捕获。
Input Capture.

2763
04:01:56,238 --> 04:01:58,756
你输入一条自然语言指令。
You type a natural language instruction.

2764
04:01:59,054 --> 04:02:06,468
比方说，重构身份验证模块，改用 JWT 标记而不是会话 Cookie。
Let's say, refactor the authentication module to use JWT tokens instead of session cookies.

2765
04:02:07,182 --> 04:02:10,084
Claude Code 立即开始收集上下文。
Claude code immediately starts gathering context.

2766
04:02:10,638 --> 04:02:19,140
它不只是孤立地接收你的句子，还会读取你的 Claude.md 配置文件，以了解项目的规范。
It doesn't just take your sentence in isolation, it reads your Claude.md configuration file to understand your project's conventions.

2767
04:02:19,694 --> 04:02:22,224
它会识别代码库中相关的相关文件。
It identifies relevant files in your code base.

2768
04:02:22,702 --> 04:02:24,996
它会查看最近的对话历史。
It looks at recent conversation history.

2769
04:02:25,326 --> 04:02:28,452
它还会调取你配置过的任何工具或权限。
It pulls in any tools or permissions you've configured.

2770
04:02:28,784 --> 04:02:33,184
所有这些内容都会被打包成一个包，发送给模型。
All of this is assembled together into a package that will be sent to the model.

2771
04:02:33,774 --> 04:02:34,464
第二步。
Step 2.

2772
04:02:34,766 --> 04:02:35,844
分词。
Tokenization.

2773
04:02:36,430 --> 04:02:46,660
在任何内容被处理之前，你的输入、文本、代码和上下文都必须转换成模型可以处理的格式，
Before anything can be processed, your input, your text, your code, your context has to be converted into a format the model can actually work with,

2774
04:02:46,990 --> 04:02:47,584
也就是标记。
tokens.

2775
04:02:47,854 --> 04:02:56,804
我们会在下一个话题深入探讨标记，但你只需要知道，在这个阶段，人类可读的文本变成了序列化的数字标记，
We'll go deep on tokens in the next topic, but just know at this stage, your human readable text becomes a sequence of numerical tokens,

2776
04:02:57,230 --> 04:02:59,876
而这个序列就是进入模型的内容。
and that sequence is what enters the model.

2777
04:03:01,262 --> 04:03:02,064
第三步。
Step 3.

2778
04:03:02,384 --> 04:03:04,064
向模型发起 API 调用。
API call to the model.

2779
04:03:05,358 --> 04:03:11,140
你的机器通过网络调用，将这个打包好的上下文发送到 Anthropic 的 API。
Your machine sends this packaged context to Anthropic's API over a network call.

2780
04:03:11,918 --> 04:03:21,028
API 对请求进行身份验证，并将其路由到相应的模型，大多数任务由 ClaudeSonnet 处理，最复杂的推理则交给 OPIS，
The API authenticates the request, routes it to the appropriate model, ClaudeSonnet for most tasks, OPIS for the heaviest reasoning,

2781
04:03:21,358 --> 04:03:22,948
然后开始处理。
and begins processing.

2782
04:03:23,950 --> 04:03:27,588
第四步，模型处理，即 AI 层。
Step four, model processing, the AI layer.

2783
04:03:28,398 --> 04:03:31,184
这是真正产生智能的地方。
This is where the actual intelligence happens.

2784
04:03:31,406 --> 04:03:37,636
模型会同时处理所有这些标记，不是一个词一个词地处理，而是全部一次性处理，
The model processes all those tokens simultaneously, not word by word, but all at once,

2785
04:03:38,286 --> 04:03:45,284
它利用一种叫做注意力机制的机制，来判断输入中的哪些部分彼此最相关。
using a mechanism called attention, where it figures out which parts of the input are most relevant to each other.

2786
04:03:45,934 --> 04:03:53,984
它逐个生成响应标记，每个标记都根据前面的所有内容，选择出最可能且最合适的那个。
It generates a response token by token, each token chosen based on what's most likely and most appropriate

2787
04:03:54,222 --> 04:03:55,824
基于之前的所有信息。
given everything before it.

2788
04:03:56,206 --> 04:04:01,904
特别是对于 Claude Code，这个处理步骤通常涉及多次迭代。
For Claude Code specifically, this processing step often involves more than one pass.

2789
04:04:02,446 --> 04:04:06,404
Claude Code 的智能体循环是一个“收集、行动、验证”的循环。
Claude Code's agent loop is a gather act verify cycle.

2790
04:04:06,862 --> 04:04:15,184
模型收集上下文，执行任务，然后验证结果，不断重复这个循环直到任务完成。
The model gathers context, acts on the task, then verifies the result, repeating this loop until the task is complete

2791
04:04:15,438 --> 04:04:17,184
或者它需要向你确认。
or it needs to check in with you.

2792
04:04:17,678 --> 04:04:18,464
第 5 步。
Step 5.

2793
04:04:18,830 --> 04:04:20,900
输出生成和工具调用。
Output generation and tool use.

2794
04:04:21,454 --> 04:04:27,492
模型原始输出从 API 返回，但 Claude Code 不只是简单地显示它。
The model's raw output comes back from the API, but Claude code doesn't just display it.

2795
04:04:27,822 --> 04:04:38,864
它会判断模型是想采取行动、运行命令、编辑文件还是读取另一个文件；如果是这样，它就会通过相应的工具执行该操作。
It interprets whether the model wants to take an action, run a command, edit a file, read another file, and if so, it executes that action through the appropriate tool.

2796
04:04:39,024 --> 04:04:43,748
该工具调用的结果会重新进入上下文，循环继续进行。
The result of that tool call goes back into the context and the loop continues.

2797
04:04:44,686 --> 04:04:45,664
第 6 步。
Step 6.

2798
04:04:46,126 --> 04:04:47,748
结果交付给你。
Output delivered to you.

2799
04:04:48,366 --> 04:04:58,116
一旦智能体循环到达停止点（任务已完成或 Claude 需要你的输入），最终响应就会在你的终端或集成开发环境中渲染出来。
Once the agent loop reaches a stopping point, either the task is done or Claude needs your input, the final response is rendered in your terminal or IDE.

2800
04:04:58,670 --> 04:05:00,804
文件更改会显示差异。
Diffs are shown for file changes.

2801
04:05:01,358 --> 04:05:03,844
命令在执行前会进行预览。
Commands are previewed before execution.

2802
04:05:04,270 --> 04:05:05,892
你进行查看并确认。
You review and approve.

2803
04:05:06,286 --> 04:05:15,204
这整个包含六个步骤的旅程，可能涉及你的机器与 API 之间的多次往返，但对于大多数任务来说，只需几秒钟。
That entire six-step journey, which can involve multiple round trips between your machine and the API, happens in seconds for most tasks

2804
04:05:15,504 --> 04:05:18,628
而对于复杂的、多步骤的工作流，则需要几分钟。
and minutes for complex multi-step workflows.

2805
04:05:19,150 --> 04:05:25,732
理解这个流水线将帮助你写出更好的请求，并理解为什么 Claude 会以这种方式做出响应。
Understanding this pipeline is what will help you write better requests and understand why Claude responds the way it does.

2806
04:05:25,904 --> 04:05:29,732
理解标记、上下文窗口和响应。
Understanding tokens, context windows, and responses.

2807
04:05:30,446 --> 04:05:35,264
这是本模块中最具技术性的主题，也是最重要的主题之一。
This is the most technical topic in this module, and also one of the most important.

2808
04:05:36,046 --> 04:05:40,644
标记和上下文窗口是语言模型运行的基本原理。
Tokens and context windows are the physics of how language models work.

2809
04:05:41,102 --> 04:05:45,700
如果你忽视它们，就会不断遇到你无法理解的限制。
Ignore them and you'll constantly bump into limits you don't understand.

2810
04:05:46,222 --> 04:05:49,956
如果你理解了它们，你就能设计出更聪明的工作流。
Understand them, and you'll design much smarter workflows.

2811
04:05:50,862 --> 04:05:52,228
什么是标记？
What is a token?

2812
04:05:53,134 --> 04:05:58,788
LLM 处理语言的方式与人类处理语言的方式有本质不同。
The way LLMs process language is fundamentally different from the way humans do.

2813
04:05:59,470 --> 04:06:09,540
人类表达语言所使用的最小信息单位是单个字符，而 AI 模型使用的最小单位是标记。
Whereas the smallest unit of information humans use to represent language is a single character, the smallest unit that AI models use is a token,

2814
04:06:09,902 --> 04:06:15,876
根据上下文的不同，一个标记可以是一个单词、一个词的一部分，甚至只是一个字符。
which can be a word, part of a word, or even just a character, depending on the context.

2815
04:06:16,750 --> 04:06:18,660
这里有一个实用的经验法则。
Here's the practical rule of thumb.

2816
04:06:19,118 --> 04:06:25,860
在英语中，一个标记大约是三个到四个字符，或者大约是一个单词的四分之三。
In English, one token is roughly three to four characters, or about three-quarters of a word.

2817
04:06:26,382 --> 04:06:29,252
所以「重构」可能占用两个标记。
So refactoring might be two tokens.

2818
04:06:29,744 --> 04:06:32,196
「JWT」可能占用一个。
JWT might be one.

2819
04:06:32,718 --> 04:06:36,868
一行完整的 Python 代码可能包含 10 到 15 个标记。
A full line of Python code might be 10 to 15 tokens.

2820
04:06:37,344 --> 04:06:41,984
一段文字可能包含 150 到 200 个标记。
A paragraph of text might be 150 to 200 tokens.

2821
04:06:42,254 --> 04:06:47,396
为了训练模型以理解语言，每个标记都会被分配一个 ID 编号。
To train a model to understand language, each token is assigned an ID number.

2822
04:06:47,918 --> 04:06:54,436
这些 ID 编号而不是单词本身，才是模型在内部实际处理的内容。
These ID numbers, rather than the words themselves, are what the model actually processes internally.

2823
04:06:55,086 --> 04:07:02,116
这种分词方式显著降低了处理和学习文本所需的计算能力。
This tokenization significantly reduces the computational power needed to process and learn from text.

2824
04:07:02,926 --> 04:07:05,104
这对你在实际操作中有什么影响呢？
Why does this matter for you practically?

2825
04:07:05,518 --> 04:07:09,092
因为你的账单是按标记计费的，而且你受到标记数量的限制。
Because you're billed in tokens and you're limited by tokens.

2826
04:07:09,646 --> 04:07:12,036
每一项输入的标记都会产生费用。
Every token of input costs something.

2827
04:07:12,462 --> 04:07:14,704
每一项输出的标记也会产生费用。
Every token of output costs something.

2828
04:07:14,926 --> 04:07:21,156
而且单次请求能容纳的标记总数受到所谓的「上下文窗口」的限制。
And the total number of tokens that can fit in a single request is bounded by something called the context window.

2829
04:07:21,646 --> 04:07:23,492
什么是上下文窗口？
What is a context window?

2830
04:07:24,046 --> 04:07:31,972
上下文窗口是 LLM 在单次交互中能够处理和参考的文本或信息的最大量。
A context window is the maximum amount of text or information an LLM can process and reference in a single interaction.

2831
04:07:32,782 --> 04:07:36,100
包括你提供的输入以及它生成的输出。
Both the input you provide and the output it generates.

2832
04:07:36,878 --> 04:07:39,204
你可以把它理解为模型的「工作记忆」。
Think of it as the model's working memory.

2833
04:07:39,822 --> 04:07:47,076
任何超出这个窗口的内容，对于模型来说都不存在，无论它对你的任务有多相关。
Everything outside that window simply doesn't exist for the model, no matter how relevant it might be to your task.

2834
04:07:47,662 --> 04:07:50,340
让我用一个比喻来让你更好地理解这一点。
Let me give you an analogy that really lands this.

2835
04:07:51,150 --> 04:07:54,468
想象你是一名被聘请来翻新建筑的承包商。
Imagine you're a contractor brought in to renovate a building.

2836
04:07:54,944 --> 04:07:59,268
只不过你只能携带装在一个公文包里的文件。
Except you can only carry documents that fit in a single briefcase.

2837
04:07:59,950 --> 04:08:08,900
建筑蓝图、业主的笔记、当地建筑规范、之前的翻新报告，所有这些都必须装进那个公文包里。
The building's blueprints, the owner's notes, the local building codes, previous renovation reports, all of it has to fit in that briefcase.

2838
04:08:09,582 --> 04:08:12,964
任何放不进去的东西，你都无法获取。
Anything that doesn't fit, you have no access to.

2839
04:08:13,582 --> 04:08:15,824
那个公文包就是上下文窗口。
That briefcase is the context window.

2840
04:08:16,174 --> 04:08:22,784
目前的 Claude 模型支持高达 100 万个标记的上下文窗口，例如 Claude 3.5 系列。
Current CLOD models support a context window of up to 1 million tokens for the CLOD 4.6 series.

2841
04:08:22,944 --> 04:08:29,924
这听起来非常庞大，但考虑到，一个大型代码库很容易达到数十万行。
That sounds enormous, but consider, a large code base can easily run into the hundreds of thousands of lines.

2842
04:08:30,606 --> 04:08:34,884
一个包含数十份文件的深度研究项目可能会迅速超出这个限制。
A deep research project with dozens of documents can exceed this quickly.

2843
04:08:35,214 --> 04:08:42,596
上下文窗口总是有限的，而这一事实影响了你在使用 Claude Code 时做出的每一个架构决策。
Context windows are always finite, and that fact shapes every architectural decision you make when building with clawed code.

2844
04:08:42,958 --> 04:08:44,548
这是在边界处发生的情况。
Here's what happens at the boundary.

2845
04:08:45,006 --> 04:08:52,452
当对话的前部分掉出上下文窗口时，模型就不再拥有那些细节的活跃记忆了。
When earlier parts of a conversation fall outside the context window, the model no longer has those details in active memory.

2846
04:08:52,846 --> 04:09:03,428
它可能会根据当前视野中剩余的内容来推测之前发生的内容，但这种推断只是最好的猜测，而这正是误解和幻觉出现的地方。
It may infer what came before from what remains in view, but that inference is just a best guess, which is exactly where misunderstandings and hallucinations can creep in.

2847
04:09:03,950 --> 04:09:09,284
Claude Code 有一种特定的机制来优雅地处理这个问题，即「上下文压缩」。
Claude Code has a specific mechanism to handle this gracefully, context compaction.

2848
04:09:09,710 --> 04:09:20,784
在每次模型调用之前，Claude Code 会运行多达五层压缩，对旧的上下文进行总结和压缩，以确保最相关的信息留在活跃窗口内。
Before every model call, Claude Code runs up to five compaction layers, summarizing and compressing older context to keep the most relevant information within the active window.

2849
04:09:21,038 --> 04:09:27,344
这就是后台运作的系统，旨在防止你在任务中途触及硬性的上下文限制。
This is the system working behind the scenes to prevent you from hitting hard context limits mid task.

2850
04:09:28,046 --> 04:09:29,024
核心要点是什么？
The takeaway?

2851
04:09:29,358 --> 04:09:32,228
有意识地控制放入上下文的内容。
Be deliberate about what goes into your context.

2852
04:09:32,622 --> 04:09:36,516
除非确实需要，否则不要把整个代码库都丢给 Claude。
Don't dump your entire code base at Claude unless you need it to.

2853
04:09:36,942 --> 04:09:41,184
上下文越聚焦，回复就越好且越快。
The more focused your context, the better and faster the responses.

2854
04:09:41,424 --> 04:09:43,844
提示词在系统行为中的作用。
The role of prompts in system behavior.

2855
04:09:44,750 --> 04:09:48,260
现在我们来聊点直接影响你日常使用的内容。
Now we get to something that directly impacts your daily use.

2856
04:09:48,688 --> 04:09:49,316
就是提示词。
Prompts.

2857
04:09:49,902 --> 04:09:54,116
我想强调一个大多数人都忽略的区别。
And I want to make a distinction here that most people miss entirely.

2858
04:09:54,862 --> 04:10:02,308
当大多数人听到「提示词」时，他们想到的是自己输入的文字、提出的问题或给出的指令。
When most people hear prompt, they think of the message they type, the question they ask, the instructions they give.

2859
04:10:02,768 --> 04:10:04,324
那是用户提示词。
That's the user prompt.

2860
04:10:04,974 --> 04:10:12,448
但在 Claude 的架构中，实际上有三种不同类型的提示词，每种的作用都完全不同。
But in Claude's architecture, there are actually three distinct types of prompts, and each plays a very different role.

2861
04:10:12,718 --> 04:10:13,764
系统提示词。
The system prompt.

2862
04:10:14,478 --> 04:10:18,308
系统提示词是在任何用户交互开始前就设定的。
The system prompt is set before any user interaction begins.

2863
04:10:18,830 --> 04:10:27,716
它建立了基础规则，规定 Claude 在这个场景下的身份、它该做什么或不该做什么、以及它应该采用什么格式，
It establishes the foundational rules, who Claude is in this context, what it should and shouldn't do, what format it should use,

2864
04:10:28,078 --> 04:10:31,748
还有哪些工具可用，以及项目的上下文。
what tools are available, what the project context is.

2865
04:10:32,558 --> 04:10:38,148
在系统提示词中设定角色，可以让 Claude 的行为和语气更符合你的使用场景。
Setting a role in the system prompt focuses Claude's behavior and tone for your use case.

2866
04:10:38,830 --> 04:10:41,648
哪怕只有一句话，也能产生显著的差异。
Even a single sentence makes a meaningful difference.

2867
04:10:41,808 --> 04:10:50,852
如果系统提示词说你是一名精通金融服务 API 的高级 Python 工程师，Claude 的表现就会不同，
If the system prompt says you are a senior Python engineer specializing in financial services APIs, Claude will behave differently,

2868
04:10:51,248 --> 04:10:56,996
它会比完全没有系统提示词时更加专注、更稳健、也更精准。
more focused, more conservative, more precise, than if it had no system prompt at all.

2869
04:10:57,518 --> 04:11:02,212
在 Claude Code 中，系统提示词在每次会话中都会自动构建。
In Claude Code, the system prompt is constructed automatically every session.

2870
04:11:02,734 --> 04:11:11,268
它包含了你的 Claude.md 配置、可用的工具、项目上下文以及 Anthropic 的核心安全准则。
It includes your Claude.md configuration, the tools available, the project context, and Anthropics Core Safety Guidelines.

2871
04:11:11,566 --> 04:11:19,648
Claude Code 的完整系统提示词包含 24 个内置工具描述，以及用于规划、探索
Cloud Code's full system prompt includes 24 built-in tool descriptions, sub-agent prompts for planning, exploration,

2872
04:11:19,854 --> 04:11:32,932
和任务执行的子智能体提示词，再加上一系列用于安全审查、批量操作和 PR 审查等特定技能的提示词，所有这些都会在你发送第一条消息前动态组装。
and task execution, plus a library of specialized skill. prompts for things like security review, batch operations, and PR review, all assembled dynamically before your first message.

2873
04:11:33,422 --> 04:11:34,368
用户提示词。
The user prompt.

2874
04:11:34,862 --> 04:11:39,236
这就是你输入的文字，也就是指令、问题或任务。
This is your message, the instruction, question, or task you type.

2875
04:11:39,918 --> 04:11:44,356
这个提示词的质量直接决定了返回结果的质量。
The quality of this prompt directly determines the quality of what comes back.

2876
04:11:44,846 --> 04:11:47,876
模糊的用户提示词会产生模糊的回答。
A vague user prompt produces a vague response.

2877
04:11:48,494 --> 04:11:55,396
一个具体、结构清晰且有明确限制的用户提示词，能产出精准且可操作的回复。
A specific, well-structured user prompt with clear constraints produces a precise, actionable response.

2878
04:11:55,822 --> 04:11:59,972
当指令模糊时，Claude 默认会给出谨慎且保守的输出。
Claude defaults to cautious, hedged outputs when instructions are vague.

2879
04:12:00,430 --> 04:12:09,796
如果你不指定语气、长度或格式，你得到的回答虽然在技术上准确，但往往因为过于谨慎而无法直接使用。
If you do not specify a tone, length, or format, you will get responses that are technically accurate, but often too careful to be immediately useful.

2880
04:12:10,094 --> 04:12:12,580
明确性不是可有可无的选项。
Specificity is not a nice to have.

2881
04:12:13,006 --> 04:12:17,088
这就是能直接用的草稿和必须重写的草稿之间的区别。
It's the difference between a draft you can use and a draft you have to rewrite.

2882
04:12:17,390 --> 04:12:26,692
Anthropic 的官方文档显示，对于复杂的、包含多份文件的输入，将长篇参考资料放在提示词顶部
Anthropic's own documentation shows that for complex, multi-document inputs, placing long reference material at the top of the prompt

2883
04:12:27,088 --> 04:12:32,356
在你的实际查询之前，可以提高高达 30% 的回复质量。
before your actual query can improve response quality by up to 30%.

2884
04:12:33,582 --> 04:12:36,836
提示词内部的结构和位置非常重要。
Structure and placement inside your prompt matter.

2885
04:12:37,422 --> 04:12:40,228
助手提示词对话历史。
The Assistant Prompt Conversation History.

2886
04:12:41,006 --> 04:12:46,276
每当 Claude 回复时，该回复都会成为当前上下文的一部分。
Every time Claude responds, that response becomes part of the ongoing context.

2887
04:12:46,862 --> 04:12:55,172
完整的对话历史、你的消息以及 Claude 的回复，都会在后续的每一次交互中反馈给模型。
The full conversation history, your messages, and Claude's responses, is fed back into the model on every subsequent turn.

2888
04:12:55,918 --> 04:12:59,492
这就是 Claude 在整个会话中保持连贯性的方式。
This is how Claude maintains continuity across a session.

2889
04:13:00,078 --> 04:13:03,556
这也是为什么长对话可能会开始变差的原因。
It's also why long conversations can start to degrade.

2890
04:13:03,950 --> 04:13:11,012
对话历史会占用越来越多的上下文窗口，导致留给新信息的空间越来越少。
The conversation history consumes more and more of the context window, leaving less room for new information.

2891
04:13:11,598 --> 04:13:20,452
这里的实践经验是：不要把提示词看作一次性的问题，而要看作塑造持久工作关系的指令。
The practical lesson here: think of prompts not as one-off questions, but as instructions that shape a persistent working relationship.

2892
04:13:21,102 --> 04:13:24,292
一个精心设计的系统提示词能奠定基础。
A well crafted system prompt sets the foundation.

2893
04:13:24,750 --> 04:13:28,208
清晰、具体的用户提示词能提供明确的方向。
Clear, specific user prompts give precise directions.

2894
04:13:28,430 --> 04:13:33,444
而有意识地管理对话历史，可以让工作记忆保持整洁和聚焦。
And managing conversation history deliberately keeps the working memory clean and focused.

2895
04:13:33,648 --> 04:13:38,084
API 层、模型处理、输出生成。
API layer, model processing, output generation.

2896
04:13:39,182 --> 04:13:43,620
现在让我们更精确地看看这三个核心架构组件。
Let's now look at the three core architectural components more precisely.

2897
04:13:44,270 --> 04:13:49,860
这些是 Claude Code 流水线中每个请求都要经过的不同站点。
These are the distinct stations in Cloud Code's pipeline that every request passes through.

2898
04:13:50,670 --> 04:13:53,380
第一个组件，API 层。
Component one, the API layer.

2899
04:13:54,254 --> 04:13:59,172
API 层是你本地环境与 Anthropic 云端之间的网关。
The API layer is the gateway between your local environment and Anthropics Cloud.

2900
04:13:59,886 --> 04:14:03,460
Claude Code 通过客户端-服务器架构运行。
Cloud Code operates through a client-server architecture.

2901
04:14:03,918 --> 04:14:09,316
你的终端在本地运行，而繁重的处理过程则通过 API 在远程进行。
Your terminal runs locally while the heavy processing happens remotely through the API.

2902
04:14:09,998 --> 04:14:15,332
API 层负责身份验证，核实你的 API 密钥；
The API layer handles authentication, verifying your API key;

2903
04:14:15,744 --> 04:14:22,020
请求格式化，将你的标记、上下文和参数打包成正确的结构；
request formatting, packaging your tokens, context, and parameters into the correct structure;

2904
04:14:22,384 --> 04:14:26,532
速率限制，确保你的使用量在允许范围内；
rate limiting, ensuring your usage stays within allowed bounds;

2905
04:14:26,958 --> 04:14:31,744
以及路由，将你的请求定向到合适的模型和计算资源。
and routing, directing your request to the appropriate model and compute resources.

2906
04:14:31,950 --> 04:14:40,944
从开发者的角度来看，当你开始基于 Claude 构建自己的应用时，API 层也是你直接交互的部分，
From a developer perspective, the API layer is also what you interact with directly when you start building your own applications on top of Claude,

2907
04:14:41,294 --> 04:14:43,972
这部分内容我们将在后续模块中深入探讨。
which is something we'll get into in later modules.

2908
04:14:44,398 --> 04:14:55,044
API 支持通过程序查询模型的各项能力和标记限制，这样你就能构建出能智能适应模型处理能力的应用程序。
The API supports querying model capabilities and token limits programmatically, so you can build applications that adapt intelligently to what the model can handle.

2909
04:14:55,598 --> 04:14:58,180
第二个组件，模型处理。
Component 2, model processing.

2910
04:14:58,638 --> 04:15:00,292
这是智能层。
This is the intelligence layer.

2911
04:15:00,686 --> 04:15:09,412
当你的请求到达 Anthropic 服务器时，模型会利用其注意力机制并行处理整个标记序列，
Once your request arrives at anthropic servers, the model processes the entire token sequence in parallel using its attention mechanism,

2912
04:15:09,806 --> 04:15:16,356
本质上是判断输入中的哪些部分彼此相关，以及它们应如何影响输出。
essentially figuring out which parts of the input are relevant to each other and how they should inform the output.

2913
04:15:16,814 --> 04:15:28,484
对于 Claude 代码而言，这一层还支持深度思考，这是一种模型在生成最终回复前，在内部对复杂问题进行逻辑推理的模式。
For Claude code specifically, this layer also supports extended thinking, a mode where the model internally reasons through complex problems before generating its final response.

2914
04:15:29,198 --> 04:15:33,988
深度思考为 Claude 在处理复杂任务时提供了更强的推理能力。
Extended thinking gives CLOD enhanced reasoning capabilities for complex tasks.

2915
04:15:34,224 --> 04:15:42,980
模型会在内部进行逐步思考，你可以选择性地控制模型在回答前允许使用的思考预算，以标记为单位，
The model works through a step-by-step thought process internally, and you can optionally control how much thinking budget, measured in tokens,

2916
04:15:43,374 --> 04:15:46,052
模型在回答之前允许使用的（思考量）
the model is allowed to use before answering.

2917
04:15:46,958 --> 04:15:55,024
模型处理层也是模型决定是回复文本还是调用工具的地方，比如读取文件、
The model processing layer is also where the model decides whether to respond with text or call a tool, like reading a file,

2918
04:15:55,278 --> 04:15:58,756
运行终端命令或获取网页。
running a terminal command, or fetching a web page.

2919
04:15:59,470 --> 04:16:05,636
该决策会传回 API 层，由它将指令路由回你的机器执行。
That decision gets sent back to the API layer, which routes it back to your machine for execution.

2920
04:16:06,446 --> 04:16:07,620
组件 3。
Component 3.

2921
04:16:07,950 --> 04:16:09,348
输出生成。
Output generation.

2922
04:16:10,158 --> 04:16:19,664
输出生成是最后一个阶段，模型内部的表征会被转换回人类可读的文本或工具调用，
Output generation is the final stage where the model's internal representations are converted back into human readable text or tool calls

2923
04:16:19,886 --> 04:16:20,964
并交付给你。
and delivered to you.

2924
04:16:21,742 --> 04:16:24,996
Claude Code 提供三种主要的输出模式。
Claude Code provides three primary output modes.

2925
04:16:25,614 --> 04:16:35,460
用于直接命令行响应的终端输出，显示文件更改内容的 集成开发环境 内行差异，清晰展示新增和删除的部分，
Terminal output for direct command line responses, inline IDE diffs for file changes showing exactly what was added and removed,

2926
04:16:36,078 --> 04:16:43,824
以及在执行高风险或不可逆操作前暂停并请求你确认的交互式提示。
and interactive prompts that pause and ask for your approval before executing risky or irreversible actions.

2927
04:16:44,064 --> 04:16:48,228
这一层的一个关键特性是 Claude Code 流式传输响应。
A key behavior in this layer Claude code streams responses.

2928
04:16:48,942 --> 04:16:56,484
它不会等待整个响应生成后再显示，而是实时逐个标记地显示输出。
Rather than waiting for the entire response to be generated before displaying it, output appears token by token in real time.

2929
04:16:57,006 --> 04:17:00,068
这就是为什么你会看到 Claude 在打字回复的原因。
This is why you see Claude typing its responses.

2930
04:17:00,526 --> 04:17:06,372
它确实是在一次产生一个标记，而你的终端在接收到这些标记时立即显示它们。
It's literally generating one token at a time and your terminal is displaying them as they arrive.

2931
04:17:07,214 --> 04:17:09,092
架构局限性。
Limitations in architecture.

2932
04:17:12,944 --> 04:17:15,364
现在让我们来点实诚的聊聊。
Now let's have the honest conversation.

2933
04:17:15,854 --> 04:17:20,784
每个工具都有局限性，了解 Claude 的局限并不代表悲观。
Every tool has limitations, and understanding Clauds is not pessimistic.

2934
04:17:21,038 --> 04:17:22,148
这是一种专业态度。
It's professional.

2935
04:17:22,734 --> 04:17:26,660
明确边界在哪里，正是让你能够绕过这些限制的关键。
Knowing where the edges are is exactly what lets you work around them.

2936
04:17:27,214 --> 04:17:28,224
局限性一。
Limitation one.

2937
04:18:00,846 --> 04:18:03,748
这被称为「迷失在中间」效应。
This is called the lost in the middle effect.

2938
04:18:04,174 --> 04:18:14,660
当上下文非常长时，模型往往更关注开头和结尾的信息，而埋在中间的细节就会被忽略。
When a context is very long, the model tends to pay more attention to information at the very beginning and the very end, and the details buried in the middle get underweighted.

2939
04:18:14,926 --> 04:18:16,528
实际的影响是什么？
The practical implication?

2940
04:18:16,848 --> 04:18:19,248
更多的上下文并不总是更好的。
More context is not always better.

2941
04:18:19,566 --> 04:18:27,172
在处理编程任务时，如果 Claude 只需要三个文件，你却把整个代码库都塞给它，反而会降低输出质量。
For coding tasks, feeding Claude your entire code base when it only needs three files actually hurts output quality.

2942
04:18:27,694 --> 04:18:29,924
要精准筛选你要包含的内容。
Be surgical about what you include.

2943
04:18:30,350 --> 04:18:31,524
限制 2。
Limitation 2.

2944
04:18:31,822 --> 04:18:32,836
幻觉。
Hallucinations.

2945
04:18:33,390 --> 04:18:39,812
所谓幻觉，就是模型生成了看似很有把握但事实错误的信息。
Hallucinations are when a model generates information that is confidently stated but factually incorrect.

2946
04:18:40,142 --> 04:18:43,648
这可能是 AI 中被误解最严重的限制。
This is perhaps the most misunderstood limitation in AI.

2947
04:18:43,854 --> 04:18:50,820
幻觉是指 LLM 生成事实错误或毫无意义的回答的情况。
Hallucinations refer to instances when LLMs generate factually incorrect or nonsensical responses.

2948
04:18:51,310 --> 04:18:56,528
模型会用一个看似合理的猜测来填补空白，而不是承认自己不确定。
The model fills in the gap with a plausible guess rather than acknowledging uncertainty.

2949
04:18:56,878 --> 04:18:58,916
从架构上讲，这是由以下原因造成的。
Here's why this happens architecturally.

2950
04:18:59,278 --> 04:19:02,020
模型的本质是一个预测引擎。
The model is fundamentally a prediction engine.

2951
04:19:02,446 --> 04:19:06,608
它会根据之前出现的所有内容，预测最可能出现的下一个标记。
It predicts the most probable next token given everything that came before.

2952
04:19:06,862 --> 04:19:16,288
当它没有足够的信息来生成正确答案时，它仍会生成最可能的答案，这在表面上看起来可能完全正确。
When it doesn't have enough information to generate the correct answer, it still generates the most probable answer, which can look completely correct on the surface.

2953
04:19:16,528 --> 04:19:26,116
幻觉在检索增强场景中特别常见，即正确的答案存在于你的代码库中，但检索未能将其找出来。
Hallucinations are especially common in retrieval-augmented scenarios, where the correct answer exists in your code base, but retrieval fails to surface it.

2954
04:19:26,766 --> 04:19:29,668
模型默认不会说「我不知道」。
The model won't say I don't know by default.

2955
04:19:30,062 --> 04:19:33,828
它会根据训练中的模式给出一个自信的回答。
It will generate a confident answer based on patterns from training.

2956
04:19:34,510 --> 04:19:43,044
特别是在 Claude Code 中，这最常表现为自信地编写出调用不存在 API 的代码，
For clawed code specifically, this manifests most often as confidently writing code that uses an API that doesn't exist,

2957
04:19:43,728 --> 04:19:52,100
编造稍微有点错误的函数签名，或者对你的代码库做出与实际实现相矛盾的假设。
inventing function signatures that are slightly wrong, or making assumptions about your code base that contradict the actual implementation.

2958
04:19:52,782 --> 04:19:54,688
缓解方法始终如一。
The mitigation is always the same.

2959
04:19:55,150 --> 04:20:03,568
让 Claude 访问它真正需要的特定文件，在执行前检查输出，并使用 Claude Code 内置的
Give Claude access to the actual specific files it needs, review outputs before executing, and use Claude code's built-in

2960
04:20:03,728 --> 04:20:04,868
验证步骤。
verification steps.

2961
04:20:05,614 --> 04:20:06,884
限制 3。
Limitation 3.

2962
04:20:07,168 --> 04:20:07,940
延迟。
Latency.

2963
04:20:08,270 --> 04:20:16,068
从发送请求到接收响应之间的时间是一个真实的架构约束，它包含两个组成部分。
The time between sending a request and receiving a response is a real architectural constraint, and it has two components.

2964
04:20:16,910 --> 04:20:18,980
首先是网络延迟。
First, network latency.

2965
04:20:19,566 --> 04:20:23,716
你的请求从你的机器传输到 Anthropic 服务器再返回。
Your request travels from your machine to anthropic servers and back.

2966
04:20:24,366 --> 04:20:26,848
这通常很快，但并非零。
This is usually fast but not zero.

2967
04:20:27,088 --> 04:20:29,380
其次是计算延迟。
Second, computation latency.

2968
04:20:29,806 --> 04:20:38,372
模型处理你的标记并生成响应所需的时间，会随着任务的复杂度和上下文的长度而增加。
The time for the model to process your tokens and generate a response scales with the complexity of the task and the length of the context.

2969
04:20:39,278 --> 04:20:44,132
长上下文会增加延迟，因为模型必须处理更多的标记。
Large contexts increase latency because the model must attend to more tokens.

2970
04:20:45,166 --> 04:20:49,444
质量不会线性增长，但计算成本会。
Quality doesn't increase linearly, but computation cost does.

2971
04:20:50,062 --> 04:20:53,956
对于大多数交互式任务，延迟几乎感觉不到。
For most interactive tasks, latency is barely noticeable.

2972
04:20:54,382 --> 04:21:02,528
但对于耗时较长的智能体化任务，比如 Claude 需要执行多个步骤、调用多个工具、管理多个文件时，
But for long-running agentic tasks, where Claude is running multiple steps, calling multiple tools, managing multiple files,

2973
04:21:02,848 --> 04:21:04,132
延迟就会累积。
latency compounds.

2974
04:21:04,782 --> 04:21:10,276
一个包含 10 个步骤的任务，如果每步有 2 秒延迟，那么最少也要耗费 20 秒。
A 10-step task with two seconds of latency per step takes 20 seconds minimum.

2975
04:21:11,054 --> 04:21:14,084
针对这一问题的架构层面的对策就是并行处理。
The architectural response to this is parallelism.

2976
04:21:14,542 --> 04:21:22,688
与其执行一个长序列任务，经验丰富的 Claude Code 用户会将工作分解为并行的工作流，即同时运行多个 Claude
Rather than one long sequential task, experienced Claude code users break work into parallel work streams, multiple Claude

2977
04:21:22,848 --> 04:21:26,500
会话来处理代码库的不同部分。
sessions running simultaneously on different parts of a code base.

2978
04:21:27,214 --> 04:21:31,492
我们将在高级智能体化工作流模块中详细讲解这一点。
We'll cover that in detail in the modules on advanced agenc workflows.

2979
04:21:31,950 --> 04:21:37,604
到目前为止，你已经建立起了一个清晰且实用的心理模型，来理解 Claude Code 的实际运作方式。
By now, you've built a clear and practical mental model of how Claude Code actually works.

2980
04:21:38,286 --> 04:21:47,840
你明白它是一个客户端-服务器系统，其中本地设置与强大的远程模型进行通信，而大部分真正的编排、
You understand it as a client-server system, where a local setup communicates with a powerful remote model, while most of the real orchestration,

2981
04:21:48,160 --> 04:21:53,124
上下文处理、安全性和工具使用都在客户端侧完成。
context handling, safety, and tool usage happens on the client side.

2982
04:21:53,838 --> 04:22:03,812
你已经看到每一次交互都是遵循从输入到处理再到输出的流水线，并且明白为什么标记和上下文窗口决定了系统的限制。
You've seen how every interaction follows the input to processing to output pipeline, and why tokens and context windows define the system's limits.

2983
04:22:04,334 --> 04:22:06,500
让我先问你一个问题。
Let me ask you something right at the top.

2984
04:22:06,894 --> 04:22:18,480
你有没有在没读说明书的情况下使用过电动工具？比如圆锯、钻孔机或雕刻机，你边做边摸索，完成了任务，但内心深处
Have you ever used the power tool without reading the manual? A circular saw, a drill press, a router, and you kind of figured it out as you went, got something done, but deep down

2985
04:22:18,640 --> 04:22:21,028
你知道自己可能操作得并不完全正确。
you knew you were probably doing it wrong.

2986
04:22:21,614 --> 04:22:27,428
也许结果不错，也可能不理想，但你肯定没能充分发挥出工具的全部潜力。
Maybe it worked out, maybe it didn't, but you definitely weren't getting the most out of the tool.

2987
04:22:28,110 --> 04:22:31,108
这就是大多数人目前使用 Claude Code 的状态。
That's where most people are with Claude Code right now.

2988
04:22:31,630 --> 04:22:39,812
他们看过演示，尝试了一些提示词，得到了反馈，可能有些令人惊艳，也可能让人沮丧，
They've seen the demos, they've tried a few prompts, they got something back, maybe something impressive, maybe something frustrating,

2989
04:22:40,238 --> 04:22:43,332
但他们是凭直觉在操作，而不是基于理解。
but they're working from instinct, not understanding.

2990
04:22:43,918 --> 04:22:54,560
而这种直觉与理解之间的差距，正是区分那些只能获得 20% 生产力提升的开发者，和能获得 300% 提升的开发者的关键。
And that gap between instinct and understanding is exactly what separates developers who get a 20% productivity boost from developers who get a 300%

2991
04:22:54,880 --> 04:22:55,876
生产力提升。
productivity boost.

2992
04:22:56,430 --> 04:23:01,796
让我给你一个具体的、实操层面的完整 Claude Code 工作流图景。
Let me give you a concrete grounded picture of what a complete Cloud Code workflow looks like.

2993
04:23:02,254 --> 04:23:05,508
不是概念上的，而是实际操作层面的。
Not conceptually, but in real operational terms.

2994
04:23:06,030 --> 04:23:14,020
任何 Claude Code 工作流的三个核心组成部分是：定义目标的初始指令或提示词，
The three fundamental components of any Cloud Code workflow are the initial instruction or prompt that defines the goal,

2995
04:23:14,798 --> 04:23:19,332
Claude 用来收集上下文并采取行动的工具和连接，
the tools and connections that Claude uses to gather context and take action,

2996
04:23:20,206 --> 04:23:26,308
以及 Claude 评估中间输出并据此调整后续步骤的反馈循环。
and the feedback loop where Claude evaluates intermediate outputs and adjusts its next steps accordingly.

2997
04:23:26,606 --> 04:23:29,316
让我用一个真实的例子让它变得具体化。
Let me make that tangible with a real example.

2998
04:23:29,838 --> 04:23:33,840
这个例子直接源自 Claude Code 在生产环境中的实际表现。
One that comes straight from how Claude Code actually behaves in production.

2999
04:23:34,254 --> 04:23:38,596
你告诉 Claude Code，给登录处理程序添加输入验证。
You tell Claude Code, add input validation to the login handler.

3000
04:23:38,958 --> 04:23:39,940
这就是一句话。
That's one sentence.

3001
04:23:40,430 --> 04:23:41,764
这是实际发生的过程。
Here's what actually happens.

3002
04:23:42,414 --> 04:23:46,500
Claude Code 读取登录处理程序文件和相关的测试文件。
Claude Code reads the login handler file and the relevant test file.

3003
04:23:47,150 --> 04:23:51,524
它识别出缺失验证的位置以及输入的格式。
It identifies where validation is missing and the format of the inputs.

3004
04:23:52,174 --> 04:23:54,788
它提出一个差异并应用补丁。
It proposes a diff and applies the patch.

3005
04:23:55,310 --> 04:24:01,520
接着它运行测试，其中一项测试失败了，因为错误信息与预期的字符串不匹配。
It then runs the tests, and one test fails because the error message doesn't match the expected string.

3006
04:24:01,742 --> 04:24:04,804
它修复了错误消息并再次运行测试。
It fixes the error message and runs the tests again.

3007
04:24:05,326 --> 04:24:05,924
测试通过了。
They pass.

3008
04:24:06,510 --> 04:24:07,556
工作流停止。
The workflow stops.

3009
04:24:08,238 --> 04:24:16,036
这整个序列：读取、识别、提议、应用、测试、失败、修复，
That entire sequence, read, identify, propose, apply, test, fail, fix,

3010
04:24:16,400 --> 04:24:20,356
测试、完成，全都是由一个句子的提示词触发的。
test, done, happens from a single-sentence prompt.

3011
04:24:21,070 --> 04:24:22,692
这个提示词只有一行。
The prompt was one line.

3012
04:24:23,022 --> 04:24:27,364
执行过程包含五个步骤，中间还包含一个自我修正循环。
The execution was five steps with a self-correction loop in the middle.

3013
04:24:28,206 --> 04:24:29,680
现在有一点很重要。
Now here's something important.

3014
04:24:30,126 --> 04:24:33,600
最适合的 Claude 工作流取决于当前的任务。
The best type of Claude workflow depends on the task at hand.

3015
04:24:33,870 --> 04:24:42,052
对于像代码格式化或生成测试这样定义明确且可重复的任务，脚本化的确定性工作流效果最好。
For well-defined repeatable tasks like code formatting or test generation, a scripted deterministic workflow works best.

3016
04:24:42,798 --> 04:24:54,724
对于开放式研究或路径不明确的调试任务，智能体化工作流——即 Claude 根据中间结果动态选择工具并做出调整——
For open-ended research or debugging tasks where the path is not known in advance, an agentic workflow where Claude dynamically selects tools and adapts based on intermediate results

3017
04:24:55,040 --> 04:24:57,188
往往能产生更好的结果。
tends to produce the strongest outcomes.

3018
04:24:57,678 --> 04:25:05,360
这是一个关键的设计决策，你将不断面临：是脚本化的还是智能体化的，是确定性的还是自适应的。
This is a critical design decision you'll make constantly, scripted or agentic, deterministic or adaptive.

3019
04:25:05,678 --> 04:25:11,364
随着你建立起对 Claude 代码的直觉，你会对每项任务需要哪种模式产生感觉。
As you build your Claude code instincts, you'll develop a feel for which mode each task calls for.

3020
04:25:11,822 --> 04:25:14,276
但目前，核心原则是这个。
But for now, the key principle is this.

3021
04:25:14,830 --> 04:25:18,160
让工作流结构与任务的可预测性相匹配。
Match the workflow structure to the task's predictability.

3022
04:25:18,414 --> 04:25:21,604
如果你明确知道需要发生什么，就写成脚本。
If you know exactly what needs to happen, script it.

3023
04:25:22,094 --> 04:25:25,520
如果路径不确定，就给 Claude 留出探索的空间。
If the path is uncertain, give Claude room to explore.

3024
04:25:25,902 --> 04:25:34,884
不过有一种模式是通用的：在应用更改之前，增加差异审查步骤、空运行标志和确认关卡。
There's one pattern that applies universally though: a diff review step, a dry run flag, and a confirmation gate before changes are applied.

3025
04:25:35,406 --> 04:25:40,320
这些操作会稍微减慢工作流，但能在弱假设变成提交代码之前将其拦截。
These slow the workflow slightly but catch weak assumptions before they become commits.

3026
04:25:40,558 --> 04:25:44,100
在智能体系统中，检查点不是官僚主义。
In agencic systems, the checkpoint isn't bureaucracy.

3027
04:25:44,526 --> 04:25:49,060
它是人类判断与自动化执行相结合的地方。
It's the place where human judgment integrates with automated execution.

3028
04:25:49,742 --> 04:25:51,236
检查点是你的朋友。
The checkpoint is your friend.

3029
04:25:51,616 --> 04:25:54,976
任何涉及生产环境的操作，都千万不要跳过它。
Never skip it for anything that touches production.

3030
04:25:55,278 --> 04:26:02,564
现在让我们来看看精确的交互流程，即开发人员在 Claude Code 会话中经历的确切步骤序列。
Now let's walk through the precise interaction flow, the exact sequence of steps a developer goes through in a Claude Code session.

3031
04:26:03,182 --> 04:26:06,628
这就是处理每个任务时的实际体验。
This is what the experience looks like, task by task.

3032
04:26:07,246 --> 04:26:09,924
第一步，会话初始化。
Step one, session initialization.

3033
04:26:10,414 --> 04:26:15,812
当你在目录中启动 Claude Code 时，如果存在 Claude.md 文件，它会自动读取该文件。
When you start Claude code in a directory, it reads your Claude.md file if one exists.

3034
04:26:16,430 --> 04:26:18,852
这是你项目的持久上下文。
This is your project's persistent context.

3035
04:26:19,342 --> 04:26:26,116
包括代码风格规范、测试框架、构建命令以及你已经做出的架构决策。
Code style conventions, testing frameworks, build commands, architectural decisions you've already made.

3036
04:26:26,670 --> 04:26:36,836
运行 /init 会分析你的代码库，以检测构建系统、测试框架和代码模式，为你提供一个随着时间推移可以不断完善的坚实基础。
Running /init analyzes your code base to detect build systems, test frameworks, and code patterns, giving you a solid foundation that you refine over time.

3037
04:26:37,422 --> 04:26:39,492
这些前期设置工作会产生复利效果。
This is the setup work that compounds.

3038
04:26:40,046 --> 04:26:46,500
你今天添加到 Claude.md 中的每一条规则，都能让你在未来的每一次会话中都不需要重复解释。
Every rule you add to Claude.md today saves you from re-explaining it in every future session.

3039
04:26:46,958 --> 04:26:49,540
这里有一个简短但很重要的区别值得了解。
A quick but important distinction worth knowing.

3040
04:26:50,094 --> 04:26:53,220
Claude.md 是一个原生识别的文件。
Claude.md is a natively recognized file.

3041
04:26:53,710 --> 04:26:58,096
Claude code 在启动时会自动读取它，你不需要做任何操作。
Claude code automatically reads it on startup without you having to do anything.

3042
04:26:58,256 --> 04:27:06,468
像 spec.md 和 lessons.md 这些文件（我们稍后会讨论），是强大的开发者惯例，
Files like spec.md and lessons.md, which we'll discuss shortly, are powerful developer conventions,

3043
04:27:06,862 --> 04:27:08,576
但它们不会被自动摄入。
but they're not auto-ingested.

3044
04:27:08,878 --> 04:27:11,748
你只需要在会话中告诉 Claude 去读取它们。
You simply tell Claude to read them during your session.

3045
04:27:12,174 --> 04:27:15,076
效果是一样的，只是需要你多输入一行指令。
Same benefit, just one extra line from you.

3046
04:27:15,598 --> 04:27:26,816
把 Claude.md 看作是 Claude 的永久简报文件，而 spec.md 和 lessons.md 则像是你在开始每个相关任务时交给它的笔记。
Think of Claude.md as Claude's permanent briefing document, and spec.md and lessons.md as the notes you hand over at the start of each relevant task.

3047
04:27:27,214 --> 04:27:27,936
第二步。
Step 2.

3048
04:27:28,206 --> 04:27:29,380
任务范围界定。
Task scoping.

3049
04:27:29,742 --> 04:27:31,364
在执行之前先做计划。
Plan before you execute.

3050
04:27:31,758 --> 04:27:37,936
在你输入实际任务之前，最高效的 Claude code 用户会花 30 秒来界定任务范围。
Before you type the actual task, the most effective Claude code users spend 30 seconds scoping it.

3051
04:27:38,158 --> 04:27:41,444
对于较大的功能，让 Claude 先对你进行访谈。
For larger features, have Claude interview you first.

3052
04:27:42,094 --> 04:27:47,492
从一个简单的提示词开始，并要求 Claude 使用「Ask User Question」工具来采访你。
Start with a minimal prompt and ask Claude to interview you using the Ask User Question tool.

3053
04:27:47,918 --> 04:27:56,096
Claude 会询问一些你可能还没考虑到的问题：技术实现、UI 或 UX、边界情况，
Claude will ask about things you might not have considered yet: technical implementation, UI slash UX, edge cases,

3054
04:27:56,256 --> 04:27:57,092
以及权衡取舍。
and trade-offs.

3055
04:27:57,646 --> 04:28:00,580
继续访谈，直到涵盖所有内容为止。
Keep the interview going until you've covered everything.

3056
04:28:00,974 --> 04:28:05,380
然后让 Claude 将完整的规范写入一个 spec.md 文件。
Then have Claude write a complete spec to a spec.md file.

3057
04:28:05,774 --> 04:28:12,356
这是一个你明确要求 Claude 创建并引用的普通文件，而不是它自动管理的文件。
A plain file you explicitly ask Claude to create and reference, not one it manages automatically.

3058
04:28:12,718 --> 04:28:15,652
这是在 Claude Code 中最被低估的一种模式。
This is the most underused pattern in Claude Code.

3059
04:28:16,142 --> 04:28:18,948
大多数开发者只是输入一个模糊的任务然后祈祷。
Most developers type a vague task and hope.

3060
04:28:19,278 --> 04:28:25,764
优秀的开发者会将范围界定的对话视为一种投资，从而避免后续两小时的返工。
The best developers treat the scoping conversation as the investment that prevents two hours of rework later.

3061
04:28:26,286 --> 04:28:27,056
第三步。
Step 3.

3062
04:28:27,374 --> 04:28:28,676
检查计划模式。
Plan mode review.

3063
04:28:29,070 --> 04:28:40,256
对于复杂的任务，进入计划模式，通常在终端中按 Shift 加 Tab，不过具体的快捷键可能会根据你的终端模拟器和 Claude
For non-trivial tasks, enter plan mode, typically by pressing Shift plus Tab in the terminal, though exact key bindings can vary depending on your terminal emulator and Claude

3064
04:28:40,416 --> 04:28:41,124
版本而有所不同。
Code version.

3065
04:28:41,582 --> 04:28:44,576
所以如果出现异常行为，请查看当前的文档。
So check the current docs if it behaves unexpectedly.

3066
04:28:44,750 --> 04:28:51,812
在生产环境中最可靠的规划工作流是让 Claude 先起草计划，暂不进行任何实现。
The most reliable planning workflow in production is Ask Claude to draft the plan with no implementation yet.

3067
04:28:52,622 --> 04:28:57,028
在编辑器中打开该计划，并在 Claude 出错的地方标注出来。
Open the plan in your editor and annotate wherever Claude got something wrong.

3068
04:28:57,870 --> 04:29:01,700
把它发回去，并注明：处理所有备注，先不要执行代码。
Send it back with Address All Notes, Don't Implement Yet.

3069
04:29:02,446 --> 04:29:05,028
重复此过程，直到所有的决策都明确为止。
Repeat until every decision is resolved.

3070
04:29:05,646 --> 04:29:07,876
只有在那之后，才要求 Claude 进行实现。
Only then ask Claude to implement.

3071
04:29:08,142 --> 04:29:12,932
如果没有这个警示短语，Claude 就会跳过修改步骤，直接开始写代码。
Without that guard phrase, Claude will skip revision and start writing code immediately.

3072
04:29:13,422 --> 04:29:14,756
最后一点非常重要。
That last point matters.

3073
04:29:15,216 --> 04:29:18,212
「先不要执行」不是可选的措辞。
Don't implement yet is not optional phrasing.

3074
04:29:18,510 --> 04:29:20,096
这是一个行为指令。
It's a behavioral directive.

3075
04:29:20,256 --> 04:29:23,300
第四步，带检查点的执行。
Step four execution with checkpoints.

3076
04:29:24,334 --> 04:29:26,788
计划获批后，Claude 开始执行。
With the plan approved, Claude executes.

3077
04:29:27,310 --> 04:29:28,964
你会看到差异内容出现。
You watch the diffs appear.

3078
04:29:29,326 --> 04:29:30,948
你来确认文件的更改。
You approve file changes.

3079
04:29:31,374 --> 04:29:32,836
你来审核工具调用。
You review tool calls.

3080
04:29:33,486 --> 04:29:41,312
最擅长使用 Claude Code 的用户，包括 Claude Code 的开发者本人，都不会在每一个微小的
The most effective Claude Code users, including the creator of Cloud Code himself, don't babysit Claude through every micro

3081
04:29:41,472 --> 04:29:41,732
步骤中去盯着 Claude。
step.

3082
04:29:42,318 --> 04:29:46,212
他们描述想要的结果，让 Claude 去搞定具体怎么做。
They describe the outcome they want and let Claude figure out the how.

3083
04:29:46,798 --> 04:29:49,284
团队的座右铭是：不要过度监管。
The team motto, don't babysit.

3084
04:29:50,062 --> 04:29:52,100
但这种自主权是经过权衡的。
But that autonomy is calibrated.

3085
04:29:52,512 --> 04:29:57,028
重大、高风险或不可逆的操作，始终需要设置检查点。
Big, risky, or irreversible actions always get a checkpoint.

3086
04:29:57,582 --> 04:30:01,732
微小、安全且可逆的操作可以连续运行。
Small, safe, reversible ones can run uninterrupted.

3087
04:30:02,862 --> 04:30:03,748
第五步。
Step 5.

3088
04:30:04,112 --> 04:30:05,156
验证。
Verification.

3089
04:30:05,870 --> 04:30:09,828
Claude 不仅仅因为代码能编译就认为任务完成了。
Claude doesn't mark a task complete just because the code compiles.

3090
04:30:10,510 --> 04:30:12,420
务必提供验证手段。
Always provide verification.

3091
04:30:12,752 --> 04:30:15,108
测试、脚本或截图。
Tests, scripts, or screenshots.

3092
04:30:15,790 --> 04:30:18,468
如果你无法验证，就不要发布。
If you cannot verify it, don't ship it.

3093
04:30:19,150 --> 04:30:29,872
「信任后验证」的差距——即 Claude 生成看似合理但无法处理边界情况的实现——是新用户最常见的失败模式
The Trust Then Verify Gap, where Claude produces a plausible-looking implementation that doesn't handle edge cases, is the most common failure mode among new Claude

3094
04:30:30,032 --> 04:30:30,820
在编写代码时。
code users.

3095
04:30:31,534 --> 04:30:33,892
测试是你外部的事实来源。
Tests are your external source of truth.

3096
04:30:34,112 --> 04:30:40,996
如果没有测试，Claude 就只能依靠自己的判断来验证工作，而随着上下文填满，它的判断力会下降。
Without tests, Claude verifies its work using its own judgment, which degrades as context fills.

3097
04:30:41,710 --> 04:30:47,460
测试能提供明确的外部信号，并且在整个会话中保持准确。
Tests create an unambiguous external signal that stays accurate for the entire session.

3098
04:30:48,206 --> 04:30:54,244
每一次从红到绿的循环，都能给 Claude 提供具体的反馈，它无需等待你的指令即可采取行动。
Each red to green cycle gives Claude concrete feedback it can act on without waiting for you.

3099
04:30:55,086 --> 04:30:57,572
第六步，上下文管理。
Step six, context management.

3100
04:30:58,254 --> 04:31:02,628
当上下文占用达到 70% 时，Claude 开始失去精准度。
At 70% context usage, Claude starts losing precision.

3101
04:31:03,086 --> 04:31:06,116
到 85% 时，幻觉会增加。
At 85%, hallucinations increase.

3102
04:31:06,638 --> 04:31:10,672
在 90% 或更高时，回复会变得不稳定。
At 90% or above, responses become erratic.

3103
04:31:10,958 --> 04:31:11,872
策略是什么？
The strategy?

3104
04:31:12,462 --> 04:31:15,908
从 0 到 50% 的上下文占用，你可以随意操作。
From 0 to 50% context, work freely.

3105
04:31:16,366 --> 04:31:19,232
从 50% 到 70%，需要注意了。
From 50 to 70%, pay attention.

3106
04:31:19,472 --> 04:31:25,124
从 70% 到 90%，使用 /compact 来压缩旧的上下文。
From 70 to 90%, use slash compact to compress older context.

3107
04:31:25,934 --> 04:31:29,892
在 90% 及以上时，必须使用 /clear。
At 90% and above, slash clear is mandatory.

3108
04:31:30,606 --> 04:31:32,432
留意那个上下文条。
Monitor that context bar.

3109
04:31:32,590 --> 04:31:35,952
不要让它在你不采取行动的情况下超过 70%。
Don't let it creep past 70% without acting on it.

3110
04:31:36,112 --> 04:31:39,844
好了，现在我们进入真正编写优秀提示词的技巧环节。
Alright, now we get into the craft of actually writing good prompts.

3111
04:31:40,558 --> 04:31:48,100
我想在这里重点介绍两种特定技术，因为仅这两项就能让你获得立竿见影的显著提升。
And I want to focus on two specific techniques here because these two alone will give you an immediate measurable improvement.

3112
04:31:48,782 --> 04:31:51,300
角色提示和少样本提示。
Role prompting and few shot prompting.

3113
04:31:51,918 --> 04:31:54,340
技巧 1，角色提示。
Technique 1, role prompting.

3114
04:31:55,086 --> 04:32:02,020
角色提示是在给 Claude 下达任务之前，为其分配一个特定的身份或人格。
Role prompting is the practice of assigning Claude a specific identity or persona before giving it a task.

3115
04:32:02,382 --> 04:32:05,444
我要明确一点，这不是花架子。
And I want to be clear, this is not a gimmick.

3116
04:32:05,774 --> 04:32:08,836
它是一种真正强大的引导机制。
It is a genuinely powerful steering mechanism.

3117
04:32:09,582 --> 04:32:15,524
在系统提示词中设定角色，可以针对你的特定用例来聚焦 Claude 的行为和语气。
Setting a role in the system prompt focuses Claude's behavior and tone for your specific use case.

3118
04:32:16,238 --> 04:32:21,540
对于相同的数据，数据科学家可能看到的见解与营销战略师不同。
A data scientist might see different insights than a marketing strategist for the same data.

3119
04:32:22,030 --> 04:32:30,084
甚至，专门从事财富 500 强公司客户洞察分析的数据科学家，可能会给出不同的结果。
A data scientist specializing in customer insight analysis for Fortune 500 companies might yield different results still.

3120
04:32:30,702 --> 04:32:33,348
这里的具体程度非常重要。
The specificity matters enormously here.

3121
04:32:33,872 --> 04:32:41,872
作为一名维护了八年遗留代码库的高级 Django 开发者，给出的结果与你仅仅作为一个“开发者”时完全不同
Act as a senior Django developer who has maintained legacy codebases for eight years gives a fundamentally different result

3122
04:32:42,112 --> 04:32:44,036
如果你只是一个普通的开发者。
than you are a developer.

3123
04:32:44,494 --> 04:32:44,992
为什么？
Why?

3124
04:32:45,294 --> 04:32:53,796
因为角色定义越具体，Claude 就越能激活训练数据中与该特定专业领域匹配的模式。
Because the more specific the role, the more Claude activates patterns from the training data that match that specific expertise profile.

3125
04:32:54,254 --> 04:33:02,672
一个有遗留代码经验的高级 Django 开发者在处理重构问题时，与普通开发者的思路完全不同。
A senior Django developer with legacy codebase experience will approach a refactoring question very differently than a generic developer.

3126
04:33:03,278 --> 04:33:05,924
他们会指出向后兼容性的担忧。
They'll flag backwards compatibility concerns.

3127
04:33:06,446 --> 04:33:09,252
他们能识别出特定的 Django 反模式。
They'll recognize specific Django anti-patterns.

3128
04:33:09,710 --> 04:33:13,988
他们会倾向于选择稳健且经过验证的方法，而不是花哨的新方法。
They'll default to conservative, proven approaches over clever new ones.

3129
04:33:14,574 --> 04:33:18,800
角色提示不仅决定内容，还会塑造沟通风格。
Role prompting also shapes communication style, not just content.

3130
04:33:19,040 --> 04:33:23,908
以 CFO 为角色的提示词会生成简洁、可供高管审阅的输出。
A CFO framed prompt produces concise executive ready output.

3131
04:33:24,238 --> 04:33:29,200
以代码审查者为角色的提示词会产出系统化的问题清单反馈。
A code reviewer framed prompt produces systematic issue-cataloged feedback.

3132
04:33:29,550 --> 04:33:41,412
无论你需要 CFO 的简洁还是文案人员的华丽，角色提示都能调整 Claude 的沟通风格，并让它更严格地符合任务的具体要求。
Whether you need a CFO's brevity or a copywriter's flare, role prompting adjusts Claude's communication style and keeps it more tightly within the bounds of your task's specific requirements.

3133
04:33:41,966 --> 04:33:44,068
来做一个简单的练习来内化这个概念。
Quick exercise to internalize this.

3134
04:33:44,462 --> 04:33:50,180
使用同一个提示词“审查此身份验证模块”，并在前面加上三个不同的角色。
Take the same prompt, review this authentication module, and prepend three different roles.

3135
04:33:50,606 --> 04:33:57,764
一个安全研究员，一个刚入职的初级开发人员，以及正在准备风险评估的 CTO。
A security researcher, a junior developer onboarding to the code base, and a CTO preparing a risk assessment.

3136
04:33:58,188 --> 04:34:03,170
你会得到三个截然不同的输出，每个都针对不同的场景进行了优化。
You'll get three genuinely different outputs, each optimized for a different context.

3137
04:34:03,630 --> 04:34:05,200
这就是角色提示的作用。
That's role prompting at work.

3138
04:34:05,438 --> 04:34:08,000
技巧 2：少样本提示。
Technique 2, few shot prompting.

3139
04:34:08,430 --> 04:34:17,604
少样本提示是指在要求 Claude 处理新输入之前，先给它提供两到五个你想要的“输入-输出”模式示例。
Few shot prompting is when you provide Claude with two to five examples of the input-output pattern you want before asking it to do the same for a new input.

3140
04:34:18,028 --> 04:34:24,452
例子并不总是必需的，但在解释概念或演示特定格式时非常有效。
Examples aren't always necessary, but they shine when explaining concepts or demonstrating specific formats.

3141
04:34:24,640 --> 04:34:34,660
这种被称为单样本或少样本提示的方法是“展示”而非“描述”，它能澄清那些仅靠文字描述很难表达的细微要求。
Known as one-shot or few shot prompting, examples show rather than tell, clarifying subtle requirements that are difficult to express through description alone.

3142
04:34:35,310 --> 04:34:36,836
核心逻辑如下：
Here's the key intuition.

3143
04:34:37,230 --> 04:34:39,278
用语言描述你想要的东西很难。
Describing what you want is hard.

3144
04:34:39,564 --> 04:34:41,604
展示你想要的东西很简单。
Showing what you want is easy.

3145
04:34:41,998 --> 04:34:49,840
如果我要求你写一封专业且亲切、有特定节奏且没有术语的客户邮件，你可能只能做到接近我的要求。
If I ask you for a professional but warm client email with a specific rhythm and no jargon, you might get close to what I mean.

3146
04:34:50,158 --> 04:34:55,200
但如果我给你看三封我已经批准过的邮件示例，你就能立刻做得完美。
But if I show you three examples of emails I've already approved, you'll nail it immediately.

3147
04:34:55,598 --> 04:34:57,040
Claude 的工作原理也是一样的。
Claude works the same way.

3148
04:34:57,278 --> 04:35:07,364
一篇关于有限状态机设计的学术论文显示，结构化的示例比没有例子的指令成功率高出 90%。
An academic paper on finite state machine design showed that structured examples achieved a 90% success rate compared to instructions without examples.

3149
04:35:07,982 --> 04:35:10,532
这是一个巨大且显著的差异。
That is a massive, consistent difference.

3150
04:35:11,534 --> 04:35:17,540
Anthropic 的官方文档也建议提供三到五个示例以获得最佳效果。
Anthropic's own documentation recommends including three to five examples for best results.

3151
04:35:18,286 --> 04:35:22,788
示例应当具有相关性，并紧密贴合你的实际使用场景。
The examples should be relevant, mirroring your actual use case closely.

3152
04:35:23,278 --> 04:35:29,540
要多样化，涵盖边界情况和各种输入，以免 Claude 学习到不必要的模式。
Diverse, covering edge cases and varied inputs, so Claude doesn't pick up unintended patterns.

3153
04:35:29,998 --> 04:35:35,524
并且要结构化，用标签包裹起来，让 Claude 能清晰地将它们与你的指令区分开。
And structured, wrapped in tags so Claude can clearly distinguish them from your instructions.

3154
04:35:36,270 --> 04:35:40,196
一个实用的建议是：从一个示例开始，也就是单样本提示。
One practical note start with one example, one shot.

3155
04:35:40,686 --> 04:35:43,812
只有当输出仍不符合你的需求时，才增加更多示例。
Only add more if the output still doesn't match your needs.

3156
04:35:44,302 --> 04:35:45,732
不要过度设计。
Don't over-engineer this.

3157
04:35:46,286 --> 04:35:50,596
一个高质量的例子往往比五个平庸的例子要好得多。
One great example is almost always better than five mediocre ones.

3158
04:35:51,182 --> 04:35:59,330
将角色提示和少样本提示结合起来，你就拥有了经验丰富的 Claude Code 用户所说的「展示与说明」技术栈。
Put role prompting and few shot prompting together, and you have what experienced Claude Code users call the show and tell stack.

3159
04:35:59,854 --> 04:36:03,598
告诉 Claude 它该扮演什么角色，然后向它展示什么样的结果才算成功。
Tell Claude who to be, then show Claude what success looks like.

3160
04:36:03,840 --> 04:36:09,040
这种组合比纯指令提示在可靠性上要高得多。
That combination is reliable in a way that pure instruction prompting rarely is.

3161
04:36:09,260 --> 04:36:17,284
在使用 Claude Code 时，你经常需要做出的决定之一是：我想要结构化输出还是非结构化输出？
One of the decisions you'll make constantly when working with Claude Code is do I want structured output or unstructured output?

3162
04:36:17,966 --> 04:36:23,556
这两者用途完全不同，选错会导致不必要的麻烦。
These serve completely different purposes, and choosing the wrong one creates unnecessary friction.

3163
04:36:24,238 --> 04:36:25,284
结构化输出。
Structured outputs.

3164
04:36:26,094 --> 04:36:34,960
结构化输出意味着 Claude 返回的数据是符合特定机器可读格式的，比如 JSON、XML、带编号的列表
Structured output means Claude returns data in a defined machine readable format, JSON, XML, a numbered list,

3165
04:36:35,200 --> 04:36:38,692
表格，或者带有特定模式的代码块。
a table, or a code block with a specific schema.

3166
04:36:39,310 --> 04:36:48,960
当你需要输出被其他系统调用、通过程序处理，或者要求多个响应之间保持高度一致时，就使用这种方式。
You use this when the output needs to be consumed by another system, processed programmatically, or when consistency across multiple responses is critical.

3167
04:36:49,326 --> 04:36:53,540
而这里有一个让开发者真正领会这个概念的关键点。
And here's the connection that makes this concept truly click for developers.

3168
04:36:54,188 --> 04:36:57,154
结构化输出不仅仅是关于格式问题。
Structured output is not just about formatting.

3169
04:36:57,518 --> 04:37:00,866
它是 Claude 在现实世界中采取行动的方式。
It is how Claude actually takes action in the real world.

3170
04:37:01,518 --> 04:37:11,024
当 Claude 执行终端命令、编辑文件或调用外部工具时，它是通过工具调用来执行的，并输出一个结构化的 JSON
When Claude runs a terminal command, edits a file, or calls an external tool, it does so through tool calling, emitting a structured JSON

3171
04:37:11,264 --> 04:37:16,464
对象，明确指定要使用哪个工具以及对应的参数。
object that specifies exactly which tool to use and with what parameters.

3172
04:37:16,624 --> 04:37:20,356
这个 JSON 就是 Claude 的智能体循环读取并做出决策的内容。
That JSON is what Claude's agent loop reads to decide.

3173
04:37:20,686 --> 04:37:24,932
执行这条命令、写入这个文件、调用这个 API。
Run this command, write to this file, call this API.

3174
04:37:25,580 --> 04:37:29,252
结构化输出是 Claude 与你的环境沟通的语言。
Structured output is the language Claude speaks to your environment.

3175
04:37:29,741 --> 04:37:38,500
所以当你要求 Claude 去采取行动而非仅仅做出回应时，无论你是否意识到，你始终是在结构化输出的范畴内工作的。
So when you ask Claude to take action, not just respond, you are always working in the structured output space, whether you realize it or not.

3176
04:37:38,990 --> 04:37:41,572
Anthropic 的官方指南对此非常明确。
Anthropic's official guidance is clear on this.

3177
04:37:42,144 --> 04:37:44,804
使用结构化格式来处理状态数据。
Use structured formats for state data.

3178
04:37:45,420 --> 04:37:53,504
当追踪如测试结果或任务状态等结构化信息时，使用 JSON 或其他结构化格式来帮助 Claude
When tracking structured information like test results or task status, use JSON or other structured formats to help Claude

3179
04:37:53,664 --> 04:37:55,330
理解模式要求。
understand schema requirements.

3180
04:37:55,854 --> 04:38:03,684
自由格式的进度笔记适用于跟踪总体进展和上下文，但结构化信息需要结构化的容器。
Freeform progress notes work well for tracking general progress and context, but structured information needs structured containers.

3181
04:38:04,174 --> 04:38:12,944
一个值得记住的实际例子是 JSON 格式的测试状态文件，它是一个包含测试对象的数组，每个对象都有一个 ID，
The practical example worth keeping in mind a test status file in JSON, an array of test objects, each with an ID,

3182
04:38:13,264 --> 04:38:17,314
名称和状态，比如通过、失败或未开始。
name, and status, passing, failing, not started.

3183
04:38:17,741 --> 04:38:22,020
总数、通过数、失败数、未开始数。
Total counts, passing counts, failing counts, not started counts.

3184
04:38:22,318 --> 04:38:25,380
这些是 Claude 可以可靠进行逻辑推理的信息。
That is information Claude can reason about reliably.

3185
04:38:25,934 --> 04:38:31,582
它可以读取当前状态，决定接下来处理什么，并精确地更新文件。
It can read the current state, decide what to tackle next, and update the file with precision.

3186
04:38:31,884 --> 04:38:35,524
当你需要结构化输出时，要明确说明模式。
When you need structured output, be explicit about the schema.

3187
04:38:35,982 --> 04:38:38,020
不要只说“给我 JSON”。
Don't just say give me JSON.

3188
04:38:38,383 --> 04:38:43,684
要说“给我一个包含这些特定字段和对应类型的 JSON 对象”。
Say give me a JSON object with these specific fields at these specific types.

3189
04:38:44,398 --> 04:38:49,604
你指定的结构越精确，Claude 生成的输出就越可靠。
The more precisely you specify the structure, the more reliably Claude produces it.

3190
04:38:49,984 --> 04:38:51,330
非结构化输出。
Unstructured outputs.

3191
04:38:51,790 --> 04:38:54,223
非结构化输出就是自然语言。
Unstructured output is natural language.

3192
04:38:54,464 --> 04:38:56,804
优点、解释、叙述。
Pros, explanation, narrative.

3193
04:38:57,390 --> 04:39:09,664
如果你需要进行分析、规划笔记、文档、代码注释、错误解释，或者任何需要人类阅读和理解而非机器解析的输出，就选这种。
This is what you want for analysis, planning notes, documentation, code comments, error explanations, and any output that a human will read and reason about rather than a machine parsing.

3194
04:39:09,934 --> 04:39:16,258
四块式结构是让 Claude 生成整洁非结构化输出最可靠的结构之一。
The four-block pattern is one of the most reliable structures for getting clean, unstructured output from Claude.

3195
04:39:16,864 --> 04:39:20,004
指令：要做什么以及如何表现。
Instructions, what to do and how to behave.

3196
04:39:20,544 --> 04:39:24,644
上下文：背景信息、数据、文档。
Context, background information, data, documents.

3197
04:39:25,294 --> 04:39:28,624
任务：本次交互的具体请求。
Task, the specific request for this interaction.

3198
04:39:28,864 --> 04:39:32,258
输出格式：预期的精确结构。
Output format, the exact structure expected.

3199
04:39:32,942 --> 04:39:34,820
关键的区别就在这里。
The distinction that matters is this.

3200
04:39:35,342 --> 04:39:38,308
结构化输出是给机器和流水线用的。
Structured output is for machines and pipelines.

3201
04:39:39,054 --> 04:39:41,988
非结构化输出是给人类和逻辑推理用的。
Unstructured output is for humans and reasoning.

3202
04:39:42,638 --> 04:39:50,784
混淆这两者，比如在需要可解析的 JSON 时让 Claude 给出一个自由格式的解释，
Mixing them up, asking Claude to give you a free form explanation when you needed parsable JSON, or demanding rigid JSON

3203
04:39:50,944 --> 04:39:56,900
或者在需要叙述性分析时要求严格的 JSON，是 AI 工作流中最常见的摩擦点之一。
when you needed narrative analysis is one of the most common sources of friction in AI workflows.

3204
04:39:57,262 --> 04:40:02,820
Claude 在使用 Git 来跨多个上下文窗口追踪状态方面表现出色。
Claude performs especially well using Git to track state across multiple context windows.

3205
04:40:03,406 --> 04:40:12,388
这与结构化输出是绝佳的搭配，它能让你的项目状态保持明确并进行版本控制，而不是仅仅存在于对话历史中。
A natural pairing with structured output that keeps your project state explicit and version controlled rather than living only in conversation history.

3206
04:40:12,814 --> 04:40:14,544
还有一个关键点。
One more key insight here.

3207
04:40:14,862 --> 04:40:19,908
你提示词的排版风格会影响 Claude 回复的排版风格。
The formatting style of your prompt influences the formatting style of Claude's response.

3208
04:40:20,622 --> 04:40:26,144
如果你的提示词是用整洁、有结构的段落写的，Claude 往往也会用同样的方式来回复。
If your prompt is written in clean, structured paragraphs, Claude tends to respond in kind.

3209
04:40:26,638 --> 04:40:30,500
如果你的提示词是一堆乱糟糟的要点，你得到的往往也是一堆乱糟糟的要点。
If your prompt is a bullet soup, you'll often get a bullet soup back.

3210
04:40:30,958 --> 04:40:34,084
让你的提示词风格与你想要的输出风格保持一致。
Match your prompt style to your desired output style.

3211
04:40:34,478 --> 04:40:38,212
让我们来聊聊当事情出错时会发生什么，因为这种情况一定会发生。
Let's talk about what happens when things go wrong, because they will.

3212
04:40:38,574 --> 04:40:46,084
而你快速且准确做出反应的能力，是整个 Claude Code 技能组中被低估最多的能力之一。
And your ability to respond quickly and correctly is one of the most underrated skills in the entire Claude Code skillset.

3213
04:40:46,830 --> 04:40:51,268
第一类：看起来合理的错误，这是最棘手的一种。
Category 1, plausible looking errors, the trickiest kind.

3214
04:40:51,918 --> 04:40:55,364
这类错误最容易误导所有人，尤其是在早期阶段。
This is the one that catches everyone, especially early on.

3215
04:40:55,950 --> 04:41:04,196
ACM 的研究发现，Claude Code 生成的逻辑错误比人类编写的代码多 1.75 倍。
Research from ACM found that Claude Code can generate 1.75 times more logic errors than human written code.

3216
04:41:04,590 --> 04:41:08,452
记住这个数字，然后继续往下看，因为解决方法很简单。
Remember that number and move on, because the fix is straightforward.

3217
04:41:08,910 --> 04:41:11,076
每一项输出都必须经过验证。
Every output must be verified.

3218
04:41:11,502 --> 04:41:15,460
这里的关键词是逻辑错误，而不是语法错误。
The keyword there is logic errors, not syntax errors.

3219
04:41:15,950 --> 04:41:19,652
Claude Code 生成的代码几乎永远不会出现无法编译的情况。
Claude code almost never produces code that fails to compile.

3220
04:41:20,014 --> 04:41:30,820
它生成的是能编译、能运行，但在特定条件或在预期输入的边界情况下表现异常的代码。
It produces code that compiles, runs, and does something slightly wrong, in a way that only shows up under specific conditions or at the edges of expected input.

3221
04:41:31,406 --> 04:41:35,140
「信任但要验证」的差距是主要的失败模式。
The trust then verify gap is the primary failure mode.

3222
04:41:35,598 --> 04:41:40,464
Claude 生成的是看起来合理、但无法处理边界情况的实现方案。
Claude produces a plausible looking implementation that doesn't handle edge cases.

3223
04:41:40,654 --> 04:41:42,372
解决方法始终如一。
The fix is always the same.

3224
04:41:42,862 --> 04:41:47,716
始终提供验证、测试、脚本和截图。
Always provide verification, tests, scripts, screenshots.

3225
04:41:48,462 --> 04:41:50,980
如果你无法验证它，就不要发布它。
If you can't verify it, don't ship it.

3226
04:41:51,598 --> 04:41:54,048
这不是在批评 Claude Code。
This is not a criticism of clawed code.

3227
04:41:54,350 --> 04:41:57,412
这是所有自动化代码生成都具备的特性。
It's a property of all automated code generation.

3228
04:41:57,998 --> 04:42:07,808
缓解方法是遵循专业实践、测试驱动开发、明确的验收标准，以及一个坚定的心理准则：
The mitigation is professional practice, test-driven development, explicit acceptance criteria, and a firm mental rule that it looks right

3229
04:42:07,968 --> 04:42:10,212
「看起来正确」并不等于「就是正确的」。
is not the same as it is right.

3230
04:42:10,734 --> 04:42:11,808
第二类。
Category 2.

3231
04:42:12,048 --> 04:42:13,060
上下文漂移。
Context drift.

3232
04:42:13,710 --> 04:42:17,568
这里有一个思维模型，能让你立刻理解什么是上下文漂移。
Here's the mental model that makes context drift immediately intuitive.

3233
04:42:17,728 --> 04:42:25,924
大多数人把 Claude 当成硬盘，认为它能永远准确地记住所有内容，无论会话持续多久。
Most people treat Claude like a hard drive, something that remembers everything forever, accurately, no matter how long the session runs.

3234
04:42:26,478 --> 04:42:28,368
那完全是错误的模型。
That's the wrong model entirely.

3235
04:42:28,718 --> 04:42:33,796
Claude 更像 RAM，快速、强大、必不可少，但它是有限的。
Claude is more like RAM, fast, powerful, essential, but finite.

3236
04:42:34,318 --> 04:42:41,572
你的会话运行得越久，加载到那块 RAM 里的内容越多，旧的信息就会被挤出或覆盖掉。
The longer your session runs and the more you load into that RAM, the more older information gets crowded out and overwritten.

3237
04:42:42,030 --> 04:42:45,860
上下文漂移正是当 RAM 填满时发生的情况。
Context drift is exactly what happens when RAM fills up.

3238
04:42:46,414 --> 04:42:51,300
随着会话变长，Claude 的回答开始偏离你的初衷。
As a session gets longer, Claude's responses start to drift from your original intent.

3239
04:42:51,726 --> 04:43:03,012
它会忘记之前的约束，开始做出与 30 条消息前做出的决定相矛盾的假设，或者丢失你在开头建立的架构方向。
It forgets earlier constraints, starts making assumptions that contradict decisions made 30 messages ago, or loses track of the architectural direction you established at the start.

3240
04:43:03,694 --> 04:43:08,004
当上下文占用达到 70% 时，Claude 开始失去精准度。
At 70% context usage, Claude starts losing precision.

3241
04:43:08,494 --> 04:43:12,612
到 85% 时，幻觉会显著增加。
At 85%, hallucinations increase significantly.

3242
04:43:13,038 --> 04:43:16,740
达到 90% 及以上时，回复就会变得不稳定。
At 90% and above, responses become erratic.

3243
04:43:17,230 --> 04:43:21,248
这不是 Bug，而是上下文窗口物理特性的体现。
This isn't a bug, it's the physics of the context window at work.

3244
04:43:21,454 --> 04:43:24,452
解决方法是主动进行上下文管理。
The mitigation is proactive context management.

3245
04:43:25,070 --> 04:43:33,508
在进入危险区域前使用 slash compact 来释放内存，并且不要让会话运行到超出其窗口支持的长度。
Use slash compact to free up that RAM before you hit the danger zone, and don't let sessions run longer than their window can support.

3246
04:43:34,318 --> 04:43:35,328
类别 3。
Category 3.

3247
04:43:35,630 --> 04:43:36,388
范围蔓延
Scope creep

3248
04:43:37,102 --> 04:43:39,168
无限探索问题。
The infinite exploration problem.

3249
04:43:39,790 --> 04:43:51,876
如果你让 Claude 去调查某件事却没限定范围，它会读取成百上千个文件，填满上下文窗口并消耗时间，却无法产出可操作的结论。
You ask Claude to investigate something without scoping it, and Claude reads hundreds of files, filling the context window and consuming time without producing actionable output.

3250
04:43:52,366 --> 04:43:53,028
解决方法。
The FIX.

3251
04:43:53,582 --> 04:44:00,612
缩小调查范围，或者使用子代理，以免探索过程耗尽你的主上下文。
Scope investigations narrowly, or use subagents so the exploration doesn't consume your main context.

3252
04:44:01,550 --> 04:44:03,972
这里的教训看似简单。
The lesson here is deceptively simple.

3253
04:44:04,430 --> 04:44:10,372
永远不要在没有明确停止条件的情况下，给 Claude 一个开放式的调查任务。
Never give Claude an open-ended investigative task without a defined stopping condition.

3254
04:44:10,862 --> 04:44:16,420
「调查身份验证模块」可能意味着读取 5 个文件，也可能意味着阅读 500 个。
Look into the authentication module can mean reading five files or reading 500.

3255
04:44:16,974 --> 04:44:27,204
始终说明你希望从调查中获得什么，比如回答一个具体问题、列出特定风险或编目特定的文件集。
Always say what you need out of the investigation, a specific question answered, a specific list of risks identified, a specific set of files cataloged.

3256
04:44:27,726 --> 04:44:28,848
类别 4。
Category 4.

3257
04:44:29,134 --> 04:44:30,564
忽视边缘情况。
Edge case blindness.

3258
04:44:31,054 --> 04:44:34,128
Claude Code 会可靠地实现理想路径。
Claude code will implement the happy path reliably.

3259
04:44:34,318 --> 04:44:42,528
但它可能会忽略掉的东西，尤其是在没有指导的情况下，就是那些边缘情况、空输入、空值、网络超时等，
What it can miss, especially without guidance, are the edge cases, empty inputs, null values, network timeouts,

3260
04:44:42,798 --> 04:44:47,620
并发请求、异常字符编码、权限失败。
concurrent requests, unusual character encodings, permissions failures.

3261
04:44:48,078 --> 04:44:52,388
对于较大的功能，让 Claude 在开始执行前先对你进行访谈。
For larger features, have Claude interview you before implementation begins.

3262
04:44:53,038 --> 04:44:55,588
要求它使用「Ask User Question」工具。
Ask it to use the Ask User Question tool.

3263
04:44:56,110 --> 04:45:03,428
Claude 会询问一些你可能还没考虑到的问题，包括技术实现、边缘情况和权衡取舍。
Claude will ask about things you might not have considered yet, including technical implementation, edge cases, and trade-offs.

3264
04:45:03,790 --> 04:45:08,324
这一步就能在编写代码前捕捉到大部分遗漏的边缘情况。
This single step catches most edge case oversights before any code is written.

3265
04:45:08,654 --> 04:45:10,768
如果不确定，就明确表述。
And when in doubt, be explicit.

3266
04:45:11,150 --> 04:45:16,448
告诉 Claude，在你写下第一行代码之前，列出这个函数需要处理的所有边缘情况。
Tell Claude, list every edge case this function needs to handle before you write a single line.

3267
04:45:16,750 --> 04:45:21,380
让边缘情况成为提示词中的首要考量，而不是事后补救。
Make edge cases a first class concern in your prompts, not an afterthought.

3268
04:45:21,710 --> 04:45:22,848
恢复模式。
Recovery pattern.

3269
04:45:23,150 --> 04:45:27,172
当会话中途出现问题时，恢复模式是统一的。
When something goes wrong mid-session, the recovery pattern is consistent.

3270
04:45:27,598 --> 04:45:30,288
停止、重新规划，不要打补丁。
Stop, replan, don't patch.

3271
04:45:30,606 --> 04:45:33,568
提前写出详细的规范，以减少歧义。
Write detailed specs up front to reduce ambiguity.

3272
04:45:33,742 --> 04:45:42,756
并在每次修正后，更新 lessons.md。这是你维护的文件，并且在相关会话开始时明确指向它。
And after any correction, update lessons.md, a file you maintain and explicitly point clawed to at the start of relevant sessions.

3273
04:45:43,470 --> 04:45:46,820
写下一条规则，防止同样的错误再次发生。
Write a rule that prevents the same mistake from happening again.

3274
04:45:47,630 --> 04:45:58,020
随着时间的推移，你的 Claude.md 和 lessons.md 将成为一个知识库，记录 Claude 在你特定的代码库中犯过的所有错误以及如何避免它们。
Over time, your Claude.md and lessons.md become a knowledge base of everything Claude got wrong in your specific codebase and how to prevent it.

3275
04:45:58,478 --> 04:46:01,604
Claude.md 是给 Claude 的自动简报。
Claude.md is Claude's automatic briefing.

3276
04:46:02,094 --> 04:46:06,884
lessons.md 是你刻意传递的机构记忆。
Lessons.md is the institutional memory you hand over deliberately.

3277
04:46:07,502 --> 04:46:10,052
两者结合起来，就是一种不断积累的资产。
Together, that's a compounding asset.

3278
04:46:10,350 --> 04:46:12,672
它的价值每周都在增加。
It gets more valuable every week.

3279
04:46:12,910 --> 04:46:14,532
现在我们扩大一下范围。
Now we step up in scope.

3280
04:46:14,958 --> 04:46:17,312
单任务的 Claude Code 很强大。
Single-task Claude Code is powerful.

3281
04:46:17,646 --> 04:46:20,324
多步骤的 Claude code 是具有变革性的。
Multi-step Claude code is transformational.

3282
04:46:20,846 --> 04:46:24,836
这是构建远超单一提示词的工作流的框架。
Here's the framework for building workflows that go well beyond a single prompt.

3283
04:46:25,550 --> 04:46:28,676
Claude Code 支持五种核心工作流模式。
Claude Code supports five core workflow patterns.

3284
04:46:29,198 --> 04:46:32,964
理解这些模式决定了你实际能完成多少工作。
Understanding these patterns determines how much you can actually get done.

3285
04:46:33,358 --> 04:46:35,876
模式一，顺序工作流。
Pattern one, sequential workflows.

3286
04:46:36,430 --> 04:46:38,884
顺序工作流是最简单的模式。
Sequential workflows are the simplest pattern.

3287
04:46:39,246 --> 04:46:44,740
Claude 按顺序执行一系列步骤，每一步的输出都会作为下一步的输入。
Claude executes a series of steps in order where the output of each step feeds into the next.

3288
04:46:45,422 --> 04:46:46,832
可以把它想象成一个流水线。
Think of it as a pipeline.

3289
04:46:47,246 --> 04:46:55,012
步骤 A 完成后，结果传递给步骤 B，步骤 B 完成后，结果传递给步骤 C，以此类推。
Step A completes, its result passes to step B, step B completes, result passes to step C, and so on.

3290
04:46:55,312 --> 04:47:04,100
例如：阅读规范、生成测试、实现代码、运行测试、修复失败、生成文档。
Example, read the spec, generate tests, implement code, run tests, fix failures, generate documentation.

3291
04:47:04,494 --> 04:47:06,672
每一步都依赖于前一步。
Each step depends on the previous one.

3292
04:47:07,022 --> 04:47:10,084
这是你处理可预测功能的常用工作流。
This is your bread and butter workflow for predictable features.

3293
04:47:10,382 --> 04:47:11,232
模式二。
Pattern 2.

3294
04:47:11,502 --> 04:47:12,912
编排者模式。
The orchestrator pattern.

3295
04:47:13,166 --> 04:47:19,460
编排者模式引入了一个控制性智能体，它负责规划并指挥其他智能体或工具调用。
The orchestrator pattern introduces a controlling agent that plans and directs other agents or tool calls.

3296
04:47:20,462 --> 04:47:31,172
一个 Claude 实例作为编排者，决定需要发生什么以及按什么顺序，然后将实际执行委派给子智能体或工具调用。
One Claude instance, the orchestrator, decides what needs to happen and in what order, then delegates the actual execution to subagents or tool calls.

3297
04:47:32,014 --> 04:47:40,068
这就是 Claude Code 的创建者本人操作的方式，他同时运行 10 到 15 个 Claude Code 会话，
This is how the creator of Claude Code himself operates, running 10 to 15 CLOD code sessions simultaneously,

3298
04:47:40,432 --> 04:47:43,908
每个会话都专注于特定的委派任务。
with each session focused on a specific delegated task.

3299
04:47:44,686 --> 04:47:47,232
子智能体负责专注的执行。
Sub-agents handle focused execution.

3300
04:47:47,566 --> 04:47:49,604
主上下文保持整洁。
The main context stays clean.

3301
04:47:49,934 --> 04:47:50,820
模式 3。
Pattern 3.

3302
04:47:51,310 --> 04:47:52,352
拆分与合并。
Split and merge.

3303
04:47:53,392 --> 04:48:02,468
当你在代码库中需要为 50 个函数编写文档时，与其一个一个来，不如将这些函数分成 10 组，每组 5 个，
When you need to document 50 functions across a code base, instead of doing them one at a time, you split the functions into 10 batches of 5,

3304
04:48:02,862 --> 04:48:09,220
同时运行 10 个 Claude 实例，并在最后合并所有生成的文档字符串。
run 10 Claude instances simultaneously, and merge all the generated doc strings at the end.

3305
04:48:09,742 --> 04:48:12,032
性能提升会非常显著。
The performance gain can be dramatic.

3306
04:48:12,398 --> 04:48:16,964
10 个并行工作节点可以在相同时间内完成 10 倍的工作量。
10 parallel workers finish 10 times as much work in the same time.

3307
04:48:17,742 --> 04:48:20,004
复杂之处在于合并步骤。
The complexity is in the merge step.

3308
04:48:20,334 --> 04:48:23,780
并行处理的结果并不总是能自动合并的。
Parallel results aren't always automatically combinable.

3309
04:48:24,142 --> 04:48:26,628
你需要明确设计合并逻辑。
You need to design the merge explicitly.

3310
04:48:27,278 --> 04:48:28,192
模式 4。
Pattern 4.

3311
04:48:28,526 --> 04:48:29,860
自我修正循环。
Self-correction loop.

3312
04:48:30,414 --> 04:48:33,348
最常见的链式调用模式就是自我修正。
The most common chaining pattern is self-correction.

3313
04:48:33,742 --> 04:48:40,196
生成草稿，让 Claude 根据标准进行审查，再让 Claude 根据审查意见进行优化。
Generate a draft, have Claude review it against criteria, have Claude refine based on the review.

3314
04:48:40,686 --> 04:48:46,436
每一步都是独立的调用，因此你可以在任何点进行记录、评估或分支处理。
Each step is a separate call so you can log, evaluate, or branch at any point.

3315
04:48:46,958 --> 04:48:54,692
这就是为什么 Claude Code 感觉内置了质量控制，因为当你正确设计工作流时，它确实具备这种能力。
This is what makes Claude Code feel like it has quality control built in, because when you design the workflow correctly, it does.

3316
04:48:55,214 --> 04:48:56,192
模式 5。
Pattern 5.

3317
04:48:56,494 --> 04:48:59,172
无头模式或 CI 工作流。
Headless slash CI workflows.

3318
04:48:59,790 --> 04:49:04,352
Claude 代码可以在自动化的流水线中完全非交互式地运行。
Claude code can run completely non-interactively in automated pipelines.

3319
04:49:04,590 --> 04:49:14,980
你可以将 Claude 接入脚本用于 CI 和批量处理，在无需人工干预的情况下，在多个上下文中用不同的参数运行相同的命令。
You can pipe Claude into scripts for CI and batch processing, running the same command with different parameters across multiple contexts without any human interaction.

3320
04:49:15,662 --> 04:49:23,940
根据任务结构选择你的模式：线性依赖关系用顺序执行，复杂委派用编排者模式，
Choose your pattern based on task structure, sequential for linear dependencies, orchestrator for complex delegation,

3321
04:49:24,430 --> 04:49:32,324
独立批次用并行处理，对质量敏感的输出用自我修正，自动化操作则用无头模式。
parallel for independent batches, self-correction for quality sensitive outputs, and headless for automation.

3322
04:49:32,974 --> 04:49:41,028
最后我们来聊点具体的习惯，即区分高效 Claude Code 会话与混乱会话的具体行为。
Let's close with the concrete habits, the specific behaviors that separate a productive Cloud Code session from a chaotic one.

3323
04:49:41,806 --> 04:49:48,644
这些习惯直接源自专家级 Claude Code 用户的操作经验，包括 Anthropic 内部的团队。
These are drawn directly from how expert Cloud Code users operate, including teams at Anthropic itself.

3324
04:49:49,614 --> 04:49:50,628
实践 1。
Practice 1.

3325
04:49:50,958 --> 04:49:52,740
执行前先计划。
Plan before you execute.

3326
04:49:53,184 --> 04:49:53,700
务必这样做。
Always.

3327
04:49:54,382 --> 04:50:00,004
假设在任何单个决策中，Claude 有 80% 的概率做出正确的判断。
Assume Claude makes the right call 80% of the time on any individual decision.

3328
04:50:00,654 --> 04:50:03,524
一个典型的功能涉及 20 个决策点。
A typical feature involves 20 decision points.

3329
04:50:04,110 --> 04:50:10,864
所有这些决策全部正确的概率是 0.8 的 20 次方，大约只有 1%。
The probability of getting all of them right is 0.8 to the power of 20, roughly 1%.

3330
04:50:11,822 --> 04:50:21,988
规划能将这 20 个模糊的决策转化为经过审查的规范，因为你已经提前做出了决定，所以每个决策的准确率都会接近 100%。
Planning collapses those 20 ambiguous decisions into a reviewed spec where each one lands near 100% because you have already made the call.

3331
04:50:22,510 --> 04:50:30,148
一名开发者花了两小时编写详细的规范，从而节省了约 6 到 10 小时的开发时间。
One developer spent two hours on a detailed spec and recovered an estimated 6 to 10 hours of implementation time.

3332
04:50:30,510 --> 04:50:33,732
在更大型的功能中，这种前期投入的收益会成倍增加。
The upfront investment compounds on larger features.

3333
04:50:34,638 --> 04:50:35,684
实践 2。
Practice 2.

3334
04:50:36,078 --> 04:50:39,204
保持 Claude.md 简洁且精炼。
Keep Claude.md short and earned.

3335
04:50:39,598 --> 04:50:47,172
最有效的 Claude.md 文件大约是 100 行，而不是 500 或 1000 行。
The most effective Claude.md files are around 100 lines, not 500, not 1000.

3336
04:50:47,758 --> 04:50:49,668
每一条规则都有存在的意义。
Every rule earns its place.

3337
04:50:50,286 --> 04:50:51,024
不要废话。
No filler.

3338
04:50:51,504 --> 04:50:53,572
不要加入“以防万一”的指令。
No just in case instructions.

3339
04:50:54,222 --> 04:50:57,504
每一条规则的存在都是为了解决实际问题。
Every rule exists because it solved a real problem.

3340
04:50:58,158 --> 04:51:04,036
如果你无法解释为什么某条规则在 Claude.md 中，那它可能就不该存在。
If you can't explain why a rule is in your Claude.md, it probably shouldn't be there.

3341
04:51:04,590 --> 04:51:11,428
记住，Claude.md 是 Claude 在每次会话启动时自动读取的唯一文件。
Remember, Claude.md is the one file Claude reads automatically on every session startup.

3342
04:51:12,046 --> 04:51:17,508
保持内容聚焦，因为其中的每一项都会消耗每次会话的上下文资源。
Keep it focused because everything in it costs context on every single session.

3343
04:51:18,062 --> 04:51:22,116
精简且精准总是优于冗长且全面。
Lean and precise beats long and comprehensive every time.

3344
04:51:22,510 --> 04:51:23,504
实践 3。
Practice 3.

3345
04:51:23,758 --> 04:51:25,316
先写失败的测试用例。
Write failing tests first.

3346
04:51:25,966 --> 04:51:27,204
先写测试。
Write tests first.

3347
04:51:27,726 --> 04:51:30,944
在开始任何实现之前，确认它们全部失败。
Confirm they all fail before any implementation.

3348
04:51:31,150 --> 04:51:33,380
将这些失败的测试作为检查点提交。
Commit the failing tests as a checkpoint.

3349
04:51:34,126 --> 04:51:40,900
要求 Claude 进行实现，直到所有测试通过，并明确指示它不得修改测试用例。
Ask Claude to implement until all tests pass with an explicit instruction not to modify the tests.

3350
04:51:41,646 --> 04:51:45,860
在智能体工作流中，测试是唯一客观的真理来源。
Tests are the only objective source of truth in an agentic workflow.

3351
04:51:46,350 --> 04:51:52,196
其他的一切都依赖于 Claude 的判断，而随着上下文填满，Claude 的判断能力会下降。
Everything else is Claude's judgment, and Claude's judgment degrades as context fills.

3352
04:51:52,526 --> 04:51:53,572
实践 4。
Practice 4.

3353
04:51:53,934 --> 04:51:56,452
记录经验，而不只是产出结果。
Capture lessons, not just outputs.

3354
04:51:56,974 --> 04:52:05,104
在任何纠正之后，每当 Claude 做错事且你对其进行修正时，让 Claude 在 lessons.md 中写下一条规则
After any correction, anytime Claude does something wrong and you correct it, have Claude write a rule in lessons.md

3355
04:52:05,422 --> 04:52:07,268
来防止同样的错误再次发生。
that prevents the same mistake.

3356
04:52:07,630 --> 04:52:12,740
记住，lessons.md 是你的约定，而不是 Claude 内置的功能。
Remember, lessons.md is your convention, not Claude's built-in.

3357
04:52:13,166 --> 04:52:20,292
由你创建、由你维护，并在相关场景的会话开始时明确要求 Claude 去阅读它。
You create it, you maintain it, and you explicitly tell Claude to read it at the start of sessions where it's relevant.

3358
04:52:20,654 --> 04:52:25,796
随着时间的推移，Claude 实际上在通过这些规则学会更好地处理你的特定项目。
Over time, Claude literally teaches itself to be better at your specific project.

3359
04:52:26,254 --> 04:52:30,084
这是将复利原理应用于 AI 工作流。
This is the compound interest principle applied to AI workflows.

3360
04:52:30,702 --> 04:52:34,916
每一个被记录下来的纠正，都是一个永远不再发生的错误。
Every correction that gets captured is a mistake that never happens again.

3361
04:52:35,184 --> 04:52:36,356
练习 5。
Practice 5.

3362
04:52:36,750 --> 04:52:39,504
缩小范围，核实一切。
Scope narrowly, verify everything.

3363
04:52:39,790 --> 04:52:43,780
官方最佳实践指南中的模式并非一成不变。
The patterns in the official best practices guide aren't set in stone.

3364
04:52:44,398 --> 04:52:49,184
有时当你深陷于一个复杂的难题时，应该让上下文不断累积。
Sometimes you should let context accumulate because you're deep in one complex problem.

3365
04:52:49,902 --> 04:52:53,444
有时对于探索性任务，你可以跳过规划步骤。
Sometimes you should skip planning for an exploratory task.

3366
04:52:54,094 --> 04:53:01,476
有时候模糊的提示词反而很合适，因为你想在限制它之前看看 Claude 是如何理解这个问题的。
Sometimes a vague prompt is exactly right because you want to see how Claude interprets the problem before constraining it.

3367
04:53:02,158 --> 04:53:04,836
上下文是让 Claude 代码变得强大的原因。
Context is what makes Claude code powerful.

3368
04:53:05,294 --> 04:53:11,108
而对给它什么、何时清除以及如何界定范围的判断，才是让你变强大的关键。
Judgment about what to give it, when to clear it, and how to scope it is what makes you powerful.

3369
04:53:11,598 --> 04:53:14,148
工具负责执行，你负责设计。
The tool executes, you design.

3370
04:53:14,542 --> 04:53:21,104
清晰划分这种职责，是每一个可靠的 Claude Code 工作流的基础。
That division of responsibility, held clearly, is the foundation of every reliable Claud Code workflow.

3371
04:53:21,344 --> 04:53:28,900
到这一步，你已经对 Claude Code 工作流在实践中究竟如何运作有了深刻的端到端理解。
At this point, you've developed a strong end-to-end understanding of how Claud Code workflows actually operate in practice.

3372
04:53:29,742 --> 04:53:42,224
你现在可以看到一个简单的提示词是如何演变成「计划、执行、验证」循环的，并且你理解了从会话设置到执行的完整用户交互流程
You can now see how a simple prompt evolves into a structured plan, execute, verify cycle, and you understand the full user interaction flow from session setup to execution

3373
04:53:42,384 --> 04:53:43,300
以及优化过程。
and refinement.

3374
04:53:44,014 --> 04:53:54,596
你知道 Claude 会自动读取的 Claude.md 与你维护并明确指向 Claude 的工作流规范（如 spec.md 和 lessons.md）之间的重要区别
You know the important distinction between Claude.md, which Claude reads automatically, and workflow conventions like spec.md and lessons.md,

3375
04:53:55,024 --> 04:53:58,340
这些是你需要手动维护并明确告知 Claude 的。
which you maintain and point Claude to explicitly.

3376
04:53:58,862 --> 04:54:08,836
你已经学会如何利用角色提示和少样本提示来引导结果，以及根据你的目标在结构化输出和非结构化输出之间做出选择
You've learned how to guide outcomes using role prompting and few shot prompting, and when to choose between structured and unstructured outputs based on your goal,

3377
04:54:09,264 --> 04:54:15,744
包括为什么结构化输出是 Claude 通过工具调用来采取行动的语言。
including why structured output is the language Claude uses to actually take action through tool calling.

3378
04:54:15,918 --> 04:54:25,348
你还具备了识别常见失败模式的能力，比如逻辑错误、上下文偏移、范围蔓延以及遗漏的边界情况。
You're also equipped to recognize common failure patterns like logic errors, context drift, scope creep, and missed edge cases.

3379
04:54:26,064 --> 04:54:34,340
而且你现在拥有了「内存与硬盘」的思维模型，来准确理解为什么上下文管理不是可有可无的。
And you now have the RAM versus hard drive mental model to understand exactly why context management isn't optional.

3380
04:54:35,214 --> 04:54:43,392
除此之外，你还掌握了五种关键的工作流模式：顺序、编排、并行
On top of that, you understand the five key workflow patterns: sequential, orchestrated, parallel,

3381
04:54:43,822 --> 04:54:52,132
自我纠正和无头模式，以及一些实用的最佳实践，比如规划先行、保持上下文、精简、
self-correcting, and headless, along with practical best practices like planning, first, keeping context, lean,

3382
04:54:52,672 --> 04:54:57,988
测试、早期介入、记录经验以及保持严格的范围。
testing, early, capturing learnings, and maintaining tight scope.

3383
04:54:58,734 --> 04:55:03,044
你现在已经准备好在真实的实操环境中应用这些技能了。
You're now ready to apply these skills in real, hands-on environments.

3384
04:55:03,694 --> 04:55:06,916
我们为这个模型选出的两个项目并非随机挑选的。
The two projects we have chosen for this model aren't random.

3385
04:55:07,342 --> 04:55:09,380
它们是经过精心设计的。
They were chosen very deliberately.

3386
04:55:09,998 --> 04:55:12,228
第一个是井字棋游戏。
The first one is a tic-tac-toe game.

3387
04:55:12,782 --> 04:55:20,420
它教会你如何在结构化、有边界的环境中，利用 Claude Code 来推理状态、逻辑和决策。
It teaches you how to use Claud code to reason about state, logic, and decisions in a structured, bounded environment.

3388
04:55:21,102 --> 04:55:31,140
第二个是一个 AI 驱动的网站，它教你如何利用 Claude 根据真实的用户需求生成动态的、感知上下文的内容。
The second one is an AI-powered website where it teaches you how to use Claude to generate dynamic, context-aware content in response to real user needs.

3389
04:55:31,854 --> 04:55:42,916
这两个项目共同涵盖了目前开发者在产品中使用 AI 的两种最基础的方式：作为推理引擎和作为内容生成引擎。
Together, these two projects cover the two most fundamental ways developers are using AI in products today, as a reasoning engine and as a content generation engine.

3390
04:55:43,374 --> 04:55:47,172
到本模块结束时，你不仅将拥有两个可运行的项目。
By the end of this module, you won't just have two working projects.

3391
04:55:47,630 --> 04:55:58,404
你将获得一套处理 AI 驱动项目的模型，因为你即将学习的这些模式在各个行业和各类应用中都会重复出现。
You will have a model for how to approach an AI-powered project, because the patterns you are about to learn repeat themselves across every industry and every application type.

3392
04:55:58,830 --> 04:56:00,192
让我们从第一个项目开始。
Let's start with project one.

3393
04:56:00,592 --> 04:56:09,508
在我们看游戏本身之前，我想重新定义一下这个项目的本质，因为仅仅称它为“井字棋”游戏大大低估了它的价值。
Before we look at the game itself, I want to reframe what this project actually is, because calling it a tic-tac-toe game undersells it significantly.

3394
04:56:09,952 --> 04:56:12,484
这个项目真正的核心在于：
What this project is really about is this.

3395
04:56:13,102 --> 04:56:19,716
如何在结构化的基于规则的系统中，将 AI 语言模型作为决策引擎？
How do you use an AI language model as the decision-making engine inside a structured rule-based system?

3396
04:56:20,334 --> 04:56:31,460
这个问题——即如何给 Claude 提供明确的游戏状态并让它返回正确的策略决策——在更重要的场景中也是同样的问题。
That question, how to give Claude a defined game state and give back a valid strategic decision, is the exact same question being asked in much more consequential contexts.

3397
04:56:32,078 --> 04:56:41,092
这和 AI 驱动的调度系统、自动交易逻辑、欺诈检测路由以及医疗分诊工具背后的核心问题是一样的。
It's the same question behind AI-powered scheduling system, automated trading logic, fraud detection routing, and medical triage tools.

3398
04:56:41,518 --> 04:56:42,592
游戏很简单。
The game is simple.

3399
04:56:42,862 --> 04:56:44,432
但模式是通用的。
The pattern is universal.

3400
04:56:44,718 --> 04:56:47,012
在这里学到它，到任何地方都能应用。
Learn it here, apply it anywhere.

3401
04:56:47,598 --> 04:56:51,972
让我们看看如何用这段简单的 Claude 代码来创建一个井字棋游戏。
Let's see how to create a tic-tac-toe game using this simple Claude code.

3402
04:56:52,750 --> 04:56:57,124
在 Claude 中，这是你进行编码部分的代码空间。
So in Claude, this is the code space where you will be doing your coding part.

3403
04:56:57,710 --> 04:57:03,556
点击代码标签下的新会话，然后这里就是输入提示词的空间。
Click on the new session under the code tab, and then here is the space where you will be giving your prompt.

3404
04:57:04,334 --> 04:57:06,084
现在让我在这里输入我的提示词。
So let me give my prompt here.

3405
04:57:06,766 --> 04:57:14,512
构建一个井字棋游戏作为一个单一的索引文件，使用原生 HTML、CSS
Build a tic-tac-toe game as a single index file where vanilla HTML were using the HTML, CSS,

3406
04:57:14,832 --> 04:57:15,748
和 JavaScript。
and JavaScript.

3407
04:57:16,494 --> 04:57:18,660
这些是需要遵循的要求。
So these are the requirements to be followed.

3408
04:57:19,246 --> 04:57:21,636
带可点击单元格的 3x3 网格。
3x3 grid with clickable cells.

