这个提示词要求生成一段三秒钟的真实视频，内容是一个正在大笑的婴儿突然失去平衡并摔倒在地上。
This prompt is asking for a short, a three-second realistic video featuring a baby who's laughing and then suddenly loses balance and falls to the ground while laughing.

4122
05:56:25,166 --> 05:56:31,396
重点是创造一个自然的、栩栩如生的瞬间，包含真实的动作、表情和视觉效果。
The focus is on creating a natural, lifelike moment with realistic motion, expressions, and visuals.

4123
05:56:31,918 --> 05:56:38,980
意图是在极短的片段中捕捉到婴儿快乐的反应以及快速、俏皮的动作。
The intention is to capture the baby's joyful reaction along with the quick, playful action happening in a very short clip.

4124
05:56:39,470 --> 05:56:41,988
让我们执行一下，看看输出结果是什么样的。
Let's execute this and see what the output looks like.

4125
05:56:42,702 --> 05:56:46,052
系统显示视频已准备好，让我播放一下。
So it says your video is ready, so let me play this.

4126
05:56:46,702 --> 05:56:47,296
哇！
Wow!

4127
05:56:47,726 --> 05:56:56,896
这就是输出结果，利用 VO3 和 NanoBanana Pro 生成了一个笑到摔倒的婴儿真实图像。
This is the output where the realistic image of a baby falling to the ground while laughing is generated using both VO3 and NanoBanana Pro.

4128
05:56:57,262 --> 05:56:58,852
太棒了，对吧？
That's fantastic, right?

4129
05:56:59,278 --> 05:57:07,140
好了，在我们开始制作交互式图像之前，花点时间了解一下这种方法为什么如此强大。
Alright, before we jump into building our interactive image, let's take a moment to understand what makes this approach so powerful.

4130
05:57:07,598 --> 05:57:15,524
乍一看，它可能看起来像一张普通的图片，只有颜色、形状和标签，但当你开始与之互动时，
At first glance, it might look like a regular image, just colors, shapes, and labels, but the moment you start interacting with it,

4131
05:57:15,776 --> 05:57:18,756
你就会发现神奇之处就在表面之下。
you realize the magic happens beneath the surface.

4132
05:57:19,406 --> 05:57:27,236
每个标签都可以点击，每个部分都会立即显示信息，整张图片变成了一种动态的学习体验。
Each label is clickable, each section reveals information instantly, and the whole image becomes a dynamic learning experience.

4133
05:57:27,918 --> 05:57:30,660
那么，到底什么是交互式图像？
So what exactly is an interactive image?

4134
05:57:31,310 --> 05:57:34,916
简单来说，它是一种旨在响应用户的图像。
Simply put, it's an image designed to respond to the user.

4135
05:57:35,406 --> 05:57:37,668
想象一个简单的花朵示意图。
Imagine a simple diagram of a flower.

4136
05:57:38,030 --> 05:57:46,816
你不再只是把它看作一张静态图片，你可以点击花瓣、茎或根部，然后会立即弹出一个包含清晰、
Instead of just seeing it as a static picture, you can click on the petals, stem, or roots, and instantly a side panel pops up with clear,

4137
05:57:47,056 --> 05:57:48,388
简洁解释的侧边栏。
concise explanations.

4138
05:57:48,878 --> 05:57:51,588
它把被动观看变成了主动学习。
It turns passive viewing into active learning.

4139
05:57:52,014 --> 05:57:57,188
交互式图像的魅力在于它们将视觉吸引力与教育深度结合在了一起。
The beauty of interactive images is that they combine visual appeal with educational depth.

4140
05:57:57,742 --> 05:58:04,548
你可以在一个简洁的界面中突出结构、解释功能，并引导观众的注意力。
You can highlight structures, explain functions, and guide the viewer's attention all in one clean interface.

4141
05:58:05,070 --> 05:58:08,836
最棒的是，你不需要复杂的编程就能实现这个功能。
And the best part is you don't need complex coding to make this happen.

4142
05:58:09,262 --> 05:58:11,940
像 Gemini 这样的工具让操作变得直观且快速。
Tools like Gemini make it intuitive and fast.

4143
05:58:12,494 --> 05:58:16,132
今天，我们将从零开始创建一个交互式图像。
Today, we are going to create an interactive image from scratch.

4144
05:58:16,686 --> 05:58:24,516
让我们看看 Gemini 如何添加标签、定义可点击区域，并设计出在点击每个标签时显示信息的侧边栏。
Let's see how Gemini adds labels, defines clickable areas, and designs side panels that reveal information when each label is clicked.

4145
05:58:25,166 --> 05:58:34,176
到这儿结束时，你就会知道如何将任何静态视觉内容转化为互动性强、信息丰富的交互式体验，非常适合教学，
By the end of this, you will know how to transform any static visual into an engaging, informative, and interactive experience, perfect for teaching,

4146
05:58:34,496 --> 05:58:37,956
用于演示，或者只是用有趣的方式来探索想法。
presentations, or simply exploring ideas in a fun way.

4147
05:58:38,446 --> 05:58:43,908
让我们开始吧，去创作那些不仅仅停留在屏幕上、而是栩栩如生的视觉内容。
Let's dive in and start creating visuals that don't just sit on the screen, they come alive.

4148
05:58:44,430 --> 05:58:45,988
这就是我的提示词。
So, this is my prompt.

4149
05:58:46,446 --> 05:58:52,996
这个提示词指示 AI 生成一个交互式视觉工具，帮助用户了解人类大脑。
This prompt instructs the AI to generate an interactive visual tool that helps users learn about the human brain.

4150
05:58:53,422 --> 05:58:59,204
它要求提供一张简洁、极简的大脑图像，并在不同的脑区放置清晰可读的标签。
It asks for a clean, minimal image of the brain with readable labels placed on different brain regions.

4151
05:58:59,726 --> 05:59:06,692
当用户点击一个标签时，界面应在侧边栏中显示关于该特定部分的简明扼要且清晰的说明。
When a user clicks a label, the interface should show a brief and clear explanation of that specific part in a side panel.

4152
05:59:07,118 --> 05:59:17,252
重点在于简洁、流畅的交互、用户友好性以及有条理的设计，让用户能够轻松探索并理解每个大脑部位。
The focus is on simplicity, smooth interactions, user friendliness, and an organized design that makes it easy for users to explore and understand each brain part.

4153
05:59:17,710 --> 05:59:20,772
这就是带有标签的人类大脑图像。
So here is the human brain image created with the labels.

4154
05:59:21,262 --> 05:59:25,028
它提供了一段 HTML 代码，以及这里的大脑图像。
So it has given me an HTML code along with the brain image here.

4155
05:59:25,390 --> 05:59:29,380
它要求我将代码保存为 HTML 文件。
So it is asking me to save the code as an HTML file.

4156
05:59:29,742 --> 05:59:31,076
让我复制一下。
So let me copy this.

4157
05:59:31,598 --> 05:59:36,096
我会仔细复制并粘贴这段特定的 HTML 代码。
I will carefully copy and then paste this specific HTML code.

4158
05:59:36,334 --> 05:59:42,660
随后，将生成的文件保存在我电脑的桌面上，命名为 brainimage.html。
And subsequently, save the resulting file on my computer's desktop as brainimage.html.

4159
05:59:43,054 --> 05:59:47,780
我会确保它确实直接保存在桌面上，方便访问。
I will ensure it is indeed saved directly onto the desktop for easy access.

4160
05:59:48,302 --> 05:59:52,452
现在我已经把大脑图像作为 HTML 文件保存在桌面上了。
Now I've saved the brain image as an HTML file on the desktop.

4161
05:59:52,814 --> 05:59:56,516
当我点击这个 HTML 文件时，交互式图像就弹出来了。
When I clicked on the HTML file, the interactive image popped up.

4162
05:59:57,646 --> 06:00:05,828
当我点击特定的标签时，该脑部特定部位的说明就会显示在右侧的侧边栏中。
When I click on a particular label, the explanation for that specific part of the brain is displayed as a side panel here on the right hand side.

4163
06:00:06,126 --> 06:00:11,204
现在，我可以要求 Gemini 为这些点击后的说明生成配音吗？
Now, can I ask Gemini to generate a voice for this explanation when I click on the label?

4164
06:00:11,502 --> 06:00:12,100
让我们看看。
Let's see.

4165
06:00:12,494 --> 06:00:20,164
我现在要求它为上述生成的图像中、用户点击每个标签时对应的说明生成配音。
Now I am asking it to generate the voiceover for the explanation of each label when clicked by the user for the above-generated image.

4166
06:00:20,718 --> 06:00:27,876
同样，它给出了一个 HTML 代码，我需要把它保存到系统中作为 HTML 文件，看看是否有效。
So again, it gave an HTML code, which I have to save as an HTML file onto my system and see whether it works.

4167
06:00:28,398 --> 06:00:38,976
我粘贴了它，并把这个文件保存在桌面，命名为 brainimage 配音.html，看看双击后是否能生成说明的配音。
I pasted it and I'll save this file as brainimage voiceover.html on the desktop and see when I double-click it if it can generate the voiceover for the explanation.

4168
06:00:39,246 --> 06:00:40,068
我们来检查一下。
Let's check it out.

4169
06:00:40,462 --> 06:00:43,376
来看看当我点击大脑的这个部分时会发生什么。
So let's see what happens when I click on this part of the brain.

4170
06:00:43,726 --> 06:00:47,076
是否能同时给出配音和文字说明？
Will the voiceover along with the explanation be given or not?

4171
06:00:47,438 --> 06:00:51,812
它处理触觉、温度和疼痛等感官信息。
It processes sensory information like touch, temperature, and pain.

4172
06:00:52,174 --> 06:00:55,536
它在空间意识和导航中起着关键作用。
It plays a key role in spatial awareness and navigation.

4173
06:00:55,854 --> 06:00:57,444
让我看看小脑部分。
Let me check the cerebellum part.

4174
06:00:57,870 --> 06:01:05,764
小脑被称为“小脑”，负责协调姿态、平衡、协调和语言等随意运动。
Cerebellum, known as the little brain, coordinates voluntary movements such as posture, balance, coordination, and speech.

4175
06:01:06,336 --> 06:01:08,100
哇，太棒了，对吧？
Wow, that's great, right?

4176
06:01:08,576 --> 06:01:19,296
